('e98a3f1e7fcde46b831d6d130d8eb4ed3d1f304dffff8b4f8b79d9887ab2b60c', 'docs/ACCESSIBILITY.md', 'Accessibility Guidance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- The current overlay primitive is modal-first. It does not yet define a full stacked overlay manager for nested dialogs, popovers, menus, and sheets. - Composite navigation focuses the keyboard model for one collection at a time. Higher-level widget authoring patterns such as tree views, grid navigation, or full combobox behaviors still need application composition. - Live-region helpers are local to the component tree that owns them. There is no global announcement bus.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 2888, 3365, '- The current overlay primitive is modal-first. It does not yet define a full stacked overlay manager for nested dialogs, popovers, menus, and sheets. - Composite navigation focuses the keyboard model for one collection at a time. Higher-level widget authoring patterns such as tree views, grid navigation, or full combobox behaviors still need application composition. - Live-region helpers are local to the component tree that owns them. There is no global announcement bus. ', 'Paragraph - The current overlay primitive is modal-first. It does not yet define a full stacked overlay manager for nested dialogs, popovers, menus, and sheets.
- Composite navigation focuses the keyboard model for one collection at a time. Higher-level widget authoring patterns such as tree views, grid navigation, or full combobox behaviors still need application composition.
