('825ddc6f9cd6e94069b850db71a8f5a504eba7af', 'docs/AUTH_AND_SESSION_INTEGRATION.md', 'Auth And Session Integration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Background refresh rules:', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10426, 10451, 'Background refresh rules:', 'Background refresh rules:', 0.9, 'pass', '', 10426, 10451, 'Background refresh rules:', 'Background refresh rules:', 0, 0, 'manual-auth_and_session_integration-20260330T214721548Z', '4eb2ea679eca5950f4d9d438ff13c5e245ade6fc580b182d7b3ae7a01bd3a510', 'f41beba9bcf163bc6b9465dab7305c85c536c6e061e226dd5490744df2bdb8ac', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('327654db0b98004b8ce6756af53fa0e94f7b7b15', 'docs/AUTH_AND_SESSION_INTEGRATION.md', 'Auth And Session Integration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- schedule refresh from an explicit server expiry or renewal hint rather than ad hoc polling - centralize refresh in one shell-owned coordinator instead of letting multiple routes or RPC callers compete - refresh early enough to avoid an avoidable expiry edge, with a small safety window and jitter when many clients may renew at once - while refresh is in flight, treat auth as pending rather than flashing unauthorized UI immediately', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10453, 10896, '- schedule refresh from an explicit server expiry or renewal hint rather than ad hoc polling - centralize refresh in one shell-owned coordinator instead of letting multiple routes or RPC callers compete - refresh early enough to avoid an avoidable expiry edge, with a small safety window and jitter when many clients may renew at once - while refresh is in flight, treat auth as pending rather than flashing unauthorized UI immediately', '- schedule refresh from an explicit server expiry or renewal hint rather than ad hoc polling - centralize refresh in one shell-owned coordinator instead of letting multiple routes or RPC callers compete - refresh early enough to avoid an avoidable expiry edge, with a small safety window and jitter when many clients may renew at once - while refresh is in flight, treat auth as pending rather than flashing unauthorized UI immediately', 0.9, 'pass', '', 10453, 10896, '- schedule refresh from an explicit server expiry or renewal hint rather than ad hoc polling - centralize refresh in one shell-owned coordinator instead of letting multiple routes or RPC callers compete - refresh early enough to avoid an avoidable expiry edge, with a small safety window and jitter when many clients may renew at once - while refresh is in flight, treat auth as pending rather than flashing unauthorized UI immediately', '- schedule refresh from a