('e8d8e9812e87c46ff8dd81ae6ac303224b602ae2', 'docs/CACHE.md', 'Shared Cache Design', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- shared cache state by key - stale-aware reloads - imperative cache reuse from route loaders or other non-hook code through `LoadCached` - optimistic replacement and optimistic update helpers - in-flight request deduplication for the same key - hard expiry through `MaxAge` - idle disposal through `DisposeAfter` - opt-in durable restore and write-through persistence through `CacheOptions.Persist` - explicit disposal through `Dispose()` or `DisposeResource(...)` - SSR bootstrap seeding through `ui.SSRBootstrap.Data["fetchCache"]` plus `fetch.RestoreCacheBootstrap(...)` - cache inspection for devtools and diagnostics through `fetch.InspectCachedResources()`', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 1514, 2177, '- shared cache state by key - stale-aware reloads - imperative cache reuse from route loaders or other non-hook code through `LoadCached` - optimistic replacement and optimistic update helpers - in-flight request deduplication for the same key - hard expiry through `MaxAge` - idle disposal through `DisposeAfter` - opt-in durable restore and write-through persistence through `CacheOptions.Persist` - explicit disposal through `Dispose()` or `DisposeResource(...)` - SSR bootstrap seeding through `ui.SSRBootstrap.Data["fetchCache"]` plus `fetch.RestoreCacheBootstrap(...)` - cache inspection for devtools and diagnostics through `fetch.InspectCachedResources()`', '- shared cache state by key - stale-aware reloads - imperative cache reuse from route loaders or other non-hook code through `LoadCached` - optimistic replacement and optimistic update helpers - in-flight request deduplication for the same key - hard expiry through `MaxAge` - idle disposal through `DisposeAfter` - opt-in durable restore and write-through persistence through `CacheOptions.Persist` - explicit disposal through `Dispose()` or `DisposeResource(...)` - SSR bootstrap seeding through `ui.SSRBootstrap.Data["fetchCache"]` plus `fetch.RestoreCacheBootstrap(...)` - cache inspection for devtools and diagnostics through `fetch.InspectCachedResources()`', 0.9, 'pass', '', 1514, 2177, '- shared cache state by key - stale-aware reloads - imperative cache reuse from route loaders or other non-hook code through `LoadCached` - optimistic replacement and optimistic update helpers - in-flight request deduplication for the same key - hard expiry through `MaxAge` - idle disposal through `DisposeAfter` - opt-in durable restore and write-through persistence through `CacheOptions.Persist` - explicit disposal through `Dispose()` or `DisposeResource(...)` - SSR bootstrap seeding through `ui.SSRBootstrap.Data["fetchCache"]` plus `fetch.RestoreCacheBootstrap(...)` - cache inspection for devtools and diagnostics through `fetch.InspectCachedResources()`', '- shared cache state by key - stale-aware reloads - imperative cache reuse from route loaders or other non-hook code through `LoadCached` - optimistic replacement and optimistic update helpers - in-flight request deduplication for the same key - hard expiry through `MaxAge` - idle disposal through `DisposeAfter` - opt-in durable restore and write-through persistence through `CacheOptions.Persist` - explicit disposal through `Dispose()` or `DisposeResource(...)` - SSR bootstrap seeding through `ui.SSRBootstrap.Data["fetchCache"]` plus `fetch.RestoreCacheBootstrap(...)` - cache inspection for devtools and diagnostics through `fetch.InspectCachedResources()`', 0, 0, 'manual-cache-20260330T214721605Z', '1e4fdf979005e827fc0eff3d189fe6140b80823a5c21ede3b573b92bceee754c', '26599cb3a7947a42750a705ef95709e832f6b3d66f5d091a24b91b4a5cde2d99', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('d3ba7ae85342ce522154d0f599985ed6ac4c0861', 'docs/CACHE.md', 'Shared Cache Design', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- Shipped: shared cache state by normalized key, stale-aware reload, durable opt-in persistence, SSR bootstrap restore, optimistic local writes, and explicit inspection or disposal helpers. - Not shipped: automatic global eviction loops, rollback transactions for optimistic mutations, or hidden persistence of arbitrary browser objects. - Cache persistence is for reconstructible JSON-shaped client data, not for secrets or server-only policy decisions.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 2200, 2654, '- Shipped: shared cache state by normalized key, stale-aware reload, durable opt-in persistence, SSR bootstrap restore, optimistic local writes, and explicit inspection or disposal helpers. - Not shipped: automatic global eviction loops, rollback transactions for optimistic mutations, or hidden persistence of arbitrary browser objects. - Cache persistence is for reconstructible JSON-shaped client data, not for secrets or server-only policy decisions.', '- Shipped: shared cache state by normalized key, stale-aware reload, durable opt-in persistence, SSR bootstrap restore, optimistic local writes, and explicit inspection or disposal helpers. - Not shipped: automatic global eviction loops, rollback transactions for optimistic mutations, or hidden persistence of arbitrary browser objects. - Cache persistence is for reconstructible JSON-shaped client data, not for secrets or server-only policy decisions.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 2200, 2654, '- Shipped: shared cache state by normalized key, stale-aware reload, durable opt-in persistence, SSR bootstrap restore, optimistic local writes, and explicit inspection or disposal helpers. - Not shipped: automatic global eviction loops, rollback transactions for optimistic mutations, or hidden persistence of arbitrary browser objects. - Cache persistence is for reconstructible JSON-shaped client data, not for secrets or server-only policy decisions.', '- Shipped: shared cache state by normalized key, stale-aware reload, durable opt-in persistence, SSR bootstrap restore, optimistic local writes, and explicit inspection or disposal helpers. - Not shipped: automatic global eviction loops, rollback transactions for optimistic mutations, or hidden persistence of arbitrary browser objects. - Cache persistence is for reconstructible JSON-shaped client data, not for secrets or server-only policy decisions.', 0, 0, 'manual-cache-20260330T214721605Z', '1e4fdf979005e827fc0eff3d189fe6140b80823a5c21ede3b573b92bceee754c', 'e052cbac31383a2f91ec63a1c785102a65a3e21717d3c30ba0e50c404fb2bf6d', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('cb330ca1fc7580d0286d14b5df08d0c0b5e73511', 'docs/CACHE.md', 'Shared Cache Design', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Shared-cache identity should be deterministic and application-owned.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 2690, 2758, 'Shared-cache identity should be deterministic and application-owned.', 'Shared-cache identity should be deterministic and application-owned.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 2690, 2758, 'Shared-cache identity should be deterministic and application-owned.', 'Shared-cache identity should be deterministic and application-owned.', 0, 0, 'manual-cache-20260330T214721605Z', '1e4fdf979005e827fc0eff3d189fe6140b80823a5c21ede3b573b92bceee754c', '48babe07ff9c87fcde1651c634c584f0eecf7ab9441a5df527b1a3cc0a4d6fac', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('b00a6e4887c72de4b12588a2bf4edb93f4d34141', 'docs/CACHE.md', 'Shared Cache Design', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- keys must be stable strings - the key should include every input that changes the logical payload - when the payload depends on path params, query values, locale, auth scope, or user-selected filters, those inputs belong in the key - do not rely on map iteration order when constructing keys - normalize empty or default query values so semantically identical queries produce the same key - use one key for list data and a separate key for detail data unless both truly share the same payload shape - if an app already has a route-loader identity, reuse that same normalized identity instead of inventing a second cache namespace', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 2768, 3399, '- keys must be stable strings - the key should include every input that changes the logical payload - when the payload depends on path params, query values, locale, auth scope, or user-selected filters, those inputs belong in the key - do not rely on map iteration order when constructing keys - normalize empty or default query values so semantically identical queries produce the same key - use one key for list data and a separate key for detail data unless both truly share the same payload shape - if an app already has a route-loader identity, reuse that same normalized identity instead of inventing a second cache namespace', '- keys must be stable strings - the key should include every input that changes the logical payload - when the payload depends on path params, query values, locale, auth scope, or user-selected filters, those inputs belong in the key - do not rely on map iteration order when constructing keys - normalize empty or default query values so semantically identical queries produce the same key - use one key for list data and a separate key for detail data unless both truly share the same payload shape - if an app already has a route-loader identity, reuse that same normalized