('47fb2a2f0fa72dc2ab8bcc545d032448debab0cc', 'docs/CACHE.md', 'Shared Cache Design', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- strings, numbers, booleans, arrays, maps, and plain structs are safe defaults - avoid storing opaque browser handles, callbacks, or environment-specific objects in shared cached values - keep secrets and server-only authorization context out of any value that might later become bootstrap data - keep payloads intentionally small so the first HTML response does not bloat for one oversized cache entry - use one bootstrap entry per normalized cache key instead of embedding ad hoc mixed payloads - prefer values that round-trip through standard JSON without custom codecs unless the server and client both deliberately own a stronger transport', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10222, 10867, '- strings, numbers, booleans, arrays, maps, and plain structs are safe defaults - avoid storing opaque browser handles, callbacks, or environment-specific objects in shared cached values - keep secrets and server-only authorization context out of any value that might later become bootstrap data - keep payloads intentionally small so the first HTML response does not bloat for one oversized cache entry - use one bootstrap entry per normalized cache key instead of embedding ad hoc mixed payloads - prefer values that round-trip through standard JSON without custom codecs unless the server and client both deliberately own a stronger transport', '- strings, numbers, booleans, arrays, maps, and plain structs are safe defaults - avoid storing opaque browser handles, callbacks, or environment-specific objects in shared cached values - keep secrets and server-only authorization context out of any value that might later become bootstrap data - keep payloads intentionally small so the first HTML response does not bloat for one oversized cache entry - use one bootstrap entry per normalized cache key instead of embedding ad hoc mixed payloads - prefer values that round-trip through standard