('e2a09bf499566ccfcc1ab8ce36cd3f4d8c6e5f0f', 'docs/CODE_SPLITTING.md', 'Code Splitting And Bundle Loading', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Component-level splitting should be reserved for self-contained subtrees that are optional, heavy, or only needed after the shell becomes interactive.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 6278, 6428, 'Component-level splitting should be reserved for self-contained subtrees that are optional, heavy, or only needed after the shell becomes interactive.', 'Component-level splitting should be reserved for self-contained subtrees that are optional, heavy, or only needed after the shell becomes interactive.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 6278, 6428, 'Component-level splitting should be reserved for self-contained subtrees that are optional, heavy, or only needed after the shell becomes interactive.', 'Component-level splitting should be reserved for self-contained subtrees that are optional, heavy, or only needed after the shell becomes interactive.', 0, 0, 'manual-code_splitting-20260330T214721627Z', 'd5091a33e378c060491d57258ec5b59832126624ada2918791a135dc42163a50', '6154fe41c09ae849ed55b996a2782f3a6238ee1496555e39796802458d9b399b', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('ca175dffacc69e8e14264bef147c141d8a3411b7', 'docs/CODE_SPLITTING.md', 'Code Splitting And Bundle Loading', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'The intended component rules are:', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 6430, 6463, 'The intended component rules are:', 'The intended component rules are:', 0.9, 'pass', '', 6430, 6463, 'The intended component rules are:', 'The intended component rules are:', 0, 0, 'manual-code_splitting-20260330T214721627Z', 'd5091a33e378c060491d57258ec5b59832126624ada2918791a135dc42163a50', '3ad10a7d55de3c33acabc45296ee45bbf2b81200dc8615513e2f6d0300ce6a6f', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('44f1429bf0be1ce7f2d4b2005d7ae0a3d74cddaf', 'docs/CODE_SPLITTING.md', 'Code Splitting And Bundle Loading', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- use `ui.Lazy` for nested panels, dialogs, tabs, widgets, or feature islands that can mount after the main route shell - pair every lazy subtree with an obvious pending fallback so the user sees that work is happening instead of a blank gap - pair every lazy subtree with an error fallback that explains the failure and exposes a retry or recovery path - use `ui.AsyncBoundary` when the lazy subtree needs a distinct pending state, delay, or timeout treatment around the component - use `ui.ErrorBoundary` when the lazy subtree should recover locally without taking down the route shell - keep lazy component boundaries stable across rerenders so the loading surface does not move around under the user - avoid deferring components that are required for the first meaningful interaction on the current route', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 6465, 7273, '- use `ui.Lazy` for nested panels, dialogs, tabs, widgets, or feature islands that can mount after the main route shell - pair every lazy subtree with an obvious pending fallback so the user sees that work is happening instead of a blank gap - pair every lazy subtree with an error fallback that explains the failure and exposes a retry or recovery path - use `ui.AsyncBoundary` when the lazy subtree needs a distinct pending state, delay, or timeout treatment around the component - use `ui.ErrorBoundary` when the lazy subtree should recover locally without taking down the route shell - keep lazy component boundaries stable across rerenders so the loading surface does not move around under the user - avoid deferring components that are required for the first meaningful interaction on the current route', '- use `ui.Lazy` for nested panels, dialogs, tabs, widgets, or feature islands that can mount after the main route shell - pair every lazy subtree with an obvious pending fallback so the user sees tha