('df1bb6e653bbd6ff609aef3c1cfdd32b34bb3559', 'docs/CONFIGURATION.md', 'Runtime Configuration and Feature Flags', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- server-only configuration never belongs in SSR bootstrap, prerender payloads, client bundles, logs, or devtools snapshots - public runtime config may move through `ui.SSRBootstrap` or explicit client initialization when the browser needs it to resume correctly - feature flags transferred to the browser should be the evaluated public decision, not the secret targeting inputs that produced that decision - prerendered and static-exported outputs should treat config payloads as public artifacts and therefore keep them within the same browser-safe boundary as bootstrap data', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 3757, 4334, '- server-only configuration never belongs in SSR bootstrap, prerender payloads, client bundles, logs, or devtools snapshots - public runtime config may move through `ui.SSRBootstrap` or explicit client initialization when the browser needs it to resume correctly - feature flags transferred to the browser should be the evaluated public decision, not the secret targeting inputs that produced that decision - prerendered and static-exported outputs should treat config payloads as public artifacts and therefore keep them within the same browser-safe boundary as bootstrap data', '- server-only configuration never belongs in SSR bootstrap, prerender payloads, client bundles, logs, or devtools snapshots - public runtime config may move through `ui.SSRBootstrap` or explicit client initialization when the browser needs it to resume correctly - feature flags transferred to the browser should be the evaluated public decision, not the secret targeting inputs that produced that decision - prerendered and static-exported outputs should treat config payloads as public artifacts and therefore keep them within the same browser-safe boundary as bootstrap data', 0.9, 'pass', '', 3757, 4334, '- server-only configuration never belongs in S