('eb14234ef3481b7a58ce0b3a2818c54c7a5ccbb0', 'docs/CONFIGURATION.md', 'Runtime Configuration and Feature Flags', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- later layers may narrow or refine earlier public values, but they should not silently convert server-only values into client-visible ones - request-time values should be used for per-user or per-request public behavior such as experiment assignment, region label, or locale hint - local development overrides should be visibly labeled and should never be treated as production defaults - one configuration owner should be responsible for final normalization before values are injected into handlers, bootstrap payloads, or component providers', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 5283, 5827, '- later layers may narrow or refine earlier public values, but they should not silently convert server-only values into client-visible ones - request-time values should be used for per-user or per-request public behavior such as experiment assignment, region label, or locale hint - local development overrides should be visibly labeled and should never be treated as production defaults - one configuration owner should be responsible for final normalization before values are injected into handlers, bootstrap payloads, or component providers', '- later layers may narrow or refine earlier public values, but they should not silently convert server-only values into client-visible ones - request-time values should be used for per-user or per-request public behavior such as experiment assignment, region label, or locale hint - local development overrides should be visibly labeled and should never be treated as production defaults - one configuration owner should be responsible for final normalization before values are injected into handlers, bootstrap payloads, or component providers', 0.9, 'pass', '', 5283, 5827, '- later layers may narrow or refine earlier public values, but they should not silently convert server-only values into client-visible ones - req