('4895d1e79daa7256c3077866177766117c4833c1', 'docs/CROSS_TAB.md', 'Cross-Tab Synchronization', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- each channel has one clear concern and stable naming - payloads are small, JSON-shaped, and revision-aware when conflicts matter - receivers can ignore stale or already-applied messages safely - narrowing events such as logout are treated more strictly than expansive state claims - storage-fallback behavior is acceptable for the supported browser baseline', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 2764, 3123, '- each channel has one clear concern and stable naming - payloads are small, JSON-shaped, and revision-aware when conflicts matter - receivers can ignore stale or already-applied messages safely - narrowing events such as logout are treated more strictly than expansive state claims - storage-fallback behavior is acceptable for the supported browser baseline', '- each channel has one clear concern and stable naming - payloads are small, JSON-shaped, and revision-aware when conflicts matter - receivers can ignore stale or already-applied messages safely - narrowing events such as logout are treated more strictly than expansive state claims - storage-fallback behavior is acceptable for the supported browser baseline', 0.9, 'pass', '', 2764, 3123, '- each channel has one clear concern and stable naming - payloads are small, JSON-shaped, and revision-aware when conflicts matter - receivers can ignore stale or already-applied messages safely - narrowing events such as logout are treated more strictly than expansive state claims - storage-fallback behavior is acceptable for the supported browser baseline', '- each channel has one clear concern and stable naming - payloads are small, JSON-shaped, and revision-aware when conflicts matter - receivers can ignore stale or already-applied messages safely - narrowing events such as logout are treated more strictly than expansive state claims - storage-fallback behavior is acceptable for the supported browser base