('5d84f6a6d2879836e8f4be11f633d651e8c050be', 'docs/CUSTOM_ELEMENTS.md', 'Custom Elements', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- consuming third-party custom elements should assume the custom element owns its own internal style model - exported GoWebComponents prototypes should default to shadow DOM when style isolation is required - light-DOM export is still possible, but then external CSS ownership and selector collisions become the caller''s responsibility - wrapper-owned shadow roots should carry the component-local `<style>` subtree or another explicit style injection path instead of assuming global stylesheet inheritance', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 5890, 6396, '- consuming third-party custom elements should assume the custom element owns its own internal style model - exported GoWebComponents prototypes should default to shadow DOM when style isolation is required - light-DOM export is still possible, but then external CSS ownership and selector collisions become the caller''s responsibility - wrapper-owned shadow roots should carry the component-local `<style>` subtree or another explicit style injection path instead of assuming global stylesheet inheritance', '- consuming third-party custom elements should assume the custom element owns its own internal style model - exported GoWebComponents prototypes should default to shadow DOM when style isolation is required - light-DOM export is still possible, but then external CSS ownership and selector collisions become the caller''s responsibility - wrapper-owned shadow roots should carry the component-local `<style>` subtree or another explicit style injection path instead of assuming global stylesheet inheritance', 0.9, 'pass', '', 5890, 6396, '- consuming third-party custom elements should assume the custom element owns its own internal style model - exported GoWebComponents prototypes should default to shadow DOM when style isolation is required - light-DOM export is still possible, but then external CSS ownership and selector collisions become the caller''s responsibility - wrapper-owned shadow roots should carry the component-local `<style>` subtree or another explicit style injection path instead of assuming global stylesheet inheritance', '- consuming third-party custom elements should assume the custom element owns its own internal style model - exported GoWebComponents prototypes should default to shadow DOM when style isolation is required - light-DOM export is still possible, but then external CSS ownership and selector collisions become the caller''s responsibility - wrapper-owned shadow roots should carry the component-local `<style>` subtree or another explicit style injection path instead of assuming global stylesheet inheritance', 0, 0, 'manual-custom_elements-20260330T214721676Z', '1676980ee6589db3114df2ac6c9d8986b815543aecded47eb464b66e388bca41', '34d8c51e308ab4222606ef36b0266d82c8cec1159b69b1b1940c46a2ebd99af6', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('6b7b7284c76556cc85a65ab8b68eef498754675e', 'docs/CUSTOM_ELEMENTS.md', 'Custom Elements', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- choose shadow DOM when the exported widget should be embeddable in arbitrary host pages without leaking or inheriting layout styles - choose light DOM only when the embedding surface explicitly wants shared CSS and accepts the coupling - do not assume one exported component can transparently support both modes without documenting differences in slot behavior, typography inheritance, and theming hooks', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 6419, 6824, '- choose shadow DOM when the exported widget should be embeddable in arbitrary host pages without leaking or inheriting layout styles - choose light DOM only when the embedding surface explicitly wants shared CSS and accepts the coupling - do not assume one exported component can transparently support both modes without documenting differences in slot behavior, typography inheritance, and theming hooks', '- choose shadow DOM when the exported widget should be embeddable in arbitrary host pages without leaking or inheriting layout styles - choose light DOM only when the embedding surface explicitly wants shared CSS and accepts the coupling - do not assume one exported component can transparently support both modes without documenting differences in slot behavior, typography inheritance, and theming hooks', 0.9, 'pass', '', 6419, 6824, '- choose shadow DOM when the exported widget should be embeddable in arbitrary host pages without leaking or inheriting layout styles - choose light DOM only when the embedding surface explicitly wants shared CSS and accepts the coupling - do not assume one exported component can transparently support both modes without documenting differences in slot behavior, typography inheritance, and theming hooks', '- choose shadow DOM when the exported widget should be embeddable in arbitrary host pages without leaking or inheriting layout styles - choose light DOM only when the embeddin