('9f251461f1fcf1eb9a1ad20a5073fe2ddfb0e6e3', 'docs/DATA_LOADING_AND_MUTATION_ARCHITECTURE.md', 'Data Loading And Mutation Architecture', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- using atoms as a shadow async cache - putting every read into route loaders even when it is deeply local - using `UseFetch(...)` everywhere instead of typed resources - inventing inconsistent cache keys across route and component readers - optimistic updates without a revalidation or rollback path - durable offline queueing for writes that should just fail fast', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 7745, 8110, '- using atoms as a shadow async cache - putting every read into route loaders even when it is deeply local - using `UseFetch(...)` everywhere instead of typed resources - inventing inconsistent cache keys across route and component readers - optimistic updates without a revalidation or rollback path - durable offline queueing for writes that should just fail fast', '- using atoms as a shadow async cache - putting every read into route loaders even when it is deeply local - using `UseFetch(...)` everywhere instead of typed resources - inventing inconsistent cache keys across route and component readers - optimistic updates without a revalidation or rollback path - durable offline queueing for writes that should just fail fast', 0.9, 'pass', '', 7745, 8110, '- using atoms as a shadow async cache - putting every read into route loaders even when it is deeply local - using `UseFetch(...)` everywhere instead of typed resources - inventing inconsistent cache keys across route and component readers - optimistic updates without a revalidation or rollback path - durable offline queueing for writes that should just fail fast', '- using atoms as a shadow async cache - putting every read into route loaders even when it is deeply local - using `UseFetch(...)` everywhere instead of typed resources - inventing inconsistent cache keys across route and component readers - optimistic updates without a revalidation or ro