('4f643a32b22ba3a38a1ae509312e4fa813f31f1e', 'docs/HOT_RELOAD.md', 'Hot Reload', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'GoWebComponents now treats state-preserving hot reload as a first-class development feature for standalone `js/wasm` apps.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 14, 136, 'GoWebComponents now treats state-preserving hot reload as a first-class development feature for standalone `js/wasm` apps.', 'GoWebComponents now treats state-preserving hot reload as a first-class development feature for standalone `js/wasm` apps.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 14, 136, 'GoWebComponents now treats state-preserving hot reload as a first-class development feature for standalone `js/wasm` apps.', 'GoWebComponents now treats state-preserving hot reload as a first-class development feature for standalone `js/wasm` apps.', 0, 0, 'manual-hot_reload-20260330T214721812Z', '77639bd1a56c2c1a0e718e3dd8cccb376209acbe77e80b558c429b4055dd15f4', '598c632c00dd404720795ee8f337890cf704d632880158324d9284195d71530f', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('eeba1632eb70ddc6ed73a743c9e9043247bc399a', 'docs/HOT_RELOAD.md', 'Hot Reload', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- Enable hot reload from the app with `hotreload.Enable()` or `hotreload.Configure(...)`. - Run the development loop through `go run ./tools/gwc dev -app ...` unless you specifically need the lower-level shell wrappers. - Expect state preservation for shared atoms and compatible local hook state, not arbitrary in-place code patching. - Use `ResetKey` or `ui.HotReloadBoundary(...)` when an edit should intentionally remount or discard preserved state. - Treat `gwc dev` as the default supported entrypoint: it enables hot reload by default on successful rebuilds, preserves state when the app and edit are compatible, and falls back to a remount or full reload when they are not.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 154, 835, '- Enable hot reload from the app with `hotreload.Enable()` or `hotreload.Configure(...)`. - Run the development loop through `go run ./tools/gwc dev -app ...` unless you specifically need the lower-level shell wrappers. - Expect state preservation for shared atoms and compatible local hook state, not arbitrary in-place code patching. - Use `ResetKey` or `ui.HotReloadBoundary(...)` when an edit should intentionally remount or discard preserved state. - Treat `gwc dev` as the default supported entrypoint: it enables hot reload by default on successful rebuilds, preserves state when the app and edit are compatible, and falls back to a remount or full reload when they are not.', '- Enable hot reload from the app with `hotreload.Enable()` or `hotreload.Configure(...)`. - Run the development loop through `go run ./tools/gwc dev -app ...` unless you specifically need the lower-level shell wrappers. - Expect state preservation for shared atoms and compatible local hook state, not arbitrary in-place code patching. - Use `ResetKey` or `ui.HotReloadBoundary(...)` when an edit should intentionally remount or discard preserved state. - Treat `gwc dev` as the default supported entrypoint: it enables hot reload by default on successful rebuilds, preserves state when the app and edit are compatible, and falls back to a remount or full reload when they are not.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 154, 835, '- Enable hot reload from the app with `hotreload.Enable()` or `hotreload.Configure(...)`. - Run the development loop through `go run ./tools/gwc dev -app ...` unless you specifically need the lower-level shell wrappers. - Expect state preservation for shared atoms and compatible local hook state, not arbitrary in-place code patching. - Use `ResetKey` or `ui.HotReloadBoundary(...)` when an edit should intentionally remount or discard preserved state. - Treat `gwc dev` as the default supported entrypoint: it enables hot reload by default on successful rebuilds, preserves state when the app and edit are compatible, and falls back to a remount or full reload when they are not.', '- Enable hot reload from the app with `hotreload.Enable()` or `hotreload.Configure(...)`. - Run the development loop through `go run ./tools/gwc dev -app ...` unless you specifically need the lower-level shell wrappers. - Expect state preservation for shared atoms and compatible local hook state, not arbitrary in-place code patching. - Use `ResetKey` or `ui.HotReloadBoundary(...)` when an edit should intentionally remount or discard preserved state. - Treat `gwc dev` as the default supported entrypoint: it enables hot reload by default on successful rebuilds, preserves state when the app and edit are compatible, and falls back to a remount or full reload when they are not.', 0, 0, 'manual-hot_reload-20260330T214721812Z', '77639bd1a56c2c1a0e718e3dd8cccb376209acbe77e80b558c429b4055dd15f4', '485bc42d60cbbc3fc16dd1e428dc5241f510ee8e19cbf612ac4d92f3a8558f1b', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
