('476432381b4b66f6965053bd7eedeabd240adf68', 'docs/HOT_RELOAD.md', 'Hot Reload', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'The repo supports in-page WASM module replacement with a state-preserving reload bridge. It preserves shared atom state and compatible serializable component-local hook state while keeping the existing DOM in place during a hot reload, runs a pre-reload cleanup bridge for old effect resources, and falls back to a remount only when the runtime cannot safely migrate the preserved state.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 1464, 1851, 'The repo supports in-page WASM module replacement with a state-preserving reload bridge. It preserves shared atom state and compatible serializable component-local hook state while keeping the existing DOM in place during a hot reload, runs a pre-reload cleanup bridge for old effect resources, and falls back to a remount only when the runtime cannot safely migrate the preserved state.', 'The repo supports in-page WASM module replacement with a state-preserving reload bridge. It preserves shared atom state and compatible serializable component-local hook state while keeping the existing DOM in place during a hot reload, runs a pre-reload cleanup bridge for old effect resources, and falls back to a remount only when the runtime cannot safely migrate the preserved state.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 1464, 1851, 'The repo supports in-page WASM module replacement with a state-preserving reload bridge. It preserves shared atom state and compatible serializable component-local hook state while keeping the existing DOM in place during a hot reload, runs a pre-reload cleanup bridge for old effect resources, and falls back to a remount only when the runtime cannot safely migrate the preserved state.', 'The repo supports in-page WASM module replacement with a state-preserving reload bridge. It preserves shared atom state and compatible serializable component-local hook state while keeping the existing DOM in place during a hot reload, runs a pre-reload cleanup bridge for old effect resources, and falls back to a remount only when the runtime cannot safely migrate the preserved state.', 0, 0, 'manual-hot_reload-20260330T214721812Z', '77639bd1a56c2c1a0e718e3dd8cccb376209acbe77e80b558c429b4055dd15f4', '825b0d9616f3a3ea0d1a0178d9578bafa6004bc4dbeb42c91bc4217a61f3b983', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('41f77b57c152b12d89568042c612220ae5116f70', 'docs/HOT_RELOAD.md', 'Hot Reload', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '`gwc dev` is the canonical supported workflow for this behavior. The launcher forwards `-hot=true` by default, so compatible rebuilds attempt preserve-state hot reload first; incompatible rebuilds still succeed through the existing remount or full-page reload fallback path instead of asking teams to switch to a different dev command.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 1853, 2188, '`gwc dev` is the canonical supported workflow for this behavior. The launcher forwards `-hot=true` by default, so compatible rebuilds attempt preserve-state hot reload first; incompatible rebuilds still succeed through the existing remount or full-page reload fallback path instead of asking teams to switch to a different dev command.', '`gwc dev` is the canonical supported workflow for this behavior. The launcher forwards `-hot=true` by default, so compatible rebuilds attempt preserve-state hot reload first; incompatible rebuilds still succeed through the existing remount or full-page reload fallback path instead of asking teams to switch to a different dev command.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 1853, 2188, '`gwc dev` is the canonical supported workflow for this behavior. The launcher forwards `-hot=true` by default, so compatible rebuilds attempt preserve-state hot reload first; incompatible rebuilds still succeed through the existing remount or full-page reload fallback path instead of asking teams to switch to a different dev command.', '`gwc dev` is the canonical supported workflow for this behavior. The launcher forwards `-hot=true` by default, so compatible rebuilds attempt preserve-state hot reload first; incompatible rebuilds still succeed through the existing remount or full-page reload fallback path instead of asking teams to switch to a different dev command.', 0, 0, 'manual-hot_reload-20260330T214721812Z', '77639bd1a56c2c1a0e718e3dd8cccb376209acbe77e80b558c429b4055dd15f4', 'b7e3674db3a