('b9d0b28b328b388c6227547151dfe8ab110aa4b8', 'docs/HOT_RELOAD.md', 'Hot Reload', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- the runtime still rebuilds the bundle as a single WASM module rather than patching one component function body in isolation - router registrations and other global registries still need explicit restart or reset behavior - preserving correctness during development is more important than keeping every ambiguous local slot alive - the current cleanup-plus-restore bridge covers the high-value developer workflow of keeping DOM, shared state, and migratable local state across edits', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 8646, 9129, '- the runtime still rebuilds the bundle as a single WASM module rather than patching one component function body in isolation - router registrations and other global registries still need explicit restart or reset behavior - preserving correctness during development is more important than keeping every ambiguous local slot alive - the current cleanup-plus-restore bridge covers the high-value developer workflow of keeping DOM, shared state, and migratable local state across edits', '- the runtime still rebuilds the bundle as a single WASM module rather than patching one component function body in isolation - router registrations and other global registries still need explicit restart or reset behavior - preserving correctness during development is more important than keeping every ambiguous local slot alive - the current cleanup-plus-restore bridge covers the high-value developer workflow of keeping DOM, shared state, and migratable local state across edits', 0.9, 'pass', '', 8646, 9129, '- the runtime still rebuilds the bundle as a single WASM module rather than patching one component function body in isolation - router registrations and other global registries still need explicit restart or reset behavior - preserving correctness during development is more important than keeping every ambiguous local slot alive - the current cleanup-plus-re