('ffabf6fe6c7a71e1889246c9573186b7faf6fa3d', 'docs/HOT_RELOAD.md', 'Hot Reload', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'In practice that means a hot reload should prefer restarting these surfaces from clean code rather than trying to continue in-flight work that still points at old closures, goroutines, or browser callbacks.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 16570, 16776, 'In practice that means a hot reload should prefer restarting these surfaces from clean code rather than trying to continue in-flight work that still points at old closures, goroutines, or browser callbacks.', 'In practice that means a hot reload should prefer restarting these surfaces from clean code rather than trying to continue in-flight work that still points at old closures, goroutines, or browser callbacks.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 16570, 16776, 'In practice that means a hot reload should prefer restarting these surfaces from clean code rather than trying to continue in-flight work that still points at old closures, goroutines, or browser callbacks.', 'In practice that means a hot reload should prefer restarting these surfaces from clean code rather than trying to continue in-flight work that still points at old closures, goroutines, or browser callbacks.', 0, 0, 'manual-hot_reload-20260330T214721812Z', '77639bd1a56c2c1a0e718e3dd8cccb376209acbe77e80b558c429b4055dd15f4', 'c2057228db7abafb0a0115fd3beabe997bacbd9921a8ee8046020f820dec7b6c', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('7be99bc2de082e8cb622ea7f7f6efedef0f27622', 'docs/HOT_RELOAD.md', 'Hot Reload', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Why this boundary exists:', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 16778, 16803, 'Why this boundary exists:', 'Why this boundary exists:', 0.9, 'pass', '', 16778, 16803, 'Why this boundary exists:', 'Why this boundary exists:', 0, 0, 'manual-hot_reload-20260330T214721812Z', '77639bd1a56c2c1a0e718e3dd8cccb376209acbe77e80b558c429b4055dd15f4', '9d47d0f2fe7f51667c8045bf0a5b8d3deae0fdf0162ccc0853b10b71bf753cf1', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('9a6794bb0c195891df9e2c2c2efc725a33285bb7', 'docs/HOT_RELOAD.md', 'Hot Reload', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- fetch hooks can restore a serializable snapshot of visible fetch state, but the in-flight goroutine and JS promise chain still belong to the old module instance - router state is stored in mutable registries and listener wiring, so preserving it across code changes risks double-registration and stale closure capture - async guards, loaders, timers, and event subscriptions are correctness-sensitive; restarting them is safer than pretending they can transparently survive a bundle swap', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 16805, 17294, '- fetch hooks can restore a serializable snapshot of visible fetch state, but the in-flight goroutine and JS promise chain still belong to the old module instance - router state is stored in mutable registries and listener wiring, so preserving it across code changes risks double-registration and stale closure capture - async guards, loaders, timers, and event subscriptions are correctness-sensitive; restarting them is safer than pretending they can transparently survive a bundle swap', '- fetch hooks can restore a serializable snapshot of visible fetch state, but the in-flight goroutine and JS promise chain still belong to the old module instance - router state is stored in mutable registries and listener wiring, so preserving it across code changes risks double-registration and stale closure capture - async guards, loaders, timers, and event subscriptions are correctness-sensitive; restarting them is safer than pretending they can transparently survive a bundle swap', 0.9, 'pass', '', 16805, 17294, '- fetch hooks can restore a serializable snapshot of visible fetch state, but the in-flight goroutine and JS promise chain still belong to the old module instance - router state is stored in mutable registries and listener wiring, so preserving it across code changes risks double-registration and stale closure capture - async guards, loaders, timers, and event subscriptions are correctness-sensitive; restarting them is safer than pretending they can transparently survive a bundle swap', '- fetch hooks can restore a serializable snapshot of visible fetch state, but the in-flight goroutine and JS promise chain still belong to the old module instance - router state is stored in mutable registries and listener wiring, so preserving it across code changes risks double-registration and stale closure capture - async guards, loaders, timers, and event subscriptions are correctness-sensitive; restarting them is safer than pretending they can transparently survive a bundle swap', 0, 0, 'manual-hot_reload-20260330T214721812Z', '77639bd1a56c2c1a0e718e3dd8cccb376209acbe77e80b558c429b4055dd15f4', '94ca9ddeb17d8a46d1dcbd60597f6656be40014044db6884af82fc14ddd37d44', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('340b70243355852f43e8f77ef36f6d53ccca544b', 'docs/HOT_RELOAD.md', 'Hot Reload', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Operationally, the preserve-versus-restart rule is:', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 17296, 17347, 'Operationally, the preserve-versus-restart rule is:', 'Operationally, the preserve-versus-restart rule is:', 0.9, 'pass', '', 17296, 17347, 'Operationally, the preserve-versus-restart rule is:', 'Operationally, the preserve-versus-restart rule is:', 0, 0, 'manual-hot_reload-20260330T214721812Z', '77639bd1a56c2c1a0e718e3dd8cccb376209acbe77e80b558c429b4055dd15f4', 'a2ff7a2d43aa093f98cfb29eda73cc69fa7ab39deb81ebbbdb3b6ebab49e341d', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
