('81f2386488bc63eebbe2cf79b2a4858a19175cb8', 'docs/IDE_INTEGRATION.md', 'IDE And Editor Integration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- document one VS Code-focused workflow first for launcher tasks, problem matching, snippets, and workspace diagnostics - keep public package APIs, comments, examples, and generated scaffolds ordinary enough that `gopls` works without editor-specific shims - treat any future JetBrains, Neovim, Zed, or broader LSP-specific work as follow-on integrations layered on the same documented command and diagnostic contracts', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 942, 1360, '- document one VS Code-focused workflow first for launcher tasks, problem matching, snippets, and workspace diagnostics - keep public package APIs, comments, examples, and generated scaffolds ordinary enough that `gopls` works without editor-specific shims - treat any future JetBrains, Neovim, Zed, or broader LSP-specific work as follow-on integrations layered on the same documented command and diagnostic contracts', '- document one VS Code-focused workflow first for launcher tasks, problem matching, snippets, and workspace diagnostics - keep public package APIs, comments, examples, and generated scaffolds ordinary enough that `gopls` works without editor-specific shims - treat any future JetBrains, Neovim, Zed, or broader LSP-specific work as follow-on integrations layered on the same documented command and diagnostic contracts', 0.9, 'pass', '', 942, 1360, '- document one VS Code-focused workflow first for launcher tasks, problem matching, snippets, and workspace diagnostics - keep public package APIs, comments, examples, and generated scaffolds ordinary enough that `gopls` works without editor-specific shims - treat any future JetBrains, Neovim, Zed, or broader LSP-specific work as follow-on integrations layered on the same documented command and diagnostic contracts', '- document one VS Code-focused workflow first for launcher tasks, problem matching, snippets, and workspace diagnostics - keep public package APIs, comments, examples, and generated scaffolds ordinary enough that `gopls` works without editor-specific shims - treat any future JetBrains, Neovim, Zed, or broader LSP-specific work as follow-on integrations layered on the same documented command and diagnostic contracts', 0, 0, 'manual-ide_integration-20260330T214721853Z', 'ebcd8b462fc087b3831f5849bf1e668fc03f44ce0a5fb8deca11b5e1d5d2766b', 'b0f560ecb293f1197ad003cc672b4962c0c0154d368f0e955f0defe49490fc0f', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
