('6c3ac96c488e4403db44ec4d86067ae5a755a3a5', 'docs/IDE_INTEGRATION.md', 'IDE And Editor Integration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- `gwc` is the command substrate - Go files, package docs, and examples remain the source of symbol truth - VS Code is the first target for launcher-owned tasks and problem wiring - `gopls` compatibility is a non-negotiable baseline even when richer editor affordances are added later', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 1508, 1792, '- `gwc` is the command substrate - Go files, package docs, and examples remain the source of symbol truth - VS Code is the first target for launcher-owned tasks and problem wiring - `gopls` compatibility is a non-negotiable baseline even when richer editor affordances are added later', '- `gwc` is the command substrate - Go files, package docs, and examples remain the source of symbol truth - VS Code is the first target for launcher-owned tasks and problem wiring - `gopls` compatibility is a non-negotiable baseline even when richer editor affordances are added later', 0.9, 'pass', '', 1508, 1792, '- `gwc` is the command substrate - Go files, package docs, and examples remain the source of symbol truth - VS Code is the first target for launcher-owned tasks and problem wiring - `gopls` compatibility is a non-negotiable baseline even when richer editor affordances are added later', '- `gwc` is the command substrate - Go files, package docs, and examples remain the source of symbol truth - VS Code is the first target for launcher-owned tasks and problem wiring - `gopls` compatibility is a non-negotiable baseline even when richer editor affordances are added later', 0, 0, 'manual-ide_integration-20260330T214721853Z', 'ebcd8b462fc087b3831f5849bf1e668fc03f44ce0a5fb8deca11b5e1d5d2766b', 'b6895a14139b76736e15dc659b042681d620957d50c98a7a550f2cf1561aa111', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
