('447a02666adf13620d000c23982e62f712a240ba', 'docs/INTEROP.md', 'Interop Guidance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- Cancel every `Subscription` returned by `Listen(...)`, `Subscribe(...)`, `ObserveResize(...)`, `ObserveIntersection(...)`, or media-query subscriptions during cleanup. - Dispose every imported `Module` once the calling component, route, or feature no longer owns it. - Do not keep long-lived global references to `Element` handles from short-lived route content. Re-resolve them from `CurrentDocument()` when the owning UI is mounted again. - Treat event payloads and DOM measurements as snapshots. Read what you need, convert it into Go values, and avoid storing raw browser handles in shared state. - When route changes or conditional rendering can replace a node, reacquire the `Element` handle after the new subtree is committed instead of assuming the old handle still points at a live host element.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 3068, 3874, '- Cancel every `Subscription` returned by `Listen(...)`, `Subscribe(...)`, `ObserveResize(...)`, `ObserveIntersection(...)`, or media-query subscriptions during cleanup. - Dispose every imported `Module` once the calling component, route, or feature no longer owns it. - Do not keep long-lived global references to `Element` handles from short-lived route content. Re-resolve them from `CurrentDocument()` when the owning UI is mounted again. - Treat event payloads and DOM measurements as snapshots. Read what you need, convert it into Go values, and avoid storing raw browser handles in shared state. - When route changes or conditional rendering can replace a node, reacquire the `Element` handle after the new subtree is committed instead of assuming the old handle still points at a live host element.', '- Cancel every `Subscription` returned by `Listen(...)`, `Subscribe(...)`, `ObserveResize(...)`, `ObserveIntersection(...)`, or media-query subscriptions during cleanup. - Dispose every imported `Module` once the calling component, route, or feature no longer owns it. - Do not keep long-lived global references to `Element` handles from short-lived route content. Re-resolve them from `CurrentDocument()` when the owning UI is mounted again. - Treat event payloads and DOM measurements as snapshots. Read what you need, convert it into Go values, and avoid storing raw browser handles in shared state. - When route changes or conditional rendering can replace a node, reacquire the `Element` handle after the new subtree is committed instead of assuming the old handle still points at a live host element.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 3068, 3874, '- Cancel every `Subscription` returned by `Listen(...)`, `Subscribe(...)`, `ObserveResize(...)`, `ObserveIntersection(...)`, or media-query subscriptions during cleanup. - Dispose every imported `Module` once the calling component, route, or feature no longer owns it. - Do not keep long-lived global references to `Element` handles from short-lived route content. Re-resolve them from `CurrentDocument()` when the owning UI is mounted again. - Treat event payloads and DOM measurements as snapshots. Read what you need, convert it into Go values, and avoid storing raw browser handles in shared state. - When route changes or conditional rendering can replace a node, reacquire the `Element` handle after the new subtree is committed instead of assuming the old handle still points at a live host element.', '- Cancel every `Subscription` returned by `Listen(...)`, `Subscribe(...)`, `ObserveResize(...)`, `ObserveIntersection(...)`, or media-query subscriptions during cleanup. - Dispose every imported `Module` once the calling component, route, or feature no longer owns it. - Do not keep long-lived global references to `Element` handles from short-lived route content. Re-resolve them from `CurrentDocument()` when the owning UI is mounted again. - Treat event payloads and DOM measurements as snapshots. Read what you need, convert it into Go values, and avoid storing raw browser 