('d86eba7b3ffd2040aa28a9bd8711573b60a0ea4c', 'docs/LOGGING.md', 'Logging', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- choose `logging.New(scope)` when one feature, route, or example needs a reusable scoped logger - choose package-level `logging.Log(...)` when you already have a level and scope and do not need a retained logger value - choose `AttachBrowserConsole(...)` in browser entrypoints when you want document, navigation, form, resize, rejection, and mount events logged through the same package - choose diagnostics or observability hooks alongside logs when the problem is framework degradation, mismatch analysis, or correlation across larger workflows rather than just event sequencing', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 911, 1493, '- choose `logging.New(scope)` when one feature, route, or example needs a reusable scoped logger - choose package-level `logging.Log(...)` when you already have a level and scope and do not need a retained logger value - choose `AttachBrowserConsole(...)` in browser entrypoints when you want document, navigation, form, resize, rejection, and mount events logged through the same package - choose diagnostics or observability hooks alongside logs when the problem is framework degradation, mismatch analysis, or correlation across larger workflows rather than just event sequencing', '- choose `logging.New(scope)` when one feature, route, or example needs a reusable scoped logger - choose package-level `logging.Log(...)` when you already have a level and scope and do not need a retained logger value - choose `AttachBrowserConsole(...)` in browser entrypoints when you want document, navigation, form, resize, rejection, and mount events logged through the same package - choose diagnostics or observability hooks alongside logs when the problem is framework degradation, mismatch analysis, or correlation across larger workflows rather than just event sequencing', 0.9, 'pass', '', 911, 1493, '- choose `logging.New(scope)` when one feature, route, or example needs