('25dbeccfee7fb4767fd58abfcf6d9f97d12ad2ac', 'docs/MULTI_SURFACE.md', 'Multi-Surface Coordination', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- the opener is authoritative for popup lifecycle - the popup is a specialized view or control surface, not the canonical owner of shared domain state - shared state changes should still flow back to one authoritative store, loader, cache key, or server write path', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 6204, 6468, '- the opener is authoritative for popup lifecycle - the popup is a specialized view or control surface, not the canonical owner of shared domain state - shared state changes should still flow back to one authoritative store, loader, cache key, or server write path', '- the opener is authoritative for popup lifecycle - the popup is a specialized view or control surface, not the canonical owner of shared domain state - shared state changes should still flow back to one authoritative store, loader, cache key, or server write path', 0.9, 'pass', '', 6204, 6468, '- the opener is authoritative for popup lifecycle - the popup is a specialized view or control surface, not the canonical owner of shared domain state - shared state changes should still flow back to one authoritative store, loader, cache key, or server write path', '- the opener is authoritative for popup lifecycle - the popup is a specialized view or control surface, not the canonical owner of shared domain state - shared state changes should still flow back to one authoritative store, loader, cache key, or server write path', 0, 0, 'manual-multi_surface-20260330T214721896Z', '95c999b0f3f975d8728c5aa90bf4dec0741b574b22f95c63a0d3f604cdedab71', 'd10d41791f46b1e3a2c487f0659488fdc6b1f94d2c4e212987c0cd4daa1a7b53', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('b0072039b3ec27cb9d788b9d5f01a8791e000dfe', 'docs/MULTI_SURFACE.md', 'Multi-Surface Coordination', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- let the opener own close or focus control for the popup - let the popup send intents, selections, and diagnostics rather than silently mutating canonical state in isolation - use cross-tab channels for peer tab invalidation, and window channels for targeted parent/child interaction - if both surfaces can edit the same logical entity, carry explicit revision metadata and reject stale writes instead of blindly applying the latest arriving message - prefer invalidation or intent messages when ownership is ambiguous', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 6490, 7009, '- let the opener own close or focus control for the popup - let the popup send intents, selections, and diagnostics rather than silently mutating canonical state in isolation - use cross-tab channels for peer tab invalidation, and window channels for targeted parent/child interaction - if both surfaces can edit the same logical entity, carry explicit revision metadata and reject stale writes instead of blindly applying the latest arriving message - prefer invalidation or intent messages when ownership is ambiguous', '- let the opener own close or focus control for the popup - let the popup send intents, selections, and diagnostics rather than silently mutating canonical state in isolation - use cross-tab channels for peer tab invalidation, and window channels for targeted parent/child interaction - if both surfaces can edit the same logical entity, carry explicit revision metadata and reject stale writes instead of blindly applying the latest arriving message - prefer invalidation or intent messages when ownership is ambiguous', 0.9, 'pass', '', 6490, 7009, '- let the opener own close or focus control for the popup - let the popup send intents, selections, and diagnostics rather than silently mutating canonical state in isolation - use cross-tab channels for peer tab invalidation, and window channels for targeted parent/child interaction - if both surfaces can edit the same logical entity, carry explicit revision metadata and reject stale writes instead of blindly applying the latest arriving message - prefer invalidation or intent messages when ownership is ambiguous', '- let the opener own close or focus control for the popup - let the popup send intents, selections, and diagnostics rather than silently mutating canonical state in isolation - use cross-tab channels for peer tab invalidation, and window channels for targeted parent/child interaction - if both surfaces can edit the same logical entity, carry explicit revision metadata and reject stale writes instead of blindly applying the latest arriving message - prefer invalidation or intent messages when ownership is ambiguous', 0, 0, 'manual-multi_surface-20260330T214721896Z', '95c999b0f3f975d8728c5aa90bf4dec0741b574b22f95c63a0d3f604cdedab71', 'fedf25d7e20a4cd790d9ab2a5801fa0790dc0056ce282da9d8e412b574f88ec6', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('f87edf79b492359e085e6061ca71b47a1347800d', 'docs/MULTI_SURFACE.md', 'Multi-Surface Coordination', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'This is the current answer to multi-surface synchronization rules: one surface should remain authoritative, and the others should act as mirrored or specialized collaborators.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 7011, 7186, 'This is the current answer to multi-surface synchronization rules: one surface should remain authoritative, and the others should act as mirrored or specialized collaborators.', 'This is the current answer to multi-surface synchronization rules: one surface should remain authoritative, and the others should act as mirrored or specialized collaborators.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 7011, 7186, 'This is the current answer to multi-surface synchronization rules: one surface should remain authoritative, and the others should act as mirrored or specialized collaborators.', 'This is the current answer to multi-surface synchronization rules: one surface should remain authoritative, and the others should act as mirrored or specialized collaborators.', 0, 0, 'manual-multi_surface-20260330T214721896Z', '95c999b0f3f975d8728c5aa90bf4dec0741b574b22f95c63a0d3f604cdedab71', '06a0d4517c16d7785dffde22deb794b14abc597ac2ea4b53ed34aa10a92c8099', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('6da7bd9197b6054dde19eb4e6df4d4d70c9be4fc', 'docs/MULTI_SURFACE.md', 'Multi-Surface Coordination', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Popup loss and opener loss are normal operational states.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 7223, 7280, 'Popup loss and opener loss are normal operational states.', 'Popup loss and opener loss are normal operational states.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 7223, 7280, 'Popup loss and opener loss are normal operational states.', 'Popup loss and opener loss are normal operational states.', 0, 0, 'manual-multi_surface-20260330T214721896Z', '95c999b0f3f975d8728c5aa90bf4dec0741b574b22f95c63a0d3f604cdedab71', 'f8e5c7aaf7d9740862fcf6e6ccd2ea958c1af2ee7544b06d7b37d7b1839e0a55', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('74e4d26313325682046b93c2b443eb208d583272', 'docs/MULTI_SURFACE.md', 'Multi-Surface Coordination', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'The current guidance is:', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 7282, 7306, 'The current guidance is:', 'The current guidance is:', 0.9, 'pass', '', 7282, 7306, 'The current guidance is:', 'The current guidance is:', 0, 0, 'manual-multi_surface-20260330T214721896Z', '95c999b0f3f975d8728c5aa90bf4dec0741b574b22f95c63a0d3f604cdedab71', '5f4cb30c6c22cbb16f866c8cacbaa848fdb7d947c488339fd46190fa4adc7f1c', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('f404302d387dab69feac68f0b701a2ef54e28f47', 'docs/MULTI_SURFACE.md', 'Multi-Surface Coordination', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- if a popup closes unexpectedly, the opener should detect `WindowChannel.Closed()` and treat the popup as disconnected rather than as a fatal app error - if the opener disappears, the popup becomes orphaned and should switch into a degraded but explicit state instead of assuming the coordinator still exists - orphaned surfaces should stop assuming remote writes or focus actions will succeed - reconnect by opening a new popup or re-establishing the opener relationship, not by pretending the old channel is still valid - if a surface owns only auxiliary UI, it is reasonable to close it when the authoritative opener goes away; if it still has operator value, keep it visible but clearly marked orphaned', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 7308, 8015, '- if a popup closes unexpectedly, the opener should detect `WindowChannel.Closed()` and treat the popup as disconnected rather than as a fatal app error - if the opener disappears, the popup becomes orphaned and should switch into a degraded but explicit state instead of assuming the coordinator still exists - orphaned surfaces should stop assuming remote writes or focus actions will succeed - reconnect by opening a new popup or re-establishing the opener relationship, not by pretending the old channel is still valid - if a surface owns only auxiliary UI, it is reasonable to close it when the authoritative opener goes away; if it still has operator value, keep it visible but clearly marked orphaned', '- if a popup closes unexpectedly, the opener should detect `WindowChannel.Closed()` and treat the popup as disconnected rather than as a fatal app error - if the opener disappears, the popup becomes orphaned and should switch into a degraded but explicit state instead of assuming the coordinator still exists - orphaned surfaces should stop assuming remote writes or focus actions will succeed - reconnect by opening a new popup or re-establishing the opener relationship, not by pretending the old channel is still valid - if a surface owns only auxiliary UI, it is reasonable to close it when the authoritative opener goes away; if it still has operator value, keep it visible but clearly marked orphaned', 0.9, 'pass', '', 7308, 8015, '- if a popup closes unexpectedly, the opener should detect `WindowChannel.Closed()` and treat the popup as disconnected rather than as a fatal app error - if the opener disappears, the popup becomes orphaned and should switch into a degraded but explicit state instead of assuming the coordinator still exists - orphaned surfaces should stop assuming remote writes or focus actions will succeed - reconnect by opening a new popup or re-establishing the opener relationship, not by pretending the old channel is still valid - if a surface owns only auxiliary UI, it is reasonable to close it when the authoritative opener goes away; if it still has operator value, keep it visible but clearly marked orphaned', '- if a popup closes unexpectedly, the opener should detect `WindowChannel.Closed()` and treat the popup as disconnected rather than as a fatal app error - if the opener disappears, the popup becomes orphaned and should switch into a degraded but explicit state instead of assuming the coordinator still exists - orphaned surfaces should stop assuming remote writes or focus actions will succeed - reconnect by opening a new popup or re-establishing the opener relationship, not by pretending the old channel is still valid - if a surface owns only auxiliary UI, it is reasonable to close it when the authoritative opener goes away; if it still has operator value, keep it visible but clearly marked orphaned', 0, 0, 'manual-multi_surface-20260330T214721896Z', '95c999b0f3f975d8728c5aa90bf4dec0741b574b22f95c63a0d3f604cdedab71', '507e24301b3f8257af9d314ef5295c9e821d43dd2f44005f5cc1e6f8279b2e41', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('8e98f5fd294e3493144d06cd8b9f0f8705cc8ce4', 'docs/MULTI_SURFACE.md', 'Multi-Surface Coordination', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'The runtime does not auto-remount, auto-close, or auto-transfer ownership between windows. Applications are expected to poll `Closed()` or handle publish failures and then update their own UI state intentionally.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 8017, 8229, 'The runtime does not auto-remount, auto-close, or auto-transfer ownership between windows. Applications are expected to poll `Closed()` or handle publish failures and then update their own UI state intentionally.', 'The runtime does not auto-remount, auto-close, or auto-transfer ownership between windows. Applications are expected to poll `Closed()` or handle publish failures and then update their own UI state intentionally.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 8017, 8229, 'The runtime does not auto-remount, auto-close, or auto-transfer ownership between windows. Applications are expected to poll `Closed()` or handle publish failures and then update their own UI state intentionally.', 'The runtime does not auto-remount, auto-close, or auto-transfer ownership between windows. Applications are expected to poll `Closed()` or handle publish failures and then update their own UI state intentionally.', 0, 0, 'manual-multi_surface-20260330T214721896Z', '95c999b0f3f975d8728c5aa90bf4dec0741b574b22f95c63a0d3f604cdedab71', 'aefdadc2c9724f52fa8865c30851ae931d9bc7d0b8f63fc90579ea8a384b01d1', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('55239f4dbb36c164be38c3449c47edc532427797', 'docs/MULTI_SURFACE.md', 'Multi-Surface Coordination', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- keep popup coordination same-origin unless there is a deliberate reason not to - use one named window channel per workflow such as `inspector`, `preview`, or `operator-console` - keep payloads JSON-shaped and typed through `SubscribeDecodedWindow[T](...)` - prefer `SubscribeSurfaceSignals(...)` and the dedicated publish helpers when the payload is one of the common shared session, route, selection, or intent workflows - close popup channels deliberately when the owning surface no longer needs them - treat orphaned or closed child windows as normal operational state, not as exceptional control flow', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 8259, 8865, '- keep popup coordination same-origin unless there is a deliberate reason not to - use one named window channel per workflow such as `inspector`, `preview`, or `operator-console` - keep payloads JSON-shaped and typed through `SubscribeDecodedWindow[T](...)` - prefer `SubscribeSurfaceSignals(...)` and the dedicated publish helpers when the payload is one of the common shared session, route, selection, or intent workflows - close popup channels deliberately when the owning surface no longer needs them - treat orphaned or closed child windows as normal operational state, not as exceptional control flow', '- keep popup coordination same-origin unless there is a deliberate reason not to - use one named window channel per workflow such as `inspector`, `preview`, or `operator-console` - keep payloads JSON-shaped and typed through `SubscribeDecodedWindow[T](...)` - prefer `SubscribeSurfaceSignals(...)` and the dedicated publish helpers when the payload is one of the common shared session, route, selection, or intent workflows - close popup channels deliberately when the owning surface no longer needs them - treat orphaned or closed child windows as normal operational state, not as exceptional control flow', 0.