('f159d6550333aa08d7a0ee442ad1c07038886ab0', 'docs/OFFLINE_MUTATIONS.md', 'Offline Mutation Queueing', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Use it when a browser app needs to queue writes locally, survive reloads, and replay those writes later without hand-rolling storage, deduplication, and retry timing.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 124, 290, 'Use it when a browser app needs to queue writes locally, survive reloads, and replay those writes later without hand-rolling storage, deduplication, and retry timing.', 'Use it when a browser app needs to queue writes locally, survive reloads, and replay those writes later without hand-rolling storage, deduplication, and retry timing.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 124, 290, 'Use it when a browser app needs to queue writes locally, survive reloads, and replay those writes later without hand-rolling storage, deduplication, and retry timing.', 'Use it when a browser app needs to queue writes locally, survive reloads, and replay those writes later without hand-rolling storage, deduplication, and retry timing.', 0, 0, 'manual-offline_mutations-20260330T214721999Z', 'c7817aff6f4da72f02f54dab66395ab84aa7648e7a06480eafc7c9acb32b20bf', '8c225678e2cda824a6a421a56977c69489984a1e8f1009a3fbff22b2d1b6b0dd', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('98a848fd51d8381507807475c6ef51ffeace10c0', 'docs/OFFLINE_MUTATIONS.md', 'Offline Mutation Queueing', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- the queue surface is already shipped and durable today - queue persistence is IndexedDB-first with `localStorage` fallback - replay remains application-owned so auth headers, merge policy, and real HTTP execution stay under app control - queue state is visible through replay reports, structured framework logs, and PWA diagnostics snapshots', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 308, 651, '- the queue surface is already shipped and durable today - queue persistence is IndexedDB-first with `localStorage` fallback - replay remains application-owned so auth headers, merge policy, and real HTTP execution stay under app control - queue state is visible through replay reports, structured framework logs, and PWA diagnostics snapshots', '- the queue surface is already shipped and durable today - queue persistence is IndexedDB-first with `localStorage` fallback - replay remains application-owned so auth headers, merge policy, and real HTTP execution stay under app control - queue state is visible through replay reports, structured framework logs, and PWA diagnostics snapshots', 0.9, 'pass', '', 308, 651, '- the queue surface is already shipped and durable today - queue persistence is IndexedDB-first with `localStorage` fallback - replay remains application-owned so auth headers, merge policy, and real HTTP execution stay under app control - queue state is visible through replay reports, structured framework logs, and PWA diagnostics snapshots', '- the queue surface is already shipped and durable today - queue persistence is IndexedDB-first with `localStorage` fallback - replay remains application-owned so auth headers, merge policy, and real HTTP execution stay under app control - queue state is visible through replay reports, structured framework logs, and PWA diagnostics snapshots', 0, 0, 'manual-offline_mutations-20260330T214721999Z', 'c7817aff6f4da72f02f54dab66395ab84aa7648e7a06480eafc7c9acb32b20bf', '6f151268344dce0f0bcb2631c912a8e29daddcb33246e5d1dab6650ef1c5e21d', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('e299adf8abbd56ab0a84300e2e5f8bd0dab5cf1d', 'docs/OFFLINE_MUTATIONS.md', 'Offline Mutation Queueing', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- use `fetch.OpenMutationQueue(...)` when browser-originated writes must survive reloads or offline periods - use `queue.Replay(...)` when normal retry and dead-letter behavior is enough - use `queue.ReplayWithOptions(...)` when version or conflict handling needs an explicit `ConflictHandler` - use `fetch.NewMutationConflict(...)` and `fetch.GetMutationConflict(...)` when the executor must signal or inspect authoritative version conflicts - use `pwa.MutationQueueDiagnosticsSource(...)` plus `pwa.InspectDiagnostics(...)` when the queue should participate in a broader offline diagnostics view', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 675, 1272, '- use `fetch.OpenMutationQueue(...)` when browser-originated writes must survive reloads or offline periods - use `queue.Replay(...)` when normal retry and dead-letter behavior is enough - use `queue.ReplayWithOptions(...)` when version or conflict handling needs an explicit `ConflictHandler` - use `fetch.NewMutationConflict(...)` and `fetch.GetMutationConflict(...)` when the executor must signal or inspect authoritative version conflicts - use `pwa.MutationQueueDiagnosticsSource(...)` plus `pwa.InspectDiagnostics(...)` when the queue should participate in a broader offline diagnostics view', '- use `fetch.OpenMutationQueue(...)` when browser-originated writes must survive reloads or offline periods - use `queue.Replay(...)` when normal retry and dead-letter behavior is enough - use `queue.ReplayWithOptions(...)` when version or conflict handling needs an explicit `ConflictHandler` - use `fetch.NewMutationConflict(...)` and `fetch.GetMutationConflict(...)` when the executor must signal or inspect authoritative version conflicts - use `pwa.MutationQueueDiagnosticsSource(...)` plus `pwa.InspectDiagnostics(...)` when the queue should participate in a broader offline diagnostics view', 0.9, 'pass', '', 675, 1272,