('11d8c52205410fc7c837553e6ae58f9b6293f71d', 'docs/OFFLINE_MUTATIONS.md', 'Offline Mutation Queueing', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '1. apply optimistic UI locally through atom state or `fetch.UseCachedResource[T]` with `Set`, `Update`, or `Invalidate` 2. enqueue the authoritative write payload in the mutation queue 3. when replay eventually succeeds, invalidate or reload the affected cache keys 4. when replay reaches `dead`, either roll back the optimistic UI or surface a conflict and recovery action to the user', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10498, 10883, '1. apply optimistic UI locally through atom state or `fetch.UseCachedResource[T]` with `Set`, `Update`, or `Invalidate` 2. enqueue the authoritative write payload in the mutation queue 3. when replay eventually succeeds, invalidate or reload the affected cache keys 4. when replay reaches `dead`, either roll back the optimistic UI or surface a conflict and recovery action to the user', '1. apply optimistic UI locally through atom state or `fetch.UseCachedResource[T]` with `Set`, `Update`, or `Invalidate` 2. enqueue the authoritative write payload in the mutation queue 3. when replay eventually succeeds, invalidate or reload the affected cache keys 4. when replay reaches `dead`, either roll back the optimistic UI or surface a conflict and recovery action to the user', 0.9, 'pass', '', 10498, 10883, '1. apply optimistic UI locally through atom state or `fetch.UseCachedResource[T]` with `Set`, `Update`, or `Invalidate` 2. enqueue the authoritative write payload in the mutation queue 3. when replay eventually succeeds, invalidate or reload the affected cache keys 4. when replay reaches `dead`, either roll back the optimistic UI or surface a conflict and recovery action to the user', '1. apply optimistic UI locally through atom state or `fetch.UseCachedResource[T]` with `Set`, `Update`, or `Invalidate` 2. enqueue the authoritative write payload in the mutation queue 3. when replay eventually succeeds, invalidate or reload the affected cache keys 4. when replay reaches `dead`, either roll back the optimistic UI or surface a conflict and recovery action to the user', 0, 0, 'manual-offline_mutations-20260330T214721999Z', 'c7817aff6f4da72f02f54dab66395ab84aa7648e7a06480eafc7c9acb32b20bf', '7ece815b272731a812a305d2d199d501066c6391717d261eabfa54ad3bb24c98', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('8dc200d10669eb08c3e2a1bce7345d2893c90da7', 'docs/OFFLINE_MUTATIONS.md', 'Offline Mutation Queueing', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- optimistic UI is application-owned - rollback is application-owned - conflict resolution is application-owned - the queue is responsible for durable storage, ordering, retry timing, and visibility into terminal failure state', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10904, 11130, '- optimistic UI is application-owned - rollback is application-owned - conflict resolution is application-owned - the queue is responsible for durable storage, ordering, retry timing, and visibility into terminal failure state', '- optimistic UI is application-owned - rollback is application-owned - conflict resolution is application-owned - the queue is responsible for durable storage, ordering, retry timing, and visibility into terminal failure state', 0.9, 'pass', '', 10904, 11130, '- optimistic UI is application-owned - rollback is application-owned - conflict resolution is application-owned - the queue is responsible for durable storage, ordering, retry timing, and visibility into terminal failure state', '- optimistic UI is application-owned - rollback is application-owned - conflict resolution is application-owned - the queue is responsible for durable storage, ordering, retry timing, and visibility into terminal failure state', 0, 0, 'manual-offline_mutations-20260330T214721999Z', 'c7817aff6f4da72f02f54dab66395ab84aa7648e7a06480eafc7c9acb32b20bf', '15b3bcba77fc12dce6d6422a70f935141fcb23aab6643cd3799c9c345675e5a6', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('aa7aa5a2baf9f1e913c7ab2f1b08220e4d24b6d6', 'docs/OFFLINE_MUTATIONS.md', 'Offline Mutation Queueing', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Queued payloads should stay intentionally simple and safe to persist.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 11174, 11243, 'Queued payloads should stay intentionally simple and safe to persist.', 'Queued payloads should stay intentionally simple and safe to persist.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 11174, 11243, 'Queued payloads should stay intentionally simple and safe to persist.', 'Queued payloads should stay intentionally simple and safe to persist.', 0, 0, 'manual-offline_mutations-20260330T214721999Z', 'c7817aff6f4da72f02f54dab66395ab84aa7648e7a06480eafc7c9acb32b20bf', '2dc238472a511de88241b6fe1c8d0980086ff58124b2ed650ed4437650b5ad68', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('fa8f5b0560ad6d5393423ef5208d58240d792987', 'docs/OFFLINE_MUTATIONS.md', 'Offline Mutation Queueing', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- use JSON-shaped request bodies and metadata - use `Headers` only for replay-relevant headers that are safe to persist - do not store bearer tokens, session secrets, CSRF secrets, or other sensitive credentials in the queue - prefer deriving volatile auth headers at replay time inside the executor instead of persisting them - do not store `js.Value`, `File`, `Blob`, streams, functions, or other browser-native handles in `Body` - include an application schema or migration hint in `Metadata` when queued payloads may span app upgrades - keep queue entries small because browser storage is limited and cleartext at rest unless the application adds its own encryption layer - clear queues on logout, user switch, or trust-boundary changes unless the queued drafts are explicitly designed to survive that account transition - if queued writes may contain regulated or highly sensitive business data, define an application-owned retention window and purge path instead of letting dead letters survive forever by accident', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 11265, 12285, '- use JSON-shaped request bodies and metadata - use `Headers` only for replay-relevant headers that are safe to persist - do not store bearer tokens, session secrets, CSRF secrets, or other sensitive credentials in the queue - prefer deriving volatile auth headers at replay time inside the executor instead of persisting them - do not store `js.Value`, `File`, `Blob`, streams, functions, or other browser-native handles in `Body` - include an application schema or migration hint in `Metadata` when queued payloads may span app upgrades - keep queue entries small because browser storage is limited and cleartext at rest unless the application adds its own encryption layer - clear queues on logout, user switch, or trust-boundary changes unless the queued drafts are explicitly designed to survive that account transition - if queued writes may contain regulated or highly sensitive business data, define an application-owned retention window and purge path instead of letting dead letters survive', '- use JSON-shaped request bodies and metadata - use `Headers` only for replay-relevant headers that are safe to persist - do not store bearer tokens, session secrets, CSRF secrets, or other sensitive credentials in the queue - prefer deriving volatile auth headers at replay time inside the executor instead of persisting them - do not store `js.Value`, `File`, `Blob`, streams, functions, or other browser-native handles in `Body` - include an application schema or migration hint in `Metadata` when queued payloads may span app upgrades - keep queue entries small because browser storage is limited and cleartext at rest unless the application adds its own encryption layer - clear queues on logout, user switch, or trust-boundary changes unless the queued drafts are explicitly designed to survive that account transition - if queued writes may contain regulated or highly sensitive business data, define an application-owned retention window and purge path instead of letting dead letters survive forever by accident', 0.9, 'pass', '', 11265, 12285, '- use JSON-shaped request bodies and metadata - use `Headers` only for replay-relevant headers that are safe to persist - do not store bearer tokens, session secrets, CSRF secrets, or other sensitive credentials in the queue - prefer deriving volatile auth headers at replay time inside the executor instead of persisting them - do not store `js.Value`, `File`, `Blob`, streams, functions, or other browser-native handles in `Body` - include an application schema or migration hint in `Metadata` when queued payloads may span app upgrades - keep queue entries small because browser storage is limited and cleartext at rest unless the application adds its own encryption layer - clear queues on logout, user switch, or trust-boundary changes unless the queued drafts are explicitly designed to survive that account transition - if queued writes may contain regulated or highly sensitive business data, define an application-owned retention window and purge path instead of letting dead letters survive', '- use JSON-shaped request bodies and metadata - use `Headers` only for replay-relevant headers that are safe to persist - do not store bearer tokens, session secrets, CSRF secrets, or other sensitive credentials in the queue - prefer deriving volatile auth headers at replay time inside the executor instead of persisting them - do not store `js.Value`, `File`, `Blob`, streams, functions, or other browser-native handles in `Body` - include an application schema or migration hint in `Metadata` when queued payloads may span app upgrades - keep queue entries small because browser storage is limited and cleartext at rest unless the application adds its own encryption layer - clear queues on logout, user switch, or trust-boundary changes unless the queued drafts are explicitly designed to survive that account transition - if queued writes may contain regulated or highly sensitive business data, define an application-owned retention window and purge path instead of letting dead letters survive forever by accident', 0, 0, 'manual-offline_mutations-20260330T214721999Z', 'c7817aff6f4da72f02f54dab66395ab84aa7648e7a06480eafc7c9acb32b20bf', 'b4bf2681ff02ec134e78ee9de6ba2e19a7e8c4261f630b44b3774c848987228c', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('6d9f8f2802867d57f66e3ecd5c7d57a05ce057e2', 'docs/OFFLINE_MUTATIONS.md', 'Offline Mutation Queueing', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'The queue currently serializes through standard JSON. If a payload cannot round-trip cleanly through JSON, it is outside the supported first-class boundary.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 12287, 12443, 'The queue currently serializes through standard JSON. If a payload cannot round-trip cleanly through JSON, it is outside the supported first-class boundary.', 'The queue currently serializes through standard JSON. If a payload cannot round-trip cleanly through JSON, it is outside the supported first-class boundary.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 12287, 12443, 'The queue currently serializes through standard JSON. If a payload cannot round-trip cleanly through JSON, it is outside the supported first-class boundary.', 'The queue currently serializes through standard JSON. If a payload cannot round-trip cleanly through JSON, it is outside the supported first-class boundary.', 0, 0, 'manual-offline_mutations-20260330T214721999Z', 'c7817aff6f4da72f02f54dab66395ab84aa7648e7a06480eafc7c9acb32b20bf', '91f48daad518fc92a5a474151050a948d9be89e628467cd1127bf6dfbadffb31', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('1847c60cd126cdcfe716379c7d1ac48ece6ab126', 'docs/OFFLINE_MUTATIONS.md', 'Offline Mutation Queueing', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- use one queue per logical workflow or trust boundary instead of one giant mixed queue - choose explicit `StorageKey` values so different apps or environments do not collide - use `DedupKey` for draft-save or submit-once semantics - keep replay executors authoritative and idempotent where possible - invalidate related shared-cache keys after successful replay - surface `dead` entries in the UI so users can retry, edit, or discard them intentionally', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 12473, 12926, '- use one queue per logical workflow or trust boundary instead of one giant mixed queue - choose explicit `StorageKey` values so different apps or environments do not collide - use `DedupKey` for draft-save or submit-once semantics - keep replay executors authoritative and idempotent where possible - invalidate related shared-cache keys after successful replay - surface `dead` entries in the UI so users can retry, edit, or discard them intentionally', '- use one queue per logical workflow or trust boundary instead of one giant mixed queue - choose explicit `StorageKey` values so different apps or environments do not collide - use `DedupKey` for draft-save or submit-once semantics - keep replay executors authoritative and idempotent where possible - invalidate related shared-cache keys after successful replay - surface `dead` entries in the UI so users can retry, edit, or discard them intentionally', 0.9, 'pass', '', 12473, 12926, '- use one queue per logical workflow or trust boundary instead of one giant mixed queue - choose explicit `StorageKey` values so different apps or environments do not collide - use `DedupKey` for draft-save or submit-once semantics - keep replay executors authoritative and idempotent where possible - invalidate related shared-cache keys after successful replay - surface `dead` entries in the UI so users can retry, edit, 