('86dafe4d741db121d97b6d636e1d9686467bd816', 'docs/ONBOARDING.md', 'Onboarding and Bootstrap', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- normal project workflows should go through `gwc` - when you intentionally run raw wasm commands, Windows users should use PowerShell environment assignment and macOS/Linux users may use shell environment prefixes such as `GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm` - `wasm_exec.js` must come from the same Go toolchain version that produced the wasm binary - browser-only code must still be kept behind browser execution paths because native `go test` does not provide `syscall/js`', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 3311, 3772, '- normal project workflows should go through `gwc` - when you intentionally run raw wasm commands, Windows users should use PowerShell environment assignment and macOS/Linux users may use shell environment prefixes such as `GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm` - `wasm_exec.js` must come from the same Go toolchain version that produced the wasm binary - browser-only code must still be kept behind browser execution paths because native `go test` does not provide `syscall/js`', '- normal project workflows should go through `gwc` - when you intentionally run raw wasm commands, Windows users should use PowerShell environment assignment and macOS/Linux users may use shell environment prefixes such as `GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm` - `wasm_exec.js` must come from the same Go toolchain version that produced the wasm binary - browser-only code must still be kept behind browser execution paths because native `go test` does not provide `syscall/js`', 0.9, 'pass', '', 3311, 3772, '- normal project workflows should go through `gwc` - when you intentionally run raw wasm commands, Windows users should use PowerShell environment assignment and macOS/Linux users may use shell environment prefixes such as `GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm` - `wasm_exec.js` must come from the same Go toolchain version that produced the wasm binary - browser-only code must still be kept behind browser execution paths becau