('3ffdb04681224b1add0bb19161797db3377f1921', 'docs/PWA.md', 'PWA and Offline App Support', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'The project may still grow additional manifest tooling later, but the current contract already includes the shipped manifest helper surface rather than only a future boundary.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 5010, 5185, 'The project may still grow additional manifest tooling later, but the current contract already includes the shipped manifest helper surface rather than only a future boundary.', 'The project may still grow additional manifest tooling later, but the current contract already includes the shipped manifest helper surface rather than only a future boundary.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 5010, 5185, 'The project may still grow additional manifest tooling later, but the current contract already includes the shipped manifest helper surface rather than only a future boundary.', 'The project may still grow additional manifest tooling later, but the current contract already includes the shipped manifest helper surface rather than only a future boundary.', 0, 0, 'manual-pwa-20260330T214722072Z', 'ccc970ee7d17b69d151e188b2a8639fed48782e05b623f5c4789510f217dd3f1', '95fb3113bb6eff2e21427b0d70445aad0c5200406980fef532cace7dac761dd2', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('b59c1433b9bfd5a96b4f1a4b3c193bb18cd93def', 'docs/PWA.md', 'PWA and Offline App Support', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Durable browser persistence now has a defined first-party seam through `interop.OpenPersistentStore(...)` plus the cache, queue, and state helpers layered on top of it. The current storage model is intentionally narrow: one logical feature store maps to one IndexedDB object store with string keys and JSON-friendly string payloads, database-version bumps own schema creation, blocked upgrades surface structured diagnostics, quota failures stay typed, and corruption recovery is opt-in so reconstructible caches can reset safely without silently deleting mutation or state data.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 5187, 5766, 'Durable browser persistence now has a defined first-party seam through `interop.OpenPersistentStore(...)` plus the cache, queue, and state helpers layered on top of it. The current storage model is intentionally narrow: one logical feature store maps to one IndexedDB object store with string keys and JSON-friendly string payloads, database-version bumps own schema creation, blocked upgrades surface structured diagnostics, quota failures stay typed, and corruption recovery is opt-in so reconstructible caches can reset safely without silently deleting mutation or state data.', 'Durable browser persistence now has a defined first-party seam through `interop.OpenPersistentStore(...)` plus the cache, queue, and state helpers layered on top of it. The current storage model is intentionally narrow: one logical feature store maps to one IndexedDB object store with string keys and JSON-friendly string payloads, database-version bumps own schema creation, blocked upgrades surface structured diagnostics, quota failures stay typed, and corruption recovery is opt-in so reconstructible caches can reset safely without silently deleting mutation or state data.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 5187, 5766, 'Durable browser persistence now has a defined first-party seam through `interop.OpenPersistentStore(...)` plus the cache, queue, and state helpers layered on top of it. The current storage model is intentionally narrow: one logical feature store maps to one IndexedDB object store with string keys and JSON-friendly string payloads, database-version bumps own schema creation, blocked upgrades surface structured diagnostics, quota failures stay typed, and corruption recovery is opt-in so reconstructible caches can reset safely without silently deleting mutation or state data.', 'Durable browser persistence now has a defined first-party seam through `interop.OpenPersistentStore(...)` plus the cache, queue, and state helpers layered on top of it. The current storage model is intentionally narrow: one logical feature store maps to one IndexedDB object store with string keys and JSON-friendly string payloads, database-version bumps own schema creation, blocked upgrades surface structured diagnostics, quota failures stay typed, and corruption recovery is opt-in so reconstructible caches can reset safely without silently deleting mutation or state data.', 0, 0, 'manual-pwa-20260330T214722072Z', 'ccc970ee7d17b69d151e188b2a8639fed48782e05b623f5c4789510f217dd3f1', '81c47f38194fcfecf56ea968aebe5baa8e08190ce215b8302b480bdcc5f2685c', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
