('36d3f2ff476012a4814f6a44617964457a6b5fc8', 'docs/ROUTER_AUTH.md', 'Router Async Guards And Auth Design', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '1. use a synchronous `BeforeEnter` redirect when the session is already known to be unauthenticated 2. preserve the requested internal target with `PreserveReturnTo(...)` 3. recover the target on the login route with `ReadReturnTo(...)` 4. use `nav.Replace(...)` after sign-in so the transient login route does not linger in history 5. render manual authorizing or unauthorized content inside the protected route when session resolution or subsection claims remain application-owned 6. keep server authorization authoritative for SSR responses, APIs, and mutations', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 6094, 6658, '1. use a synchronous `BeforeEnter` redirect when the session is already known to be unauthenticated 2. preserve the requested internal target with `PreserveReturnTo(...)` 3. recover the target on the login route with `ReadReturnTo(...)` 4. use `nav.Replace(...)` after sign-in so the transient login route does not linger in history 5. render manual authorizing or unauthorized content inside the protected route when session resolution or subsection claims remain application-owned 6. keep server authorization authoritative for SSR responses, APIs, and mutations', '1. use a synchronous `BeforeEnter` redirect when the session is already known to be unauthenticated 2. preserve the requested internal target with `PreserveReturnTo(...)` 3. recover the target on the login route with `ReadReturnTo(...)` 4. use `nav.Replace(...)` after sign-in so the transient login route does not linger in history 5. render manual authorizing or unauthorized content inside the protected route when session resolution or subsection claims remain application-owned 6. keep server authorization authoritative for SSR responses, APIs, and mutations', 0.9, 'pass', '', 6094, 6658, '1. use a synchronous `BeforeEnter` redirect when the session is already known to be unauthenticated 2. preserve the requested internal target with `PreserveReturnTo(...)` 3. recover the target on the login route with `ReadReturnTo(...)` 4. use `nav.Replace(...)` after sign-in so the transient login route does not linger in history 5. render manual authorizing or unauthorized content inside the protected route when session resolution or subsection claims remain application-owned 6. keep server authorization authoritative for SSR responses, APIs, and mutations', '1. use a synchronous `BeforeEnter` redirect when the session is already known to be unauthenticated 2. preserve the requested internal target with `PreserveReturnTo(...)` 3. recover the target on the login route with `ReadReturnTo(...)` 4. use `nav.Replace(...)` after sign-in so the transient login route does not linger in history 5. render manual authorizing or unauthorized content inside the protected route when session resolution or subsection claims remain application-owned 6. keep server authorization authoritative for SSR responses, APIs, and mutations', 0, 0, 'manual-router_auth-20260330T214722106Z', 'db9a6446af37a0d655bbd1ab499a0467bca4e3536feb6d46ede124db7871d585', '6a9631148ef7eb999317448a62c2a312529a21a96cd6983d15b7f5b58481825f', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
