('ac04bac98f9dbe00f733210f9c653629eed4dde6', 'docs/RUNNER_CONFIG.md', 'Runner Config Schema', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- Add new runner-owned path fields in the shared Go `tools/runnerconfig` package first. - Keep launcher-owned consumers aligned with the same field names and relative-path semantics. - Validate the canonical example from each consumer surface so schema drift is caught by tests before release.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 1387, 1680, '- Add new runner-owned path fields in the shared Go `tools/runnerconfig` package first. - Keep launcher-owned consumers aligned with the same field names and relative-path semantics. - Validate the canonical example from each consumer surface so schema drift is caught by tests before release.', '- Add new runner-owned path fields in the shared Go `tools/runnerconfig` package first. - Keep launcher-owned consumers aligned with the same field names and relative-path semantics. - Validate the canonical example from each consumer surface so schema drift is caught by tests before release.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 1387, 1680, '- Add new runner-owned path fields in the shared Go `tools/runnerconfig` package first. - Keep launcher-owned consumers aligned with the same field names and relative-path semantics. - Validate the canonical example from each consumer surface so schema drift is caught by tests before release.', '- Add new runner-owned path fields in the shared Go `tools/runnerconfig` package first. - Keep launcher-owned consumers aligned with the same field names and relative-path semantics. - Validate the canonical example from each consumer surface so schema drift is caught by tests before release.', 0, 0, 'manual-runner_config-20260330T214722145Z', '867366aadb058e77b48231ff0b37fed545303f90d8e503b1492ca16113fad28d', '2c57ac810ea5e757cf340045489c7074c45ca1a0b161011baa97532880d4746d', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('fce0b04ff891e4f98fde72e46b722898a580ec05', 'docs/RUNNER_CONFIG.md', 'Runner Config Schema', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- Put organization-wide enforcement, trusted executable roots, inherited environment policy, and company-standard runner paths in a centrally managed config distributed through `GWC_RUNNER_CONFIG` or a shared home-level `.gwc/runner.json`. - Put project-local workspace layout choices in checked-in `gwc-runner.json` only when the whole repository needs the same browser workspace, livereload workspace, or artifact policy for every contributor. - Keep short-lived experimentation, one-off output destinations, and local debugging needs on explicit command flags instead of committing them into runner config. - Prefer the org-managed layer for security and compliance rules, the project layer for reproducible repository layout, and CLI flags for temporary operator intent.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 1703, 2477, '- Put organization-wide enforcement, trusted executable roots, inherited environment policy, and company-standard runner paths in a centrally managed config distributed through `GWC_RUNNER_CONFIG` or a shared home-level `.gwc/runner.json`. - Put project-local workspace layout choices in checked-in `gwc-runner.json` only when the whole repository needs the same browser workspace, livereload workspace, or artifact policy for every contributor. - Keep short-lived experimentation, one-off output destinations, and local debugging needs on explicit command flags instead of committing them into runner config. - Prefer the org-managed layer for security and compliance rules, the project layer for reproducible repository layout, and CLI flags for temporary operator intent.', '- Put organization-wide enforcement, trusted executable roots, inherited environment policy, and company-standard runner paths in a centrally managed config distributed through `GWC_RUNNER_CONFIG` or a shared home-level `.gwc/runner.json`. - Put project-local workspace layout choices in checked-in `gwc-runner.json` only when the whole repository needs the same browser workspace, livereload workspace, or artifact policy for every contributor. - Keep short-lived experimentation, one-off output destinations, and local debugging needs on explicit command flags instead of committing them into runner config. - Prefer the org-managed layer for security and compliance rules, the project layer for reproducible repository layout, and CLI flags for temporary operator intent.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 1703, 2477, '- Put organization-wide enforcement, trusted executable roots, inherited environment policy, and company-standard runner paths in a centrally managed config distributed through `GWC_RUNNER_CONFIG` or a shared home-level `.gwc/runner.json`. - Put project-local workspace layout choices in checked-in `gwc-runner.json` only when the whole repository needs the same browser workspace, livereload workspace, or artifact policy for every contributor. - Keep short-lived experimentation, one-off output destinations, and local debugging needs on explicit command flags instead of committing them into runner config. - Prefer the org-managed layer for security and compliance rules, the project layer for reproducible repository layout, and CLI flags for temporary operator intent.', '- Put organization-wide enforcement, trusted executable roots, inherited environment policy, and company-standard runner paths in a centrally managed config distributed through `GWC_RUNNER_CONFIG` or a shared home-level `.gwc/runner.json`. - Put project-local workspace layout choices in checked-in `gwc-runner.json` only when the whole repository needs the same browser workspace, livereload workspace, or artifact policy for every contributor. - Keep short-lived experimentation, one-off output destinations, and local debugging needs on explicit command flags instead of committing them into runner config. - Prefer the org-managed layer for security and compliance rules, the project layer for reproducible repository layout, and CLI flags for temporary operator intent.', 0, 0, 'manual-runner_config-20260330T214722145Z', '867366aadb058e77b48231ff0b37fed545303f90d8e503b1492ca16113fad28d', '3d15267d0ddcbb03ee5a6372455e7a6933825cee82fc1e7b5312dcfbb9f98bb8', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now'));

