('1841d225d3c8e9737398daaf8375f3957e20b410', 'docs/SECURITY.md', 'Security, Compliance, and Governance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- never emit raw cookies, authorization headers, CSRF secrets, bootstrap payload bodies, or full form submissions into framework-owned logs - prefer route ids, status codes, durations, cache keys, mutation kinds, counts, and payload-size metrics over raw payload content - keep correlation ids opaque and non-user-identifying - treat diagnostics metadata and devtools snapshots under the same redaction boundary as logs - do not assume snapshot export is safe for production support bundles unless the application has already reviewed what the runtime can observe', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 6771, 7334, '- never emit raw cookies, authorization headers, CSRF secrets, bootstrap payload bodies, or full form submissions into framework-owned logs - prefer route ids, status codes, durations, cache keys, mutation kinds, counts, and payload-size metrics over raw payload content - keep correlation ids opaque and non-user-identifying - treat diagnostics metadata and devtools snapshots under the same redaction boundary as logs - do not assume snapshot export is safe for production support bundles unless the application has already reviewed what the runtime can observe', '- never emit raw cookies, authorization headers, CSRF secrets, bootstrap payload bodies, or full form submissions into framework-owned logs - prefer route ids, status codes, durations, cache keys, mutation kinds, counts, and payload-size metrics over raw payload content - keep correlation ids opaque and non-user-identifying - treat diagnostics metadata and devtools snapshots under the same redaction boundary as logs - do not assume snapshot export is safe for production support bundles unless the application has already reviewed what the runtime can observe', 0.9, 'pass', '', 6771, 7334, '- never emit raw cookies, authorization headers, CSRF secrets, bootstrap payload bodies, or full