('eefeb2cc45c381e7cca334ad7dccd512947f93d3', 'docs\AUTH_AND_SESSION_INTEGRATION.md', 'Auth And Session Integration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- SSR handlers can resolve the current user before render - same-origin form posts and API calls can reuse the same session boundary - the browser does not need raw upstream bearer tokens just to make ordinary app requests - logout and expiry can be handled once in the server session layer instead of copied across multiple client transports', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 1520, 1862, '- SSR handlers can resolve the current user before render - same-origin form posts and API calls can reuse the same session boundary - the browser does not need raw upstream bearer tokens just to make ordinary app requests - logout and expiry can be handled once in the server session layer instead of copied across multiple client transports', '- SSR handlers can resolve the current user before render - same-origin form posts and API calls can reuse the same session boundary - the browser does not need raw upstream bearer tokens just to make ordinary app requests - logout and expiry can be handled once in the server session layer instead of copied across multiple client transports', 0.9, 'pass', '', 1520, 1862, '- SSR handlers can resolve the current user before render - same-origin form posts and API calls can reuse the same session boundary - the browser does not need raw upstream bearer tokens just to make ordinary app requests - logout and expiry can be handled once in the server session layer instead of copied across multiple client transports', '- SSR handlers can resolve the current user before render - same-origin form posts and API calls can reuse the same session boundary - the browser does not need raw upstream bearer tokens just to make ordinary app requests - logout and expiry can be handled once in the server session layer instead of copied across multiple client transports', 0, 0, 'manual-auth_and_session_integration-20260330T2148