('62699c73e8473a61db970f7bbaa41b93e85efb84', 'docs\BROWSER_SUPPORT.md', 'Browser Support', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- if prerendered or SSR content exists, prefer serving readable static content over a broken interactive shell - if the full application cannot run, show a clear unsupported-browser message instead of silent failure - distinguish between fully unsupported browsers and partially supported browsers where only optional features are unavailable - provide direct fallback actions when possible, such as a plain form post, a non-enhanced document view, or a link to a supported environment', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10410, 10895, '- if prerendered or SSR content exists, prefer serving readable static content over a broken interactive shell - if the full application cannot run, show a clear unsupported-browser message instead of silent failure - distinguish between fully unsupported browsers and partially supported browsers where only optional features are unavailable - provide direct fallback actions when possible, such as a plain form post, a non-enhanced document view, or a link to a supported environment', '- if prerendered or SSR content exists, prefer serving readable static content over a broken interactive shell - if the full application cannot run, show a clear unsupported-browser message instead of silent failure - distinguish between fully unsupported browsers and partially supported browsers where only optional features are unavailable - provide direct fallback actions when possible, such as a plain form post, a non-enhanced document view, or a link to a supported environment', 0.9, 'pass', '', 10410, 10895, '- if prerendered or SSR content exists, prefer serving readable static content over a broken interactive shell - if the full application cannot run, show a clear unsupported-browser message instead of silent failure - distinguish between fully unsupported browsers and partially supported browsers where only optional features are unavailab