('ae83316ad62d0f8cad7fc77aeb1930f980bbbcf4', 'docs\CACHE.md', 'Shared Cache Design', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- `trust-once` The seeded value is treated as ready and fresh until normal invalidation or `StaleAfter` says otherwise. - `stale-while-revalidate` The seeded value remains visible, and the first client read marks it stale only when the embedded timestamp is already older than the bootstrap entry''s `staleAfter` window or when that timestamp is absent. - `always-refetch` The seeded value remains visible for first paint, but the first client subscriber still forces an authoritative load regardless of the embedded timestamp.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 9442, 9974, '- `trust-once` The seeded value is treated as ready and fresh until normal invalidation or `StaleAfter` says otherwise. - `stale-while-revalidate` The seeded value remains visible, and the first client read marks it stale only when the embedded timestamp is already older than the bootstrap entry''s `staleAfter` window or when that timestamp is absent. - `always-refetch` The seeded value remains visible for first paint, but the first client subscriber still forces an authoritative load regardless of the embedded timestamp.', '- `trust-once` The seeded value is treated as ready and fresh until normal invalidation or `StaleAfter` says otherwise. - `stale-while-revalidate` The seeded value remains visible, and the first client read marks it stale only when the embedded timestamp is already older than the bootstrap entry''s `staleAfter` window or when that timestamp is absent. - `always-refetch` The seeded value remains visible for first paint, but the first client subscriber still forces an authoritative load regardless of the embedded timestamp.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 9442, 9974, '- `trust-once` The seeded value is treated as ready and fresh until normal invalidation or `StaleAfter` says otherwise. - `stale-while-revalidate` The seeded value remains visible, and the first client read marks it stale only when the embedded timestamp is already older than the bootstrap entry''s `staleAfter` window or when that timestamp is absent. - `always-refetch` The seeded value remains visible for first paint, but the first client subscriber still forces an authoritative load regardless of the embedded timestamp.', '- `trust-once` The seeded value is treated as ready and fresh until normal invalidation or `StaleAfter` says otherwise. - `stale-while-revalidate` The seeded value remains visible, and the first client read marks it stale only when the embedded timestamp is already older than the bootstrap entry''s `staleAfter` window or when that timestamp is absent. - `always-refetch` The seeded value remains visible for first paint, but the first client subscriber still forces an authoritative load regardless of the embedded timestamp.', 0, 0, 'manual-cache-20260330T214856081Z', '1e4fdf979005e827fc0eff3d189fe6140b80823a5c21ede3b573b92bceee754c', 'ef5e7f06fcf54ad703ea6550cb1250dd0ca8894999913186834ebf2183d1c7b0', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('9936651f679b4d0e7bb9a1557f1659368d2a0e00', 'docs\CACHE.md', 'Shared Cache Design', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'These policies are explicit because startup speed and freshness are different product choices.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 9976, 10070, 'These policies are explicit because startup speed and freshness are different product choices.', 'These policies are explicit because startup speed and freshness are different product choices.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 9976, 10070, 'These policies are explicit because startup speed and freshness are different product choices.', 'These policies are explicit because startup speed and freshness are different product choices.', 0, 0, 'manual-cache-20260330T214856081Z', '1e4fdf979005e827fc0eff3d189fe6140b80823a5c21ede3b573b92bceee754c', 'eb83fb4eb87df3cd2ebfed270345b6a880893e14445c27ab18a24749b9ac3af2', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('e2d1e9079dad68e8ce394ce24d61448a128c8cf7', 'docs\CACHE.md', 'Shared Cache Design', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Cached values should stay JSON-shaped when they are candidates for route-loader reuse or SSR bootstrap.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10097, 10200, 'Cached values should stay JSON-shaped when they are candidates for route-loader reuse or SSR bootstrap.', 'Cached values should stay JSON-shaped when they are candidates for route-loader reuse or SSR bootstrap.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 10097, 10200, 'Cached values should stay JSON-shaped when they are candidates for route-loader reuse or SSR bootstrap.', 'Cached values should stay JSON-shaped when they are candidates for route-loader reuse or SSR bootstrap.', 0, 0, 'manual-cache-20260330T214856081Z', '1e4fdf979005e827fc0eff3d189fe6140b80823a5c21ede3b573b92bceee754c', '86104d73cde16fb5e78ca4c7256747488e8584a31c588176b33798fc67148c09', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('bf0b15f7c86b9675b99a44c77076bb5054a32871', 'docs\CACHE.md', 'Shared Cache Design', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- strings, numbers, booleans, arrays, maps, and plain structs are safe defaults - avoid storing opaque browser handles, callbacks, or environment-specific objects in shared cached values - keep secrets and server-only authorization context out of any value that might later become bootstrap data - keep payloads intentionally small so the first HTML response does not bloat for one oversized cache entry - use one bootstrap entry per normalized cache key instead of embedding ad hoc mixed payloads - prefer values that round-trip through standard JSON without custom codecs unless the server and client both deliberately own a stronger transport', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10222, 10867, '- strings, numbers, booleans, arrays, maps, and plain structs are safe defaults - avoid storing opaque browser handles, callbacks, or environment-specific objects in shared cached values - keep secrets and server-only authorization context out of any value that might later become bootstrap data - keep payloads intentionally small so the first HTML response does not bloat for one oversized cache entry - use one bootstrap entry per normalized cache key instead of embedding ad hoc mixed payloads - prefer values that round-trip through standard JSON without custom codecs unless the server and client both deliberately own a stronger transport', '- strings, numbers, booleans, arrays, maps, and plain structs are safe defaults - avoid storing opaque browser handles, callbacks, or environment-specific objects in shared cached values - keep secrets and server-only authorization context out of any value that might later become bootstrap data - keep payloads intentionally small so the first HTML response does not bloat for one oversized cache entry - use one bootstrap entry per normalized cache key instead of embedding ad hoc mixed payloads - prefer values that round-trip through standard