('acc394788eac0fd84fd001eb5299725e34a582b7', 'docs\CLIENT_SHELL_ROUTING.md', 'Single-Shell Routing Patterns', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- one `js/wasm` client shell should own public and private routes - one router tree should host both marketing and workspace route families - one shared shell layout should own navigation, metadata defaults, and global providers - route-family shells should layer public and authenticated concerns without duplicate app roots - code splitting should keep shell-entry cost stable as route count grows', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 379, 778, '- one `js/wasm` client shell should own public and private routes - one router tree should host both marketing and workspace route families - one shared shell layout should own navigation, metadata defaults, and global providers - route-family shells should layer public and authenticated concerns without duplicate app roots - code splitting should keep shell-entry cost stable as route count grows', '- one `js/wasm` client shell should own public and private routes - one router tree should host both marketing and workspace route families - one shared shell layout should own navigation, metadata defaults, and global providers - route-family shells should layer public and authenticated concerns without duplicate app roots - code splitting should keep shell-entry cost stable as route count grows', 0.9, 'pass', '', 379, 778, '- one `js/wasm` client shell should own public and private routes - one router tree should host both marketing and workspace route families - one shared shell layout should own navigation, metadata defaults, and global providers - route-family shells should layer public and authenticated concerns without duplicate app roots - code splitting should keep shell-entry cost stable as route count grows', '- one `js/wasm` client shell should own public and private routes - one router tree should host both marketing and workspace route families - one shared shell layout should own navigat