('54d49e4daeb548abeb19983ea2a8e357eb7b4e2e', 'docs\CODE_SPLITTING.md', 'Code Splitting And Bundle Loading', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- prefetch only the routes that are likely next, such as sibling detail pages, the immediate next step in a wizard, or the next tab in a high-intent flow - keep route bundles named after the user-facing area they represent so profiling and cache invalidation stay understandable - if a route is required for the initial landing experience, treat it as part of the shell rather than as a deferred route chunk - align browser-router, SSR, and prerender routes on the same logical split boundaries so the server and client agree on which chunk family owns each screen', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 5680, 6244, '- prefetch only the routes that are likely next, such as sibling detail pages, the immediate next step in a wizard, or the next tab in a high-intent flow - keep route bundles named after the user-facing area they represent so profiling and cache invalidation stay understandable - if a route is required for the initial landing experience, treat it as part of the shell rather than as a deferred route chunk - align browser-router, SSR, and prerender routes on the same logical split boundaries so the server and client agree on which chunk family owns each screen', '- prefetch only the routes that are likely next, such as sibling detail pages, the immediate next step in a wizard, or the next tab in a high-intent flow - keep route bundles named after the user-facing area they represent so profiling and cache invalidation stay understandable - if a route is required for the initial landing experience, treat it as part of the shell rather than as a deferred route chunk - align browser-router, SSR, and prerender routes on the same logical split boundaries so the server and client agree on which chunk family owns each screen', 0.9, 'pass', '', 5680, 6244, '- prefetch only the routes that are likely next, such as sibling detail pages, the immedia