('52ab8142cd51cb495b4d7c7e9e8cc2fe0efb9879', 'docs\CODE_SPLITTING.md', 'Code Splitting And Bundle Loading', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- use `ui.Lazy` for nested panels, dialogs, tabs, widgets, or feature islands that can mount after the main route shell - pair every lazy subtree with an obvious pending fallback so the user sees that work is happening instead of a blank gap - pair every lazy subtree with an error fallback that explains the failure and exposes a retry or recovery path - use `ui.AsyncBoundary` when the lazy subtree needs a distinct pending state, delay, or timeout treatment around the component - use `ui.ErrorBoundary` when the lazy subtree should recover locally without taking down the route shell - keep lazy component boundaries stable across rerenders so the loading surface does not move around under the user - avoid deferring components that are required for the first meaningful interaction on the current route', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 6465, 7273, '- use `ui.Lazy` for nested panels, dialogs, tabs, widgets, or feature islands that can mount after the main route shell - pair every lazy subtree with an obvious pending fallback so the user sees that work is happening instead of a blank gap - pair every lazy subtree with an error fallback that explains the failure and exposes a retry or recovery path - use `ui.AsyncBoundary` when the lazy subtree needs a distinct pending state, delay, or timeout treatment around the component - use `ui.ErrorBoundary` when the lazy subtree should recover locally without taking down the route shell - keep lazy component boundaries stable across rerenders so the loading surface does not move around under the user - avoid deferring components that are required for the first meaningful interaction on the current route', '- use `ui.Lazy` for nested panels, dialogs, tabs, widgets, or feature islands that can mount after the main route shell - pair every lazy subtree with an obvious pending fallback so the user sees tha