cally without taking down the route shell - keep lazy component boundaries stable across rerenders so the loading surface does not move around under the user - avoid deferring components that are required for the first meaningful interaction on the current route', 0, 0, 'manual-code_splitting-20260330T214856098Z', 'd5091a33e378c060491d57258ec5b59832126624ada2918791a135dc42163a50', 'f10b275ec683615deb71c28dfb3705d9689d1c33a7c0f8c15856fbea705d43d9', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('2ee27a31cbf83454254886030f9add19d8ddc8ff', 'docs\CODE_SPLITTING.md', 'Code Splitting And Bundle Loading', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- preserve layout with fixed sizing, skeletons, or placeholder containers so the deferred subtree does not cause layout shift - if a component owns state that must survive hydration or resumed state, ensure the state is available before the lazy boundary activates or keep that component in the critical shell - keep retry controls explicit so users can ask for the deferred subtree again without reloading the whole page - if a component has a large visual or data cost but is still visible above the fold, prefer a shell-friendly split that keeps the immediate interactive surface intact - treat lazy child components as load-on-demand leaves, not as a way to hide the route''s essential structure', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 7296, 7994, '- preserve layout with fixed sizing, skeletons, or placeholder containers so the deferred subtree does not cause layout shift - if a component owns state that must survive hydration or resumed state, ensure the state is available before the lazy boundary activates or keep that component in the critical shell - keep retry controls explicit so users can ask for the deferred subtree again without reloading the whole page - if a component has a large visual or data cost but is still visible above the fold, prefer a shell-friendly split that keeps the immediate interactive surface intact - treat lazy child components as load-on-demand leaves, not as a way to hide the route''s essential structure', '- preserve layout with fixed sizing, skeletons, or placeholder containers so the deferred subtree does not cause layout shift - if a component owns state that must survive hydration or resumed state, ensure the state is available before the lazy boundary activates or keep that component in the critical shell - keep retry controls explicit so users can ask for the deferred subtree again without reloading the whole page - if a component has a large visual or data cost but is still visible above the fold, prefer a shell-friendly split that keeps the immediate interactive surface intact - treat lazy child components as load-on-demand leaves, not as a way to hide the route''s essential structure', 0.9, 'pass', '', 7296, 7994, '- preserve layout with fixed sizing, skeletons, or placeholder containers so the deferred subtree does not cause layout shift - if a component owns state that must survive hydration or resumed state, ensure the state is available before the lazy boundary activates or keep that component in the critical shell - keep retry controls explicit so users can ask for the deferred subtree again without reloading the whole page - if a component has a large visual or data cost but is still visible above the fold, prefer a shell-friendly split that keeps the immediate interactive surface intact - treat lazy child components as load-on-demand leaves, not as a way to hide the route''s essential structure', '- preserve layout with fixed sizing, skeletons, or placeholder containers so the deferred subtree does not cause layout shift - if a component owns state that must survive hydration or resumed state, ensure the state is available before the lazy boundary activates or keep that component in the critical shell - keep retry controls explicit so users can ask for the deferred subtree again without reloading the whole page - if a component has a large visual or data cost but is still visible above the fold, prefer a shell-friendly split that keeps the immediate interactive surface intact - treat lazy child components as load-on-demand leaves, not as a way to hide the route''s essential structure', 0, 0, 'manual-code_splitting-20260330T214856098Z', 'd5091a33e378c060491d57258ec5b59832126624ada2918791a135dc42163a50', 'f182eb1f94b33bebb80c149e164048c5cc66d6926a1d0b261948f1d3fffa03f8', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('7b63250aeeaa5898638118279337c7f9709b01a8', 'docs\CODE_SPLITTING.md', 'Code Splitting And Bundle Loading', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Server-rendered and prerendered pages should know which chunks are required before the client starts interactive work.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 8018, 8136, 'Server-rendered and prerendered pages should know which chunks are required before the client starts interactive work.', 'Server-rendered and prerendered pages should know which chunks are required before the client starts interactive work.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 8018, 8136, 'Server-rendered and prerendered pages should know which chunks are required before the client starts interactive work.', 'Server-rendered and prerendered pages should know which chunks are required before the client starts interactive work.', 0, 0, 'manual-code_splitting-20260330T214856098Z', 'd5091a33e378c060491d57258ec5b59832126624ada2918791a135dc42163a50', '5a1a417298e531a20ce5399c413597d4c75e15371b28d414efdf68ffe2868f31', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('11211c16dbfdc841cbb652045908998532e34827', 'docs\CODE_SPLITTING.md', 'Code Splitting And Bundle Loading', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'The intended rule is:', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 8138, 8159, 'The intended rule is:', 'The intended rule is:', 0.9, 'pass', '', 8138, 8159, 'The intended rule is:', 'The intended rule is:', 0, 0, 'manual-code_splitting-20260330T214856098Z', 'd5091a33e378c060491d57258ec5b59832126624ada2918791a135dc42163a50', '8784cfb0f288e1e3558e040ad8c7251b9c00120ad4cdac067b7a0c0ed8a0f897', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('d1768da0701ff5d0ae9314c1c2a09a1cbbbf5478', 'docs\CODE_SPLITTING.md', 'Code Splitting And Bundle Loading', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- the server or prerender output should emit a manifest-backed chunk declaration for the resolved route or page shell - the document should include the shell code plus any chunks needed for first paint or first interaction, either through direct preload hints or an equivalent bootstrap reference - chunk discovery should use the same logical names and manifest lookup rules that the build tooling emitted, not guessed filenames - lazy chunks may load later, but hydration should not race a missing shell dependency - if a page depends on a deferred chunk during immediate resume, that chunk should be treated as part of the critical delivery path - bundle order should be resolved by the manifest and the runtime loader, not by template ordering alone', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 8161, 8913, '- the server or prerender output should emit a manifest-backed chunk declaration for the resolved route or page shell - the document should include the shell code plus any chunks needed for first paint or first interaction, either through direct preload hints or an equivalent bootstrap reference - chunk discovery should use the same logical names and manifest lookup rules that the build tooling emitted, not guessed filenames - lazy chunks may load later, but hydration should not race a missing shell dependency - if a page depends on a deferred chunk during immediate resume, that chunk should be treated as part of the critical delivery path - bundle order should be resolved by the manifest and the runtime loader, not by template ordering alone', '- the server or prerender output should emit a manifest-backed chunk declaration for the resolved route or page shell - the document should include the shell code plus any chunks needed for first paint or first interaction, either through direct preload hints or an equivalent bootstrap reference - chunk discov