('bd0b508354383c34dcca766afa79d4b5ca1d9268', 'docs\CROSS_TAB.md', 'Cross-Tab Synchronization', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- use last-writer-wins only for low-risk preferences such as theme, density, sidebar openness, or active model selection - publish the smallest changed preference slice rather than a full workspace snapshot - if a preference also lives on the server, treat the browser fanout as a fast local hint and let the next authoritative server read or mutation confirm the final value - preference fanout should update open tabs for the same active session, not rehydrate dormant or signed-out tabs into a new identity automatically', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 7343, 7876, '- use last-writer-wins only for low-risk preferences such as theme, density, sidebar openness, or active model selection - publish the smallest changed preference slice rather than a full workspace snapshot - if a preference also lives on the server, treat the browser fanout as a fast local hint and let the next authoritative server read or mutation confirm the final value - preference fanout should update open tabs for the same active session, not rehydrate dormant or signed-out tabs into a new identity automatically', '- use last-writer-wins only for low-risk preferences such as theme, density, sidebar openness, or active model selection - publish the smallest changed preference slice rather than a full workspace snapshot - if a preference also lives on the server, treat the browser fanout as a fast local hint and let the next authoritative server read or mutation confirm the final value - preference fanout should update open tabs for the same active session, not rehydrate dormant or signed-out tabs into a new identity automatically', 0.9, 'pass', '', 7343, 7876, '- use last-writer-wins only for low-risk preferences such as theme, density, sidebar openness, or active model selection - publish the smallest changed preference slice rather than a full workspace snapshot - if a preference also lives on the server, treat the browser fanout as a fast local hint and let the next authoritative server read or mutation confirm the final value - preference fanout should update open tabs for the same active session, not rehydrate dormant or signed-out tabs into a new identity automatically', '- use last-writer-wins only for low-risk preferences such as theme, density, sidebar openness, or active model selection - publish the smallest changed preference slice rather than a full workspace snapshot - if a preference also lives on the server, treat the browser fanout as a fast local hint and let the next authoritative server read or mutation confirm the final value - preference fanout should update open tabs for the same active session, not rehydrate dormant or signed-out tabs into a new identity automatically', 0, 0, 'manual-cross_tab-20260330T214856134Z', '7eb6a2c78d5c69a328820c688c9f50c72857c4a79e330d48c8757704699173eb', '801bf8bd9d1eca56c781afda7d757cdafa8627ef25e9b883cd598f8f8d770e16', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('46ba0ee63796f00df3d7ee57ae72dc20e616d7f0', 'docs\CROSS_TAB.md', 'Cross-Tab Synchronization', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Cross-tab synchronization should not blindly overwrite fresher state restored from SSR bootstrap or persisted snapshots.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 7915, 8035, 'Cross-tab synchronization should not blindly overwrite fresher state restored from SSR bootstrap or persisted snapshots.', 'Cross-tab synchronization should not blindly overwrite fresher state restored from SSR bootstrap or persisted snapshots.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 7915, 8035, 'Cross-tab synchronization should not blindly overwrite fresher state restored from SSR bootstrap or persisted snapshots.', 'Cross-tab synchronization should not blindly overwrite fresher state restored from SSR bootstrap or persisted snapshots.', 0, 0, 'manual-cross_tab-20260330T214856134Z', '7eb6a2c78d5c69a328820c688c9f50c72857c4a79e330d48c8757704699173eb', '167eef31c5326a85386f2ec73db2a032d35e89bb6c2d165ea196bc319f7e45d3', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('324358a744747e9d81c7f3a0f62fda6861d28d7c', 'docs\CROSS_TAB.md', 'Cross-Tab Synchronization', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- restore SSR bootstrap or persisted snapshots first - open cross-tab channels after the owning state is initialized - ignore incoming messages that are older than the locally restored revision or timestamp - for cache-backed data, prefer cross-tab invalidation messages that trigger revalidation instead of shipping full bootstrap payloads across tabs - for auth hints, treat a narrowing change such as logout as authoritative immediately, but re-check expansive changes such as regained privileges against the app''s real auth source', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 8057, 8591, '- restore SSR bootstrap or persisted snapshots first - open cross-tab channels after the owning state is initialized - ignore incoming messages that are older than the locally restored revision or timestamp - for cache-backed data, prefer cross-tab invalidation messages that trigger revalidation instead of shipping full bootstrap payloads across tabs - for auth hints, treat a narrowing change such as logout as authoritative immediately, but re-check expansive changes such as regained privileges against the app''s real auth source', '- restore SSR bootstrap or persisted snapshots first - open cross-tab channels after the owning state is initialized - ignore incoming messages that are older than the locally restored revision or timestamp - for cache-backed data, prefer cross-tab invalidation messages that trigger revalidation instead of shipping full bootstrap payloads across tabs - for auth hints, treat a narrowing change such as logout as authoritative immediately, but re-check expansive changes such as regained privileges against the app''s real auth source', 0.9, 'pass', '', 8057, 8591, '- restore SSR bootstrap or persisted snapshots first - open cross-tab channels after the owning state is initialized - ignore incoming messages that are older than the locally restored revis