('027a6bb43c5b8d813c6ff309a2642a6e9cc875bb', 'docs\DATA_LOADING_AND_MUTATION_ARCHITECTURE.md', 'Data Loading And Mutation Architecture', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- using atoms as a shadow async cache - putting every read into route loaders even when it is deeply local - using `UseFetch(...)` everywhere instead of typed resources - inventing inconsistent cache keys across route and component readers - optimistic updates without a revalidation or rollback path - durable offline queueing for writes that should just fail fast', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 7745, 8110, '- using atoms as a shadow async cache - putting every read into route loaders even when it is deeply local - using `UseFetch(...)` everywhere instead of typed resources - inventing inconsistent cache keys across route and component readers - optimistic updates without a revalidation or rollback path - durable offline queueing for writes that should just fail fast', '- using atoms as a shadow async cache - putting every read into route loaders even when it is deeply local - using `UseFetch(...)` everywhere instead of typed resources - inventing inconsistent cache keys across route and component readers - optimistic updates without a revalidation or rollback path - durable offline queueing for writes that should just fail fast', 0.9, 'pass', '', 7745, 8110, '- using atoms as a shadow async cache - putting every read into route loaders even when it is deeply local - using `UseFetch(...)` everywhere instead of typed resources - inventing inconsistent cache keys across route and component readers - optimistic updates without a revalidation or rollback path - durable offline queueing for writes that should just fail fast', '- using atoms as a shadow async cache - putting every read into route loaders even when it is deeply local - using `UseFetch(...)` everywhere instead of typed resources - inventing inconsistent cache keys across route and component readers - optimistic updates without a revalidation or ro