('b65a5cf8f117ca6bf10f47fb89ff5be2c7c99a7d', 'docs\FRAMEWORK_SCOPE.md', 'Framework Scope', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'GoWebComponents remains a UI framework, not a first-party app framework.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 19, 91, 'GoWebComponents remains a UI framework, not a first-party app framework.', 'GoWebComponents remains a UI framework, not a first-party app framework.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 19, 91, 'GoWebComponents remains a UI framework, not a first-party app framework.', 'GoWebComponents remains a UI framework, not a first-party app framework.', 0, 0, 'manual-framework_scope-20260330T214856259Z', 'b444d27ef5ea88366d58bc857b866cda59d2960a2cbe73e25fd4faf81df927ef', '010c8ad0acce2d718ba1692eb5e583bed44d35177a1c622bca0775ae72de8947', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('0d985e0d7c46dc0eed3ec0b86feb073c5f74f7a7', 'docs\FRAMEWORK_SCOPE.md', 'Framework Scope', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- Core owns reusable UI/runtime primitives: rendering, hooks, state, fetch, router primitives, SSR or hydration, devtools, and diagnostics. - Core does not aim to become a convention-heavy application platform with file-based routing, deployment adapters, or starter-owned build rules. - Opinionated app shells should live in starters, sibling packages, or documented workflows rather than expanding the core runtime API by default. - Fine-grained reactivity is in scope as a performance direction when it improves narrow hot-path updates without replacing the existing component model. - Server-owned interactive rendering is not part of the current core product direction.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 109, 783, '- Core owns reusable UI/runtime primitives: rendering, hooks, state, fetch, router primitives, SSR or hydration, devtools, and diagnostics. - Core does not aim to become a convention-heavy application platform with file-based routing, deployment adapters, or starter-owned build rules. - Opinionated app shells should live in starters, sibling packages, or documented workflows rather than expanding the core runtime API by default. - Fine-grained reactivity is in scope as a performance direction when it improves narrow hot-path updates without replacing the existing component model. - Server-owned interactive rendering is not part of the current core product direction.', '- Core owns reusable UI/runtime primitives: rendering, hooks, state, fetch, router primitives, SSR or hydration, devtools, and diagnostics. - Core does not aim to become a convention-heavy application platform with file-based routing, deployment adapters, or starter-owned build rules. - Opinionated app shells should live in starters, sibling packages, or documented workflows rather than expanding the core runtime API by default. - Fine-grained reactivity is in scope as a performance direction when it improves narrow hot-path updates without replacing the existing component model. - Server-owned interactive rendering is not part of the current core product direction.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 109, 783, '- Core owns reusable UI/runtime primitives: rendering, hooks, state, fetch, router primitives, SSR or hydration, devtools, and diagnostics. - Core does not aim to become a convention-heavy application platform with file-based routing, deployment adapters, or starter-owned build rules. - Opinionated app shells should live in starters, sibling packages, or documented workflows rather than expanding the core runtime API by default. - Fine-grained reactivity is in scope as a performance direction when it improves narrow hot-path updates without replacing the existing component model. - Server-owned interactive rendering is not part of the current core product direction.', '- Core owns reusable UI/runtime primitives: rendering, hooks, state, fetch, router primitives, SSR or hydration, devtools, and diagnostics. - Core does not aim to become a convention-heavy application platform with file-based routing, deployment adapters, or starter-owned build rules. - Opinionated app shells should live in starters, sibling packages, or documented workflows rather than expanding the core runtime API by default. - Fine-grained reactivity is in scope as a performance direction when it improves narrow hot-path updates without replacing the existing component model. - Server-owned interactive rendering is not part of the current core product direction.', 0, 0, 'manual-framework_scope-20260330T214856259Z', 'b444d27ef5ea88366d58bc857b866cda59d2960a2cbe73e25fd4faf81df927ef', '69eeae12aaf97325930ecc4e802349ece665d88cd58e95a3223daa0c5ffca3c8', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
