('342c4ca9c190fd10c86e0d6ba9eadc6d27cf4873', 'docs\FRAMEWORK_SCOPE.md', 'Framework Scope', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- file-based routing conventions - deployment adapters for specific hosts or platforms - opinionated starter scaffolds and generated project layouts - convention-heavy build pipelines that assume one app shape - server-owned interactive rendering as a normal framework mode', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 4643, 4916, '- file-based routing conventions - deployment adapters for specific hosts or platforms - opinionated starter scaffolds and generated project layouts - convention-heavy build pipelines that assume one app shape - server-owned interactive rendering as a normal framework mode', '- file-based routing conventions - deployment adapters for specific hosts or platforms - opinionated starter scaffolds and generated project layouts - convention-heavy build pipelines that assume one app shape - server-owned interactive rendering as a normal framework mode', 0.9, 'pass', '', 4643, 4916, '- file-based routing conventions - deployment adapters for specific hosts or platforms - opinionated starter scaffolds and generated project layouts - convention-heavy build pipelines that assume one app shape - server-owned interactive rendering as a normal framework mode', '- file-based routing conventions - deployment adapters for specific hosts or platforms - opinionated starter scaffolds and generated project layouts - convention-heavy build pipelines that assume one app shape - server-owned interactive rendering as a normal framework mode', 0, 0, 'manual-framework_scope-20260330T214856259Z', 'b444d27ef5ea88366d58bc857b866cda59d2960a2cbe73e25fd4faf81df927ef', '8e52281bbb7b2aeefeef202b98d9130124e263f31583fb78094d41f6267ee047', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('6c7a7cd32befbbd4cd86f6bb4c48f0ef4e65c24e', 'docs\FRAMEWORK_SCOPE.md', 'Framework Scope', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- Keep the core API focused on reusable UI/runtime primitives. - Add production-app guidance in the onboarding and server-integration docs instead of moving those conventions into the runtime. - Prefer starter variants when a project wants a more opinionated app shell. - Introduce fine-grained primitives only behind explicit APIs, benchmarks, and diagnostics so the narrower update model stays debuggable.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 4937, 5344, '- Keep the core API focused on reusable UI/runtime primitives. - Add production-app guidance in the onboarding and server-integration docs instead of moving those conventions into the runtime. - Prefer starter variants when a project wants a more opinionated app shell. - Introduce fine-grained primitives only behind explicit APIs, benchmarks, and diagnostics so the narrower update model stays debuggable.', '- Keep the core API focused on reusable UI/runtime primitives. - Add production-app guidance in the onboarding and server-integration docs instead of moving those conventions into the runtime. - Prefer starter variants when a project wants a more opinionated app shell. - Introduce fine-grained primitives only behind explicit APIs, benchmarks, and diagnostics so the narrower update model stays debuggable.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 4937, 5344, '- Keep the core API focused on reusable UI/runtime primitives. - Add production-app guidance in the onboarding and server-integration docs instead of moving those conventions into the runtime. - Prefer starter variants when a project wants a more opinionated app shell. - Introduce fine-grained primitives only behind explicit APIs, benchmarks, and diagnostics so the narrower update model stays debuggable.', '- Keep the core API focused on reusable UI/runtime primitives. - Add production-app guidance in the onboarding and server-integration docs instead of moving those conventions into the runtime. - Prefer starter variants when a project wants a more opinionated app shell. - Introduce fine-grained primitives only behind explicit APIs, benchmarks, and diagnostics so the narrower update model stays debuggable.', 0, 0, 'manual-framework_scope-20260330T214856259Z', 'b444d27ef5ea88366d58bc857b866cda59d2960a2cbe73e25fd4faf81df927ef', '60a3548e1f54128c5ab521f205284e19918c45b184e9b80b2ac58e9356e0b838', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('bf1696eb3005349f64c50d87ee840cfc7b312ee8', 'docs\FRAMEWORK_SCOPE.md', 'Framework Scope', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Before moving a new capability into core, verify all of the following:', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 5367, 5437, 'Before moving a new capability into core, verify all of the following:', 'Before moving a new capability into core, verify all of the following:', 0.9, 'pass', '', 5367, 5437, 'Before moving a new capability into core, verify all of the following:', 'Before moving a new capability into core, verify all of the following:', 0, 0, 'manual-framework_scope-20260330T214856259Z', 'b444d27ef5ea88366d58bc857b866cda59d2960a2cbe73e25fd4faf81df927ef', '65726ed69316ad1ad1a30d4fbd05b087661e431084dfc4ab86091b4329e83be2', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
