('2c59e405d01bdd1468506a7c94d337f2b1f726be', 'docs\HYDRATION.md', 'Hydration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Use it when you need to know what the runtime will reuse, when it gives up on reuse, and which hydration behaviors are already implemented versus still open backlog work.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 125, 295, 'Use it when you need to know what the runtime will reuse, when it gives up on reuse, and which hydration behaviors are already implemented versus still open backlog work.', 'Use it when you need to know what the runtime will reuse, when it gives up on reuse, and which hydration behaviors are already implemented versus still open backlog work.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 125, 295, 'Use it when you need to know what the runtime will reuse, when it gives up on reuse, and which hydration behaviors are already implemented versus still open backlog work.', 'Use it when you need to know what the runtime will reuse, when it gives up on reuse, and which hydration behaviors are already implemented versus still open backlog work.', 0, 0, 'manual-hydration-20260330T214856310Z', 'f4aa3cc9fdff8e4443060281483a69ca49fb808b844bbfb00a9d0ddadb0731f0', 'a9059dc2e9f2dda53c599cab1e51f5ac9e7769ca46765b75e9c35fb0effcaf74', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('bf301b43780b7407f6e7a379dc8ca543f3097819', 'docs\HYDRATION.md', 'Hydration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- `ui.Hydrate(...)` is the browser resume path for SSR-rendered DOM. - `ui.HydrationOptions` can load bootstrap inline, from a bootstrap-reference script, or from an explicit `BootstrapRef`, and also controls strict mismatch behavior plus observability. - `router.HydrateMount(...)` uses the same underlying DOM-reuse path while layering router startup and route data reuse on top. - Hydration is reuse-first but not reuse-at-all-costs: structural mismatches fall back per subtree, while text and attribute mismatches warn and let the client commit own the final DOM.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 313, 880, '- `ui.Hydrate(...)` is the browser resume path for SSR-rendered DOM. - `ui.HydrationOptions` can load bootstrap inline, from a bootstrap-reference script, or from an explicit `BootstrapRef`, and also controls strict mismatch behavior plus observability. - `router.HydrateMount(...)` uses the same underlying DOM-reuse path while layering router startup and route data reuse on top. - Hydration is reuse-first but not reuse-at-all-costs: structural mismatches fall back per subtree, while text and attribute mismatches warn and let the client commit own the final DOM.', '- `ui.Hydrate(...)` is the browser resume path for SSR-rendered DOM. - `ui.HydrationOptions` can load bootstrap inline, from a bootstrap-reference script, or from an explicit `BootstrapRef`, and also controls strict mismatch behavior plus observability. - `router.HydrateMount(...)` uses the same underlying DOM-reuse path while layering router startup and route data reuse on top. - Hydration is reuse-first but not reuse-at-all-costs: structural mismatches fall back per subtree, while text and attribute mismatches warn and let the client commit own the final DOM.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 313, 880, '- `ui.Hydrate(...)` is the browser resume path for SSR-rendered DOM. - `ui.HydrationOptions` can load bootstrap in