('0be5601559942b95e736fd44010ffb345bd690d3', 'docs\HYDRATION.md', 'Hydration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'The same public options shape also supports `ScriptID`, `ReferenceScriptID`, and `BootstrapRef` when bootstrap payload discovery should come from the DOM or an external bootstrap reference instead of a pre-read payload.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 1626, 1845, 'The same public options shape also supports `ScriptID`, `ReferenceScriptID`, and `BootstrapRef` when bootstrap payload discovery should come from the DOM or an external bootstrap reference instead of a pre-read payload.', 'The same public options shape also supports `ScriptID`, `ReferenceScriptID`, and `BootstrapRef` when bootstrap payload discovery should come from the DOM or an external bootstrap reference instead of a pre-read payload.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 1626, 1845, 'The same public options shape also supports `ScriptID`, `ReferenceScriptID`, and `BootstrapRef` when bootstrap payload discovery should come from the DOM or an external bootstrap reference instead of a pre-read payload.', 'The same public options shape also supports `ScriptID`, `ReferenceScriptID`, and `BootstrapRef` when bootstrap payload discovery should come from the DOM or an external bootstrap reference instead of a pre-read payload.', 0, 0, 'manual-hydration-20260330T214856310Z', 'f4aa3cc9fdff8e4443060281483a69ca49fb808b844bbfb00a9d0ddadb0731f0', '4e1d85600c7093f4686865e6861a137d5a4b191507cc5545bfeb5a947402f0d1', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('f782331913d06a2064274d87589dc1fa411a3d17', 'docs\HYDRATION.md', 'Hydration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- Hydration is a browser resume path over HTML that already exists in the DOM. - `ui.Hydrate(...)` restores bootstrap data first, then asks the runtime to reuse matching DOM where possible. - `router.HydrateMount(...)` layers router startup on top of that same resume path. - The current implementation targets normal host trees, text nodes, route shells, and supported provider or component descendants.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 1865, 2269, '- Hydration is a browser resume path over HTML that already exists in the DOM. - `ui.Hydrate(...)` restores bootstrap data first, then asks the runtime to reuse matching DOM where possible. - `router.HydrateMount(...)` layers router startup on top of that same resume path. - The current implementation targets normal host trees, text nodes, route shells, and supported provider or component descendants.', '- Hydration is a browser resume path over HTML that already exists in the DOM. - `ui.Hydrate(...)` restores bootstrap data first, then asks the runtime to reuse matching DOM where possible. - `router.HydrateMount(...)` layers router startup on top of that same resume path. - The current implementation targets normal host trees, text nodes, route shells, and supported provider or component descendants.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 1865, 2269, '- Hydration is a browser resume path over HTML that already exists in the DOM. - `ui.Hydrate(...)` restores bootstrap data first, then asks the runtime to reuse matching DOM where possible. - `router.HydrateMount(...)` layers router startup on top of that same resume path. - The current implementation targets normal host trees, text nodes, route shells, and supported provider or component descendants.', '- Hydration is a browser resume path over HTML that already exists in the DOM. - `ui.Hydrate(...)` restores bootstrap data first, then asks the runtime to reuse matching DOM where possible. - `router.HydrateMount(...)` layers router startup on top of that same resume path. - The current implementation targets normal host trees, text nodes, route shells, and supported provider or component descendants.', 0, 0, 'manual-hydration-20260330T214856310Z', 'f4aa3cc9fdff8e4443060281483a69ca49fb808b844bbfb00a9d0ddadb0731f0', '5c4fee8d08014bac725b33567c084ae21acc3cba8e706572ade5420c924740fb', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('b626fbab32491585a18c7d631bcd03a5605601b8', 'docs\HYDRATION.md', 'Hydration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- The runtime starts each hydration pass with a boundary rooted at the target container''s first child. - Each hydrated fiber asks the boundary for the next non-ignorable DOM candidate. - Matching host fibers bind directly to that existing DOM node instead of creating a fresh node. - Matching text fibers bind to the existing text node and stay reusable for later updates. - Provider, fragment, and function-component fibers do not claim DOM nodes themselves. Their descendants continue matching inside the same parent boundary.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 2296, 2824, '- The runtime starts each hydration pass with a boundary rooted at the target container''s first child. - Each hydrated fiber asks the boundary for the next non-ignorable DOM candidate. - Matching host fibers bind directly to that existing DOM node instead of creating a fresh node. - Matching text fibers bind to the existing text node and stay reusable for later updates. - Provider, fragment, and function-component fibers do not claim DOM nodes themselves. Their descendants continue matching inside the same parent boundary.', '- The runtime starts each hydration pass with a boundary rooted at the target container''s first child. - Each hydrated fiber asks the boundary for the next non-ignorable DOM candidate. - Matching host fibers bind directly to that existing DOM node instead of creating a fresh node. - Matching text fibers bind to the existing text node and stay reusable for later updates. - Provider, fragment, and function-component fibers do not claim DOM nodes themselves. Their descendants continue matching inside the same parent boundary.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 2296, 2824, '- The runtime starts each hydration pass with a boundary rooted at the target container''s first child. - Each hydrated fiber asks the boundary for the next non-ignorable DOM candidate. - Matching host fibers bind directly to that existing DOM node instead of creating a fresh node. - Matching text fibers bind to the existing text node and stay reusable for later updates. - Provider, fragment, and function-component fibers do not claim DOM nodes themselves. Their descendants continue matching inside the same parent boundary.', '- The runtime starts each hydration pass with a boundary rooted at the target container''s first child. - Each hydrated fiber asks the boundary for the next non-ignorable DOM candidate. - Matching host fibers bind directly to that existing DOM node instead of creating a fresh node. - Matching text fibers bind to the existing text node and stay reusable for later updates. - Provider, fragment, and function-component fibers do not claim DOM nodes themselves. Their descendants continue matching inside the same parent boundary.', 0, 0, 'manual-hydration-20260330T214856310Z', 'f4aa3cc9fdff8e4443060281483a69ca49fb808b844bbfb00a9d0ddadb0731f0', '9c475059746e2ca5e400a20ef165e74643f6240fffe29ba2de2265b85675e47e', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('b31a4403d897b08a518f0fe4abeee88535980521', 'docs\HYDRATION.md', 'Hydration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'This binding path is implemented in `internal/runtime/hydration.go` through `claimHydrationNode(...)`, `nextHydrationCandidate(...)`, and the per-fiber hydration boundary fields wired during reconciliation.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 2826, 3032, 'This binding path is implemented in `internal/runtime/hydration.go` through `claimHydrationNode(...)`, `nextHydrationCandidate(...)`, and the per-fiber hydration boundary fields wired during reconciliation.', 'This binding path is implemented in `internal/runtime/hydration.go` through `claimHydrationNode(...)`, `nextHydrationCandidate(...)`, and the per-fiber hydration boundary fields wired during reconciliation.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 2826, 3032, 'This binding path is implemented in `internal/runtime/hydration.go` through `claimHydrationNode(...)`, `nextHydrationCandidate(...)`, and the per-fiber hydration boundary fields wired during reconciliation.', 'This binding path is implemented in `internal/runtime/hydration.go` through `claimHydrationNode(...)`, `nextHydrationCandidate(...)`, and the per-fiber hydration boundary fields wired during reconciliation.', 0, 0, 'manual-hydration-20260330T214856310Z', 'f4aa3cc9fdff8e4443060281483a69ca49fb808b844bbfb00a9d0ddadb0731f0', 'feab4cfc8e5e24536dac8f33eea9d242fc7b2232ac3a87439d059789619ce65a', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('71b9ecf5b073796fc49cd1d02da4c2980810ec3e', 'docs\HYDRATION.md', 'Hydration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- Whitespace-only text nodes between siblings are ignored during candidate selection. - Host elements reuse DOM only when the next candidate is an element node with the same tag name. - Text nodes reuse DOM only when the next candidate is a text node. - Fragments do not require a dedicated wrapper node. Their children continue matching against the shared boundary. - Missing candidates, wrong node kinds, or wrong tag names abort reuse for the current subtree boundary. - Extra trailing DOM nodes under an otherwise successful boundary are removed with a warning once matching completes. - Comparable SSR-visible attributes are checked after reuse. Mismatches warn through diagnostics, and the client commit still owns the final DOM state. - Text mismatches also warn through diagnostics, then the reused text node is updated to the client value during commit.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 3053, 3915, '- Whitespace-only text nodes between siblings are ignored during candidate selection. - Host elements reuse DOM only when the next candidate is an element node with the same tag name. - Text nodes reuse DOM only when the next candidate is a text node. - Fragments do not require a dedicated wrapper node. Their children continue matching against the shared boundary. - Missing candidates, wrong node kinds, or wrong tag names abort reuse for the current subtree boundary. - Extra trailing DOM nodes under an otherwise successful boundary are removed with a warning once matching completes. - Comparable SSR-visible attributes are checked after reuse. Mismatches warn through diagnostics, and the client commit still owns the final DOM state. - Text mismatches also warn through diagnostics, then the reused text node is updated to the client value during commit.', '- Whitespace-only text nodes between siblings are ignored during candidate selection. - Host elements reuse DOM only when the next candidate is an element node with the same tag name. - Text nodes reuse DOM only when the next candidate is a text node. - Fragments do not require a dedicated wrapper node. Their children continue matching against the shared boundary. - Missing candidates, wrong node kinds, or wrong tag names abort reuse for the current subtree boundary. - Extra trailing DOM nodes under an otherwise successful boundary are removed with a warning once matching completes. - Comparable SSR-visible attributes are checked after reuse. Mismatches warn through diagnostics, and the client commit still owns the final DOM state. - Text mismatches also warn through diagnostics, then the reused text node is updated to the client value during commit.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 3053, 3915, '- Whitespace-only text nodes between siblings are ignored during candidate selection. - Host elements reuse DOM only when the next candidate is an element node with the same tag name. - Text nodes reuse DOM only when the next candidate is a text node. - Fragments do not require a dedicated wrapper node. Their children continue matching against the shared boundary. - Missing candidates, wrong node kinds, or wrong tag names abort reuse for the current subtree boundary. - Extra trailing DOM nodes under an otherwise successful boundary are removed with a warning once matching completes. - Comparable SSR-visible attributes are checked after reuse. Mismatches warn through diagnostics, and the client commit still owns the final DOM state. - Text mismatches also warn through diagnostics, then the reused text node is updated to the client value during commit.', '- Whitespace-only text nodes between siblings are ignored during candidate selection. - Host elements reuse DOM only when the next candidate is an element node with the same tag name. - Text nodes reuse DOM only when the next candidate is a text node. - Fragments do not require a dedicated wrapper node. Their children continue matching against the shared bo