('c24559498be29ef19aab51aedca176d9e01b8413', 'docs\IDE_INTEGRATION.md', 'IDE And Editor Integration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Use it when deciding how `gwc` tasks, `gopls`-friendly conventions, snippets, diagnostics, route navigation, and editor-facing framework help should fit around the current Go-first workflow.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 130, 320, 'Use it when deciding how `gwc` tasks, `gopls`-friendly conventions, snippets, diagnostics, route navigation, and editor-facing framework help should fit around the current Go-first workflow.', 'Use it when deciding how `gwc` tasks, `gopls`-friendly conventions, snippets, diagnostics, route navigation, and editor-facing framework help should fit around the current Go-first workflow.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 130, 320, 'Use it when deciding how `gwc` tasks, `gopls`-friendly conventions, snippets, diagnostics, route navigation, and editor-facing framework help should fit around the current Go-first workflow.', 'Use it when deciding how `gwc` tasks, `gopls`-friendly conventions, snippets, diagnostics, route navigation, and editor-facing framework help should fit around the current Go-first workflow.', 0, 0, 'manual-ide_integration-20260330T214856319Z', 'ebcd8b462fc087b3831f5849bf1e668fc03f44ce0a5fb8deca11b5e1d5d2766b', 'cb10f8bb172b104811349c46ee0152a67c9140145417884a99d9750dec98e7b2', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('2ca69090a21bc636a4d484e64b6d9830d01fc2d9', 'docs\IDE_INTEGRATION.md', 'IDE And Editor Integration', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- First-party editor support is VS Code-oriented first, because it is the most direct path for tasks, problem matchers, snippets, and workspace guidance around the existing `gwc` launcher. - The repo should still keep the underlying conventions `gopls`-friendly and ordinary-Go-compatible so teams are not forced onto one editor to use the framework correctly. - Broader editor or IDE integrations may come later, but the public DevX story should not imply a richer multi-IDE extension ecosystem than the repo currently ships.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 338, 864, '- First-party editor support is VS Code-oriented first, because it is the most direct path for tasks, problem matchers, snippets, and workspace guidance around the existing `gwc` launcher. - The repo should still keep the underlying conventions `gopls`-friendly and ordinary-Go-compatible so teams are not forced onto one editor to use the framework correctly. - Broader editor or IDE integrations may come later, but the public DevX story should not imply a richer multi-IDE extension ecosystem than the repo currently ships.', '- First-party editor support is VS Code-oriented first, because it is the most direct path for tasks, problem matchers, snippets, and workspace guidance around the existing `gwc` launcher. - The repo should still keep the underlying conventions `gopls`-friendly and ordinary-Go-compatible so teams are not forced onto one editor to use the framework correctly. - Broader editor or IDE integrations may come later, but the public DevX story should not imply a richer multi-IDE extension ecosystem than the repo currently ships.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 338, 864, '- First-party editor support is VS Code-oriented first, because it is the most direct path for tasks, problem matchers, snippets, and workspace guidance around the existing `gwc` launcher. - The repo should still keep the underlying conventions `gopls`-friendly and ordinary-Go-compatible so teams are not forced onto one editor to use the framework correctly. - Broader editor or IDE integrations may come later, but the public DevX story should not imply a richer multi-IDE extension ecosystem than the repo currently ships.', '- First-party editor support is VS Code-oriented first, because it is the most direct path for tasks, problem matchers, snippets, and workspace guidance around the existing `gwc` launcher. - The repo should still keep the underlying conventions `gopls`-friendly and ordinary-Go-compatible so teams are not forced onto one editor to use the framework correctly. - Broader editor or IDE integrations may come later, but the public DevX story should not imply a richer multi-IDE extension ecosystem than the repo currently ships.', 0, 0, 'manual-ide_integration-20260330T214856319Z', 'ebcd8b462fc087b3831f5849bf1e668fc03f44ce0a5fb8deca11b5e1d5d2766b', 'a361846ec1de736fb83f3582904293ca20684faed63a8c97e62ec0ac6de5a7a8', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
