('f6e5b11d034827dee1932eec965fe92531fa5625', 'docs\INTEROP.md', 'Interop Guidance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Use it when an app needs browser APIs, DOM measurement, observers, or dynamic module access without dropping back to raw `syscall/js`.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 101, 235, 'Use it when an app needs browser APIs, DOM measurement, observers, or dynamic module access without dropping back to raw `syscall/js`.', 'Use it when an app needs browser APIs, DOM measurement, observers, or dynamic module access without dropping back to raw `syscall/js`.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 101, 235, 'Use it when an app needs browser APIs, DOM measurement, observers, or dynamic module access without dropping back to raw `syscall/js`.', 'Use it when an app needs browser APIs, DOM measurement, observers, or dynamic module access without dropping back to raw `syscall/js`.', 0, 0, 'manual-interop-20260330T214856330Z', 'f097c7e83dba08cc48b31c40235cb0400f180dc64d6fc0f4ea302c9bc003d029', '7ed437375e9155cd0d2e8b471112d5d8b053b3cf4a3a26058d385ac3759e2737', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('4d26f5967676e919f3f96799747cf6230139cb81', 'docs\INTEROP.md', 'Interop Guidance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- Prefer `interop` over raw `syscall/js` whenever the public package already covers the browser capability you need. - Keep interop ownership local: components or features that create subscriptions, modules, workers, or element handles should also clean them up. - Treat `interop` values as typed boundary objects or JSON-shaped payloads, not as long-lived shared runtime state. - Handle browser unavailability explicitly on SSR or native paths through structured `interop.Error` codes rather than assuming browser globals exist.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 253, 782, '- Prefer `interop` over raw `syscall/js` whenever the public package already covers the browser capability you need. - Keep interop ownership local: components or features that create subscriptions, modules, workers, or element handles should also clean them up. - Treat `interop` values as typed boundary objects or JSON-shaped payloads, not as long-lived shared runtime state. - Handle browser unavailability explicitly on SSR or native paths through structured `interop.Error` codes rather than assuming browser globals exist.', '- Prefer `interop` over raw `syscall/js` whenever the public package already covers the browser capability you need. - Keep interop ownership local: components or features that create subscriptions, modules, workers, or element handles should also clean them up. - Treat `interop` values as typed boundary objects or JSON-shaped payloads, not as long-lived shared runtime state. - Handle browser unavailability explicitly on SSR or native paths through structured `interop.Error` codes rather than assuming browser globals exist.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 253, 782, '- Prefer `interop` over raw `syscall/js` whenever the public package already covers the browser capability you need. - Keep interop ownership local: components or features that create subscriptions, modules, workers, or element handles should also clean them up. - Treat `interop` values as typed boundary objects or JSON-shaped payloads, not as long-lived shared runtime state. - Handle browser unavailability explicitly on SSR or native paths through structured `interop.Error` codes rather than assuming browser globals exist.', '- Prefer `interop` over raw `syscall/js` whenever the public package already covers the browser capability you need. - Keep interop ownership local: components or features that create subscriptions, modules, workers, or element handles should also clean them up. - Treat `interop` values as typed boundary objects or JSON-shaped payloads, not as long-lived shared runtime state. - Handle browser unavailability explicitly on SSR or native paths through structured `interop.Error` codes rather than assuming browser globals exist.', 0, 0, 'manual-interop-20260330T214856330Z', 'f097c7e83dba08cc48b31c40235cb0400f180dc64d6fc0f4ea302c9bc003d029', 'e05748e48ce252458cfb5ab6d23c7ced292e38f9a9deabc01dd7c1566a920482', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
