('f2d6cd7a81cb88dd0178672e4e0f8ef9fd1f73c6', 'docs\LOGGING.md', 'Logging', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Use it when you need one coherent logging model for runtime, router, fetch, hydration, SSR, interop, worker, and form activity instead of ad hoc `fmt.Println(...)` output.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 131, 302, 'Use it when you need one coherent logging model for runtime, router, fetch, hydration, SSR, interop, worker, and form activity instead of ad hoc `fmt.Println(...)` output.', 'Use it when you need one coherent logging model for runtime, router, fetch, hydration, SSR, interop, worker, and form activity instead of ad hoc `fmt.Println(...)` output.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 131, 302, 'Use it when you need one coherent logging model for runtime, router, fetch, hydration, SSR, interop, worker, and form activity instead of ad hoc `fmt.Println(...)` output.', 'Use it when you need one coherent logging model for runtime, router, fetch, hydration, SSR, interop, worker, and form activity instead of ad hoc `fmt.Println(...)` output.', 0, 0, 'manual-logging-20260330T214856345Z', '00f696c07b49101debb9b4580a3ce99ba9dd5a625f4d368a5591884dc80248e0', '5f67457e1178cfb12319b58b3749c1d4fb86cfedb669bbe89c6943b3b055e392', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('fb98f7cf2a6701f03597a2d5a07e4ee9fc5e994d', 'docs\LOGGING.md', 'Logging', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- The public `logging` package already ships a small structured logger built around stable scopes, levels, messages, and field maps. - `logging.New(scope)` is the normal application entrypoint for emitting scoped `debug`, `info`, `warn`, and `error` events. - `logging.AttachBrowserConsole(...)` can wire common browser lifecycle and interaction events into that same structured surface on `js/wasm` builds. - Broader redaction, diagnostics, and observability rules still matter because logs are only one part of the framework feedback model.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 320, 862, '- The public `logging` package already ships a small structured logger built around stable scopes, levels, messages, and field maps. - `logging.New(scope)` is the normal application entrypoint for emitting scoped `debug`, `info`, `warn`, and `error` events. - `logging.AttachBrowserConsole(...)` can wire common browser lifecycle and interaction events into that same structured surface on `js/wasm` builds. - Broader redaction, diagnostics, and observability rules still matter because logs are only one part of the framework feedback model.', '- The public `logging` package already ships a small structured logger built around stable scopes, levels, messages, and field maps. - `logging.New(scope)` is the normal application entrypoint for emitting scoped `debug`, `info`, `warn`, and `error` events. - `logging.AttachBrowserConsole(...)` can wire common browser lifecycle and interaction events into that same structured surface on `js/wasm` builds. - Broader redaction, diagnostics, and observability rules still matter because logs are only one part of the framework feedback model.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 320, 862, '- The public `logging` package already ships a small structured logger built around stable scopes, levels, messages, and field maps. - `logging.New(scope)` is the normal application entrypoint for emitting scoped `debug`, `info`, `warn`, and `error` events. - `logging.AttachBrowserConsole(...)` can wire common browser lifecycle and interaction events into that same structured surface on `js/wasm` builds. - Broader redaction, diagnostics, and observability rules still matter because logs are only one part of the framework feedback model.', '- The public `logging` package already ships a small structured logger built around stable scopes, levels, messages, and field maps. - `logging.New(scope)` is the normal application entrypoint for emitting scoped `debug`, `info`, `warn`, and `error` events. - `logging.AttachBrowserConsole(...)` can wire common browser lifecycle and interaction events into that same structured surface on `js/wasm` builds. - Broader redaction, diagnostics, and observability rules still matter because logs are only one part of the framework feedback model.', 0, 0, 'manual-logging-20260330T214856345Z', '00f696c07b49101debb9b4580a3ce99ba9dd5a625f4d368a5591884dc80248e0', 'abc43595871e0bdf892caec5f2a967b54ba320cf439a45dd86af2b6e60c00aed', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
