('4ae65fb71b0854b6fb7759516aecc8455535bfe1', 'docs\LOGGING.md', 'Logging', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- correctness failures should surface as `error` logs or diagnostics - performance issues should stay warnings unless the runtime cannot safely continue - recovered and unsupported-but-recovered cases should stay warnings with enough context to explain the fallback - informational notices should be suppressible in production-oriented sinks', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 6718, 7059, '- correctness failures should surface as `error` logs or diagnostics - performance issues should stay warnings unless the runtime cannot safely continue - recovered and unsupported-but-recovered cases should stay warnings with enough context to explain the fallback - informational notices should be suppressible in production-oriented sinks', '- correctness failures should surface as `error` logs or diagnostics - performance issues should stay warnings unless the runtime cannot safely continue - recovered and unsupported-but-recovered cases should stay warnings with enough context to explain the fallback - informational notices should be suppressible in production-oriented sinks', 0.9, 'pass', '', 6718, 7059, '- correctness failures should surface as `error` logs or diagnostics - performance issues should stay warnings unless the runtime cannot safely continue - recovered and unsupported-but-recovered cases should stay warnings with enough context to explain the fallback - informational notices should be suppressible in production-oriented sinks', '- correctness failures should surface as `error` logs or diagnostics - performance issues should stay warnings unless the runtime cannot safely continue - recovered and unsupported-but-recovered cases should stay warnings with enough context to explain the fallback - informational notices should be suppressible in production-oriented sinks', 0, 0, 'manual-logging-20260330T214856345Z', '00f696c07b49101debb9b4580a3ce99ba9dd5a625f4d368a5591884dc8