('ed32c717b1acef40764dedde891516269ee7f336', 'docs\OBSERVABILITY.md', 'Observability', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Use it when you need to instrument SSR requests, hydration, routed client activity, or framework lifecycle events without inventing a different event shape for each subsystem.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 102, 277, 'Use it when you need to instrument SSR requests, hydration, routed client activity, or framework lifecycle events without inventing a different event shape for each subsystem.', 'Use it when you need to instrument SSR requests, hydration, routed client activity, or framework lifecycle events without inventing a different event shape for each subsystem.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 102, 277, 'Use it when you need to instrument SSR requests, hydration, routed client activity, or framework lifecycle events without inventing a different event shape for each subsystem.', 'Use it when you need to instrument SSR requests, hydration, routed client activity, or framework lifecycle events without inventing a different event shape for each subsystem.', 0, 0, 'manual-observability-20260330T214856445Z', 'd0121aa40334c2fb39f5a9d230fe0239ac4edd9f2b17bb8c3cdd5f91901c3082', '21288b1dfe5b38852cec1b8d059bb70281a5ea27b05d2850acc67ee8fe6e1c2d', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('36488b7c169188e96241ed1480807258943acfb7', 'docs\OBSERVABILITY.md', 'Observability', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- a real first-class observability slice already ships for SSR render, bootstrap serialization, and hydration - the public entry points are `ui.ObserveSSR(...)`, `ui.RenderToStringObserved(...)`, `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapObserved(...)`, `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapBinaryObserved(...)`, `ui.RenderBootstrapScriptObserved(...)`, and hydration options with `SSRObservabilityOptions` - `devtools` and runtime diagnostics remain the current in-process inspection surface for broader client debugging - broader router, fetch, worker, and long-lived client lifecycle instrumentation is still planned rather than fully emitted today', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 295, 913, '- a real first-class observability slice already ships for SSR render, bootstrap serialization, and hydration - the public entry points are `ui.ObserveSSR(...)`, `ui.RenderToStringObserved(...)`, `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapObserved(...)`, `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapBinaryObserved(...)`, `ui.RenderBootstrapScriptObserved(...)`, and hydration options with `SSRObservabilityOptions` - `devtools` and runtime diagnostics remain the current in-process inspection surface for broader client debugging - broader router, fetch, worker, and long-lived client lifecycle instrumentation is still planned rather than fully emitted today', '- a real first-class observability slice already ships for SSR render, bootstrap serialization, and hydration - the public entry points are `ui.ObserveSSR(...)`, `ui.RenderToStringObserved(...)`, `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapObserved(...)`, `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapBinaryObserved(...)`, `ui.RenderBootstrapScriptObserved(...)`, and hydration options with `SSRObservabilityOptions` - `devtools` and runtime diagnostics remain the current in-process inspection surface for broader client debugging - broader router, fetch, worker, and long-lived client lifecycle instrumentation is still planned rather than fully emitted today', 0.9, 'pass', '', 295, 913, '- a real first-class observability slice already ships for SSR render, bootstrap serialization, and hydration - the public entry points are `ui.ObserveSSR(...)`, `ui.RenderToStringObserved(...)`, `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapObserved(...)`, `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapBinaryObserved(...)`, `ui.RenderBootstrapScriptObserved(...)`, and hydration options with `SSRObservabilityOptions` - `devtools` and runtime diagnostics remain the current in-process inspection surface for broader client debugging - broader router, fetch, worker, and long-lived client lifecycle instrumentation is still planned rather than fully emitted today', '- a real first-class observability slice already ships for SSR render, bootstrap serialization, and hydration - the public entry points are `ui.ObserveSSR(...)`, `ui.RenderToStringObserved(...)`, `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapObserved(...)`, `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapBinaryObserved(...)`, `ui.RenderBootstrapScriptObserved(...)`, and hydration options with `SSRObservabilityOptions` - `devtools` and runtime diagnostics remain the current in-process inspection surface for broader client debugging - broader router, fetch, worker, and long-lived client lifecycle instrumentation is still planned rather than fully emitted today', 0, 0, 'manual-observability-20260330T214856445Z', 'd0121aa40334c2fb39f5a9d230fe0239ac4edd9f2b17bb8c3cdd5f91901c3082', '1f974a12ad81d8dd535c3efeb9c68e9b3448350bbf194c3b5e4b236c615dd821', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('9f7470247896e93e460530d9c2a4c82adda747cd', 'docs\OBSERVABILITY.md', 'Observability', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- use `ui.RenderToStringObserved(...)` when an SSR render should emit one structured render observation - use `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapObserved(...)`, `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapBinaryObserved(...)`, or `ui.RenderBootstrapScriptObserved(...)` when bootstrap payload size needs to be measured alongside render work - use `ui.ObserveSSR(...)` when the application wants a shared subscription for SSR and hydration observations - use `ui.Hydrate(...)` or `ui.HydrateInto(...)` with `HydrationOptions{Observability: ...}` when correlation ids and hydration metrics should flow into the same event stream - use `devtools.SnapshotNow()` or `devtools.UseSnapshot(...)` when the goal is interactive inspection of diagnostics, cache state, logs, or multi-client state rather than SSR event collection', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 937, 1722, '- use `ui.RenderToStringObserved(...)` when an SSR render should emit one structured render observation - use `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapObserved(...)`, `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapBinaryObserved(...)`, or `ui.RenderBootstrapScriptObserved(...)` when bootstrap payload size needs to be measured alongside render work - use `ui.ObserveSSR(...)` when the application wants a shared subscription for SSR and hydration observations - use `ui.Hydrate(...)` or `ui.HydrateInto(...)` with `HydrationOptions{Observability: ...}` when correlation ids and hydration metrics should flow into the same event stream - use `devtools.SnapshotNow()` or `devtools.UseSnapshot(...)` when the goal is interactive inspection of diagnostics, cache state, logs, or multi-client state rather than SSR event collection', '- use `ui.RenderToStringObserved(...)` when an SSR render should emit one structured render observation - use `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapObserved(...)`, `ui.MarshalSSRBootstrapBinaryObserved(...)`, or `ui.RenderBootstrapScriptObserved(...)` when bootstrap payload size ne