('00e8986ceba5e1e7a9ad3644ce77b536397ed255', 'docs\ONBOARDING.md', 'Onboarding and Bootstrap', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '1. scaffold or bootstrap the app with `go run ./tools/gwc bootstrap` or `go run ./tools/gwc start` 2. run `go run ./tools/gwc dev -app .\main.go` from the app workspace 3. use `gwc build`, `gwc test`, and `gwc verify` against the app root instead of copying monorepo-only example commands 4. treat the generated app as user-owned code that upgrades through package releases and documented migrations, not by diffing random repo internals', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 8683, 9120, '1. scaffold or bootstrap the app with `go run ./tools/gwc bootstrap` or `go run ./tools/gwc start` 2. run `go run ./tools/gwc dev -app .\main.go` from the app workspace 3. use `gwc build`, `gwc test`, and `gwc verify` against the app root instead of copying monorepo-only example commands 4. treat the generated app as user-owned code that upgrades through package releases and documented migrations, not by diffing random repo internals', '1. scaffold or bootstrap the app with `go run ./tools/gwc bootstrap` or `go run ./tools/gwc start` 2. run `go run ./tools/gwc dev -app .\main.go` from the app workspace 3. use `gwc build`, `gwc test`, and `gwc verify` against the app root instead of copying monorepo-only example commands 4. treat the generated app as user-owned code that upgrades through package releases and documented migrations, not by diffing random repo internals', 0.9, 'pass', '', 8683, 9120, '1. scaffold or bootstrap the app with `go run ./tools/gwc bootstrap` or `go run ./tools/gwc start` 2. run `go run ./tools/gwc dev -app .\main.go` from the app workspace 3. use `gwc build`, `gwc test`, and `gwc verify` against the app root instead of copying monorepo-only example commands 4. treat the generated app as user-owned code that upgrades through package releases and documented migrations, not by diffing random repo internals', '1. scaffold or bootstrap the app with `go r