('da222729d7c08a45c492812b5035ee28fa8ee97e', 'docs\PWA.md', 'PWA and Offline App Support', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- The `pwa` package already ships a real companion surface for manifests, installability observation, explicit service-worker registration, release-manifest-driven asset planning, Cache Storage coordination, and structured PWA diagnostics. - PWA support in this repo is integration-oriented: the framework provides explicit helpers, but applications still own service-worker code, route fallback policy, retention policy, and deployment rollout. - Durable offline writes are first-class through `fetch.OpenMutationQueue(...)`, while broader PWA state can be inspected through `pwa.InspectDiagnostics(...)`. - Use [OFFLINE_MUTATIONS.md](OFFLINE_MUTATIONS.md) for replay semantics, [ASSETS.md](ASSETS.md) for cache and manifest alignment, and [BROWSER_SUPPORT.md](BROWSER_SUPPORT.md) for capability-gated behavior.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 360, 1172, '- The `pwa` package already ships a real companion surface for manifests, installability observation, explicit service-worker registration, release-manifest-driven asset planning, Cache Storage coordination, and structured PWA diagnostics. - PWA support in this repo is integration-oriented: the framework provides explicit helpers, but applications still own service-worker code, route fallback policy, retention policy, and deployment rollout. - Durable offline writes are first-class through `fetch.OpenMutationQueue(...)`, while broader PWA state can be inspected through `pwa.InspectDiagnostics(...)`. - Use [OFFLINE_MUTATIONS.md](OFFLINE_MUTATIONS.md) for replay semantics, [ASSETS.md](ASSETS.md) for cache and manifest alignment, and [BROWSER_SUPPORT.md](BROWSER_SUPPORT.md) for capability-gated behavior.', '- The `pwa` package already ships a real companion surface for manifests, installability observation, explicit service-worker registration, release-manifest-driven asset planning, Cache Storage coordination, a