('c570c65c8e524e68295c204161475b1c29a41f04', 'docs\PWA.md', 'PWA and Offline App Support', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- routes that can render safely from a cached shell plus durable client data may open offline through an application-owned fallback document or shell route - routes that require authoritative online data for correctness should fail closed with an explicit offline-unavailable experience instead of rendering misleading stale content - deep links should resolve through the same router ownership model as online opens; the service worker may provide a shell or fallback document, but route policy still belongs to the application - fallback documents should preserve enough bootstrap or route context to show a useful offline state, retry action, and navigation back to known-openable surfaces - applications should distinguish “offline-openable with stale data” from “offline-openable empty shell” and from “online required” rather than treating every route as one generic offline case', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 11337, 12234, '- routes that can render safely from a cached shell plus durable client data may open offline through an application-owned fallback document or shell route - routes that require authoritative online data for correctness should fail closed with an explicit offline-unavailable experience instead of rendering misleading stale content - deep links should resolve through the same router ownership model as online opens; the service worker may provide a shell or fallback document, but route policy still belongs to the application - fallback documents should preserve enough bootstrap or route context to show a useful offline state, retry action, and navigation back to known-openable surfaces - applications should distinguish “offline-openable with stale data” from “offline-openable empty shell” and from “online required” rather than treating every route as one generic offline case', '- routes that can render safely from a cached shell plus durable client data may open offline through an application-owned fallback document or shell route - routes that require authoritative online data for correctness should fail closed with an explicit offline-unavailable experience instead of rendering misleading stale content - deep links should resolve through the same router ownership model as online opens; the service worker may provide a shell or fallback document, but route policy still belongs to the application - fallback documents should preserve enough bootstrap or route context to show a useful offline state, retry action, and navigation back to known-openable surfaces - applications should distinguish “offline-openable with stale data” from “offline-openable empty shell” and from “online required” rather than treating every route as one generic offline case', 0.9, 'pass', '', 11337, 12234, '- routes that can render safely from a cached shell plus durable client data may open offline through an application-owned fallback document or shell route - routes that require authoritative online data for correctness should fail closed with an explicit offline-unavailable experience instead of rendering misleading stale content - deep links should resolve through the same router ownership model as online opens; the service worker may provide a shell or fallback document, but route policy still belongs to the application - fallback documents should preserve enough bootstrap or route context to show a useful offline state, retry action, and navigation back to known-openable surfaces - applications should distinguish “offline-openable with stale data” from “offline-openable empty shell” and from “online required” rather than treating every route as one generic offline case', '- routes that can render safely from a cached shell plus durable client data may open offline through an application-owned fallback document or shell route - routes that require authoritative online data for correctness should fail closed with an explicit offline-unavailable experience instead of rendering misleading stale content - deep links should resolve through the same router ownership model as online opens; the service worker may provide a shell or fallback document, but route policy still belongs to the application - fallback documents should preserve enough bootstrap or route context to show a useful offline state, retry action, and navigation back to known-openable surfaces - applications should distinguish “offline-openable with stale data” from “offline-openable empty shell” and from “online required” rather than treating every route as one generic offline case', 0, 0, 'manual-pwa-20260330T214856535Z', 'ccc970ee7d17b69d151e188b2a8639fed48782e05b623f5c4789510f217dd3f1', '22afec95e3ffbe94729164c5f93e67815cf62df7eae01941edde2e933a0abde7', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('4e22fd51ed7d9d77e0089c27d8f72995906aac9d', 'docs\PWA.md', 'PWA and Offline App Support', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- shell-capable routes: marketing pages, settings shells, draft-centric workflows, and other surfaces that can recover from cached shell plus later revalidation - partial offline routes: routes that may open the shell and local state but must mark some panels or actions unavailable until the network returns - online-required routes: privileged or correctness-sensitive flows where stale or partial rendering would be misleading or unsafe', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 12256, 12695, '- shell-capable routes: marketing pages, settings shells, draft-centric workflows, and other surfaces that can recover from cached shell plus later revalidation - partial offline routes: routes that may open the shell and local state but must mark some panels or actions unavailable until the network returns - online-required routes: privileged or correctness-sensitive flows where stale or partial rendering would be misleading or unsafe', '- shell-capable routes: marketing pages, settings shells, draft-centric workflows, and other surfaces that can recover from cached shell plus later revalidation - partial offline routes: routes that may open the shell and local state but must mark some panels or actions unavailable until the network returns - online-required routes: privileged or correctness-sensitive flows where stale or partial rendering would be misleading or unsafe', 0.9, 'pass', '', 12256, 12695, '- shell-capable routes: marketing pages, settings shells, draft-centric workflows, and other surfaces that can recover from cached shell plus later revalidation - partial offline routes: routes that may open the shell and local state but must mark some panels or actions unavailable until the network returns - online-required routes: privileged or correctness-sensitive flows where stale or partial rendering would be misleading or unsafe', '- shell-capable routes: marketing p