('0fb7f183cbac37d5b28393a347156bd9f6301696', 'docs\PWA.md', 'PWA and Offline App Support', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- use one logical cross-tab topic for offline replay ownership and one for cache invalidation or replay results when an application opens multiple tabs for the same surface - elect one active replay owner at a time; other tabs may observe queue state and results, but should not stampede the same queued writes concurrently - treat logout, session expiry, and trust-boundary narrowing as immediately authoritative across tabs; apply those messages before any further replay or cache reuse - broadcast cache invalidation and replay outcomes after authoritative success so sibling tabs can refresh or dispose their own local state deliberately - when tabs disagree about freshness, prefer the narrowest safe action such as invalidation or reload over optimistic cross-tab replacement of richer local state', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 15487, 16290, '- use one logical cross-tab topic for offline replay ownership and one for cache invalidation or replay results when an application opens multiple tabs for the same surface - elect one active replay owner at a time; other tabs may observe queue state and results, but should not stampede the same queued writes concurrently - treat logout, session expiry, and trust-boundary narrowing as immediately authoritative across tabs; apply those messages before any further replay or cache reuse - broadcast cache invalidation and replay outcomes after authoritative success so sibling tabs can refresh or dispose their own local state deliberately - when tabs disagree about freshness, prefer the narrowest safe action such as invalidation or reload over optimistic cross-tab replacement of richer local state', '- use one logical cross-tab topic for offline replay ownership and one for cache invalidation or replay results when an application opens multiple tabs for the same surface - elect one active replay owner at a time; other tabs may observe queue state and results, but should not stampede the same queued writes concurrently - treat logout, session expiry, and trust-boundary narrowing as immediately authoritative across tabs; apply those messages before any further replay or cache reuse - broadcast cache invalidation and replay outcomes after authoritative success so sibling tabs can refresh or dispose their own local state deliberately - when tabs disagree about freshness, prefer the narrowest safe action such as invalidation or reload over optimistic cross-tab replacement of richer local state', 0.9, 'pass', '', 15487, 16290, '- use one logical cross-tab topic for offline replay ownership and one for cache invalidation or replay results when an application opens multiple tabs for the same surface - elect one active replay owner at a time; other tabs may observe queue state and results, but should not stampede the same queued writes concurrently - treat logout, session expiry, and trust-boundary narrowing as immediately authoritative across tabs; apply those messages before any further replay or cache reuse - broadcast cache invalidation and replay outcomes after authoritative success so sibling tabs can refresh or dispose their own local state deliberately - when tabs disagree about freshness, prefer the narrowest safe action such as invalidation or reload over optimistic cross-tab replacement of richer local state', '- use one logical cross-tab topic for offline replay ownership and one for cache invalidation or replay results when an application opens multiple tabs for the same surface - elect one active replay owner at a time; other tabs may observe queue state and results, but should not stampede the same queued writes concurrently - treat logout, session expiry, and trust-boundary narrowing as immediately authoritative across tabs; apply those messages before any further replay or cache reuse - broadcast cache invalidation and replay outcomes after authoritative success so sibling 