('9bace6ab23acced1a1942ddc6aba989201e14c5c', 'docs\ROUTER_AUTH.md', 'Router Async Guards And Auth Design', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Protected-route loaders should not start before an auth gate allows the navigation. Public shell loaders may still run earlier only when explicitly attached to an already-allowed parent layout.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 9809, 10002, 'Protected-route loaders should not start before an auth gate allows the navigation. Public shell loaders may still run earlier only when explicitly attached to an already-allowed parent layout.', 'Protected-route loaders should not start before an auth gate allows the navigation. Public shell loaders may still run earlier only when explicitly attached to an already-allowed parent layout.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 9809, 10002, 'Protected-route loaders should not start before an auth gate allows the navigation. Public shell loaders may still run earlier only when explicitly attached to an already-allowed parent layout.', 'Protected-route loaders should not start before an auth gate allows the navigation. Public shell loaders may still run earlier only when explicitly attached to an already-allowed parent layout.', 0, 0, 'manual-router_auth-20260330T214856567Z', 'db9a6446af37a0d655bbd1ab499a0467bca4e3536feb6d46ede124db7871d585', 'f45c0f9d50b6afa34bc8fe3f643fb0605ca9426fd95021407b0208675beb108c', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('c0054747caff453a9de7f7f1d6eeedfcfd59e946', 'docs\ROUTER_AUTH.md', 'Router Async Guards And Auth Design', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Silent token or session refresh should not look like a brand-new navigation when the active authenticated principal and route entitlement remain the same.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10052, 10206, 'Silent token or session refresh should not look like a brand-new navigation when the active authenticated principal and route entitlement remain the same.', 'Silent token or session refresh should not look like a brand-new navigation when the active authenticated principal and route entitlement remain the same.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 10052, 10206, 'Silent token or session refresh should not look like a brand-new navigation when the active authenticated principal and route entitlement remain the same.', 'Silent token or session refresh should not look like a brand-new navigation when the active authenticated principal and route entitlement remain the same.', 0, 0, 'manual-router_auth-20260330T214856567Z', 'db9a6446af37a0d655bbd1ab499a0467bca4e3536feb6d46ede124db7871d585', '96278148ef37eef804922bef54ad957f9b17bcfca3332aa18f55ebcbf2863d1c', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('c8769451e7506fc21df4affd34bfb1e7b8d87fe2', 'docs\ROUTER_AUTH.md', 'Router Async Guards And Auth Design', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- do not re-fire active route guards purely because a background refresh renewed the current session for the same user and tenant boundary - do not cold-reload already allowed protected-route loaders unless the refresh changed data-shaping auth inputs such as principal, tenant, or claims that the route actually depends on - update auth-derived atoms and session hints in one coordinated transition so the route tree does not briefly flash unauthorized UI and then recover a moment later - while refresh is still unresolved, prefer an explicit pending or authorizing state over eagerly downgrading the current protected route - if refresh proves the principal or tenant changed, treat that as a real auth boundary change: cancel protected loaders, clear stale route-owned data, and re-run the guard path intentionally', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10228, 11062, '- do not re-fire active route guards purely because a background refresh renewed the current session for the same user and tenant boundary - do not cold-reload already allowed protected-route loaders unless the refresh changed data-shaping auth inputs such as principal, tenant, or claims that the route actually depends on - update auth-derived atoms and session hints in one coordinated transition so the route tree does not briefly flash unauthorized UI and then recover a moment later - while refresh is still unresolved, prefer an explicit pending or authorizing state over eagerly downgrading the current protected route - if refresh proves the principal or tenant changed, treat that as a real auth boundary change: cancel protected loaders, clear stale route-owned data, and re-run the guard path intentionally', '- do not re-fire active route guards purely because a background refresh renewed the current session for the same user and tenant boundary - do not cold-reload already allowed protected-route loaders unless the refresh changed data-shaping auth inputs such as principal, tenant, or claims that the route actually depends on - update auth-derived atoms and session hints in one coordinated transition so the route tree does not briefly flash unauthorized UI and then recover a moment later - while refresh is still unresolved, prefer an explicit pending or authorizing state over eagerly downgrading the current protected route - if refresh proves the principal or tenant changed, treat that as a real auth boundary change: cancel protected loaders, clear stale route-owned data, and re-run the guard path intentionally', 0.9, 'pass', '', 10228, 11062, '- do not re-fire active route guards purely because a background refresh renewed the current session for the same user and tenant boundary - do not cold-reload already allowed protected-route loaders unless the refresh changed data-shaping auth inputs such as principal, tenant, or claims that the route actually depends on - update auth-derived atoms and session hints in one coordinated transition so the route tree does not briefly flash unauthorized UI and then recover a moment later - while refresh is still unresolved, prefer an explicit pending or authorizing state over eagerly downgrading the current protected route - if refresh proves the principal or tenant changed, treat that as a real auth boundary change: cancel protected loaders, clear stale route-owned data, and re-run the guard path intentionally', '- do not re-fire active route guards purely because a background refresh renewed the current session for the same user and tenant boundary - do not cold-reload already allowed protected-route loaders unless the refresh changed data-shaping auth inputs such as principal, tenant, or claims that the route actually depends on - update auth-derived atoms and session hints in one coordinated transition so the route tree does not briefly flash unauthorized UI and then recover a moment later - while refresh is still unresolved, prefer an explicit pending or authorizing state over eagerly downgrading the current protected route - if refresh proves the principal or tenant changed, treat that as a real auth boundary change: cancel protected loaders, clear stale route-owned data, and re-run the guard path intentionally', 0, 0, 'manual-router_auth-20260330T214856567Z', 'db9a6446af37a0d655bbd1ab499a0467bca4e3536feb6d46ede124db7871d585', '53152f048fc8970a6d7ce9284434062a42e32b7e4e1c8a28398ade5fefa64d64', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
