('d7094ab7adc975a9ecd76de86ab362a91de7f1c7', 'docs\RPC_TRANSPORT.md', 'Typed RPC and Streaming Transport', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- Typed browser RPC is not part of the core rendering contract. - It should not expand the base `interop` package into a framework-owned RPC stack by default. - If the repo ships a first-party browser RPC client, it should live in a dedicated companion package layered on documented public APIs. - The first transport package should start as `Experimental`, not as stable core or an automatic app default.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 203, 608, '- Typed browser RPC is not part of the core rendering contract. - It should not expand the base `interop` package into a framework-owned RPC stack by default. - If the repo ships a first-party browser RPC client, it should live in a dedicated companion package layered on documented public APIs. - The first transport package should start as `Experimental`, not as stable core or an automatic app default.', '- Typed browser RPC is not part of the core rendering contract. - It should not expand the base `interop` package into a framework-owned RPC stack by default. - If the repo ships a first-party browser RPC client, it should live in a dedicated companion package layered on documented public APIs. - The first transport package should start as `Experimental`, not as stable core or an automatic app default.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 203, 608, '- Typed browser RPC is not part of the core rendering contract. - It should not expand the base `interop` package into a framework-owned RPC stack by default. - If the repo ships a first-party browser RPC client, it should live in a dedicated companion package layered on documented public APIs. - The first transport package should start as `Experimental`, not as stable core or an automatic app default.', '- Typed browser RPC is not part of the core rendering contract. - It should not expand the base `interop` package into a framework-owned RPC stack by default. - If