('cedc37a0ec6386fe05854ebbe3fba6946a494fa7', 'docs\RPC_TRANSPORT.md', 'Typed RPC and Streaming Transport', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'The safe default is to surface only coarse auth state in tooling, such as "connected", "unauthenticated", or "permission denied", plus non-secret tenant or correlation identifiers when the application already treats them as safe to expose.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 15520, 15759, 'The safe default is to surface only coarse auth state in tooling, such as "connected", "unauthenticated", or "permission denied", plus non-secret tenant or correlation identifiers when the application already treats them as safe to expose.', 'The safe default is to surface only coarse auth state in tooling, such as "connected", "unauthenticated", or "permission denied", plus non-secret tenant or correlation identifiers when the application already treats them as safe to expose.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 15520, 15759, 'The safe default is to surface only coarse auth state in tooling, such as "connected", "unauthenticated", or "permission denied", plus non-secret tenant or correlation identifiers when the application already treats them as safe to expose.', 'The safe default is to surface only coarse auth state in tooling, such as "connected", "unauthenticated", or "permission denied", plus non-secret tenant or correlation identifiers when the application already treats them as safe to expose.', 0, 0, 'manual-rpc_transport-20260330T214856580Z', 'b64ddfb9b1d91f2cb743b98c390738ad442c4a48c9b799b1b62e5c217b79108b', 'abe8cf956f5fde395fef1331bf2834392feb84dce41323eb5fd93b3a80fc26cd', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('c3652accc1ffb939ec90a84faeef15df3269bb38', 'docs\RPC_TRANSPORT.md', 'Typed RPC and Streaming Transport', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'The first RPC companion should be context-driven, like the rest of the repo''s long-running async work.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 15806, 15908, 'The first RPC companion should be context-driven, like the rest of the repo''s long-running async work.', 'The first RPC companion should be context-driven, like the rest of the repo''s long-running async work.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 15806, 15908, 'The first RPC companion should be context-driven, like the rest of the repo''s long-running async work.', 'The first RPC companion should be context-driven, like the rest of the repo''s long-running async work.', 0, 0, 'manual-rpc_transport-20260330T214856580Z', 'b64ddfb9b1d91f2cb743b98c390738ad442c4a48c9b799b1b62e5c217b79108b', '598280bbaf0ebea328ac5509d3c7f15f4536142a36e7611b2b82f6186aadfc6c', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('24acf6d7e09862b469d26b2d3df47966cb2e5de6', 'docs\RPC_TRANSPORT.md', 'Typed RPC and Streaming Transport', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- every unary call and stream should start with a caller-owned `context.Context` - `context.WithCancel(...)` cancels local waiting immediately and sends a best-effort stream cancel or half-close frame when the socket is still available - `context.WithTimeout(...)` or deadline contexts should propagate an explicit deadline into transport metadata and fail locally with a typed timeout when the deadline expires - if the transport is already closed, local cancellation still wins and should not wait on remote acknowledgement', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 15930, 16455, '- every unary call and stream should start with a caller-owned `context.Context` - `context.WithCancel(...)` cancels local waiting immediately and sends a best-effort stream cancel or half-close frame when the socket is still available - `context.WithTimeout(...)` or deadline contexts should propagate an explicit deadline into transport metadata and fail locally with a typed timeout when the deadline expires - if the transport is already closed, local cancellation still wins and should not wait on remote acknowledgement', '- every unary call and stream should start with a caller-owned `context.Context` - `context.WithCancel(...)` cancels local waiting immediately and sends a best-effort stream cancel or half-close frame when the socket is still available - `context.WithTimeout(...)` or deadline contexts should propagate an explicit deadline into transport metadata and fail locally with a typed timeout when the deadline expires - if the transport is already closed, local cancellation still wins and should not wait on remote acknowledgement', 0.9, 'pass', '', 15930, 16455, '- every unary call and stream should start with a caller-owned `context.Context` - `context.WithCancel(...)` cancels local waiting immediately and sends a best-effort stream cancel or half-close frame when the socket is still available - `context.WithTimeout(...)` or deadline contexts should propagate an explicit deadline into transport metadata and fail locally with a typed timeout when the deadline expires - if the transport is already closed, local cancellation still wins and should not wait on remote acknowledgement', '- every unary call and stream should start with a caller-owned `context.Context` - `context.WithCancel(...)` cancels local waiting immediately and sends a best-effort stream cancel or half-close frame when the socket is still available - `context.WithTimeout(...)` or deadline contexts should propagate an explicit deadline into transport metadata and fail locally with a typed timeout when the deadline expires - if the transport is already closed, local cancellation still wins and should not wait on remote acknowledgement', 0, 0, 'manual-rpc_transport-20260330T214856580Z', 'b64ddfb9b1d91f2cb743b98c390738ad442c4a48c9b799b1b62e5c217b79108b', 'f7070d15b677c0ffebb961cf4d93c86815958ead979554bbe7ceffc41122b271', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('a66462c2957e41849aa58bd0263d28f63a4de81d', 'docs\RPC_TRANSPORT.md', 'Typed RPC and Streaming Transport', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Late traffic should be ignored after the owner stops listening.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 16457, 16520, 'Late traffic should be ignored after the owner stops listening.', 'Late traffic should be ignored after the owner stops listening.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 16457, 16520, 'Late traffic should be ignored after the owner stops listening.', 'Late traffic should be ignored after the owner stops listening.', 0, 0, 'manual-rpc_transport-20260330T214856580Z', 'b64ddfb9b1d91f2cb743b98c390738ad442c4a48c9b799b1b62e5c217b79108b', 'b955d285fe3bf6d0ca13715b16a788de3ea62f7f16ef36a136d4f48f1ad973a1', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('2414984d9099c9555887f6e139a5661054081eca', 'docs\RPC_TRANSPORT.md', 'Typed RPC and Streaming Transport', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- once a unary call resolves, times out, or is cancelled, later response frames for that call id are dropped - once a server-stream consumer unsubscribes or the owning route unmounts, later stream frames are ignored and counted only as diagnostics noise - client-streaming and bidirectional calls should reject further sends after local cancellation, local timeout, or terminal completion', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 16535, 16923, '- once a unary call resolves, times out, or is cancelled, later response frames for that call id are dropped - once a server-stream consumer unsubscribes or the owning route unmounts, later stream frames are ignored and counted only as diagnostics noise - client-streaming and bidirectional calls should reject further sends after local cancellation, local timeout, or terminal completion', '- once a unary call resolves, times out, or is cancelled, later response frames for that call id are dropped - once a server-stream consumer unsubscribes or the owning route unmounts, later stream frames are ignored and counted only as diagnostics noise - client-streaming and bidirectional calls should reject further sends after local cancellation, local timeout, or terminal completion', 0.9, 'pass', '', 16535, 16923, '- once a unary call resolves, times out, or is cancelled, later response frames for that call id are dropped - once a server-stream consumer unsubscribes or the owning route unmounts, later stream frames are ignored and counted only as diagnostics noise - client-streaming and bidirectional calls should reject further sends after local cancellation, local timeout, or terminal completion', '- once a unary call resolves, times out, or is cancelled, later response frames for that call id are dropped - once a server-stream consumer unsubscribes or the owning route unmounts, later stream frames are ignored and counted only as diagnostics noise - client-streaming and bidirectional calls should reject further sends after local cancellation, local timeout, or terminal completion', 0, 0, 'manual-rpc_transport-20260330T214856580Z', 'b64ddfb9b1d91f2cb743b98c390738ad442c4a48c9b799b1b62e5c217b79108b', 'abfe1c89ac8c32dbd6313f85abdcd177fc4c8fc49602ca9ed471de809dd6759c', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
