('0c2ce64ac5d85364a87a99b0fbdb08e1be7b72a3', 'docs\SECURITY.md', 'Security, Compliance, and Governance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- treat both inline bootstrap and sidecar bootstrap as public data channels, not as secret transport - keep CSP, nonce, and inline-script policy explicit in the server document template or HTTP layer - keep route loaders and SSR handlers responsible for narrowing upstream data before rendering or bootstrapping it - keep user-generated HTML behind application-owned sanitization policy - treat hydration mismatch recovery as a correctness concern, not a security boundary', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 5025, 5497, '- treat both inline bootstrap and sidecar bootstrap as public data channels, not as secret transport - keep CSP, nonce, and inline-script policy explicit in the server document template or HTTP layer - keep route loaders and SSR handlers responsible for narrowing upstream data before rendering or bootstrapping it - keep user-generated HTML behind application-owned sanitization policy - treat hydration mismatch recovery as a correctness concern, not a security boundary', '- treat both inline bootstrap and sidecar bootstrap as public data channels, not as secret transport - keep CSP, nonce, and inline-script policy explicit in the server document template or HTTP layer - keep route loaders and SSR handlers responsible for narrowing upstream data before rendering or bootstrapping it - keep user-generated HTML behind application-owned sanitization policy - treat hydration mismatch recovery as a correctness concern, not a security boundary', 0.9, 'pass', '', 5025, 5497, '- treat both inline bootstrap and sidecar bootstrap as public data channels, not as secret transport - keep CSP, nonce, and inline-script policy explicit in the server document template or HTTP layer - keep route loaders and SSR handlers responsible for narrowing upstream data before rendering or bootstrapping it - keep user-generated HTML behind application-owned sa