('65a03dbdcef568c6cf450496f5f03533b61832f3', 'docs\SECURITY.md', 'Security, Compliance, and Governance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- `ui.NewCSRFToken(...)` normalizes the default header and hidden-field names - `ui.DefaultCSRFHeaderName` and `ui.DefaultCSRFFormFieldName` make transport naming consistent across server-rendered forms and imperative requests - `ui.UseForm(...)` can apply server-shaped errors and preserve CSRF token conventions, but it does not validate tokens itself', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 5644, 5997, '- `ui.NewCSRFToken(...)` normalizes the default header and hidden-field names - `ui.DefaultCSRFHeaderName` and `ui.DefaultCSRFFormFieldName` make transport naming consistent across server-rendered forms and imperative requests - `ui.UseForm(...)` can apply server-shaped errors and preserve CSRF token conventions, but it does not validate tokens itself', '- `ui.NewCSRFToken(...)` normalizes the default header and hidden-field names - `ui.DefaultCSRFHeaderName` and `ui.DefaultCSRFFormFieldName` make transport naming consistent across server-rendered forms and imperative requests - `ui.UseForm(...)` can apply server-shaped errors and preserve CSRF token conventions, but it does not validate tokens itself', 0.9, 'pass', '', 5644, 5997, '- `ui.NewCSRFToken(...)` normalizes the default header and hidden-field names - `ui.DefaultCSRFHeaderName` and `ui.DefaultCSRFFormFieldName` make transport naming consistent across server-rendered forms and imperative requests - `ui.UseForm(...)` can apply server-shaped errors and preserve CSRF token conventions, but it does not validate tokens itself', '- `ui.NewCSRFToken(...)` normalizes the default header and hidden-field names - `ui.DefaultCSRFHeaderName` and `ui.DefaultCSRFFormFieldName` make transport naming consistent across server-rendered forms and imperative requests - `ui.UseForm(...)` can apply server-shaped errors and preserve CSRF token conventions, but it does not validate tokens itself', 0, 0, 'manual