('564ab43e94fc6cbf549dbf8c9c91a6011b918f04', 'docs\SECURITY.md', 'Security, Compliance, and Governance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- keep build and release pipelines reproducible enough to explain how shipped wasm, JavaScript, HTML, and manifest artifacts were produced - separate development, staging, and production environments so they do not share secrets or logging sinks accidentally - align audit logging with the application''s own auth, mutation, and administrative boundaries instead of assuming framework lifecycle logs are sufficient evidence - review CDN, reverse-proxy, browser-cache, and browser-storage behavior so public caches and local persistence do not outlive intended policy windows - apply explicit retention and deletion policy to browser-visible logs, bootstrap payloads, stored drafts, caches, and exported snapshots when the domain requires it', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10666, 11405, '- keep build and release pipelines reproducible enough to explain how shipped wasm, JavaScript, HTML, and manifest artifacts were produced - separate development, staging, and production environments so they do not share secrets or logging sinks accidentally - align audit logging with the application''s own auth, mutation, and administrative boundaries instead of assuming framework lifecycle logs are sufficient evidence - review CDN, reverse-proxy, browser-cache, and browser-storage behavior so public caches and local persistence do not outlive intended policy windows - apply explicit retention and deletion policy to browser-visible logs, bootstrap payloads, stored drafts, caches, and exported snapshots when the domain requires it', '- keep build and release pipelines reproducible enough to explain how shipped wasm, JavaScript, HTML, and manifest artifacts were produced - separate development, staging, and production environments so they do not share secrets or logging sinks accidentally - align audit logging with the application''s own auth, mutation, and adminis