('f2e77bd01c741d41a793b530623baf12acf2c27d', 'docs\WASM_RELEASES.md', 'Wasm Build Profiles and Release Engineering', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Use it when deciding how local development builds, CI verification builds, benchmark builds, and production release builds should differ, and which production-oriented build flags are the default safe baseline.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 162, 372, 'Use it when deciding how local development builds, CI verification builds, benchmark builds, and production release builds should differ, and which production-oriented build flags are the default safe baseline.', 'Use it when deciding how local development builds, CI verification builds, benchmark builds, and production release builds should differ, and which production-oriented build flags are the default safe baseline.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 162, 372, 'Use it when deciding how local development builds, CI verification builds, benchmark builds, and production release builds should differ, and which production-oriented build flags are the default safe baseline.', 'Use it when deciding how local development builds, CI verification builds, benchmark builds, and production release builds should differ, and which production-oriented build flags are the default safe baseline.', 0, 0, 'manual-wasm_releases-20260330T214856763Z', '30a6ed13f257b5ab85935440633a8b22d001d8d414ba3e8b0e9e866267982c22', 'd1a3877713a293d35bc32d2b32adf185c387bb1847b4a0b588f448bcf8db25af', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('03dc52b1db60732362380bc92b9b4f2e6b56e7e5', 'docs\WASM_RELEASES.md', 'Wasm Build Profiles and Release Engineering', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- The repo already ships a real Go-native launcher path for wasm build and release work through `gwc build` and `gwc release`. - `gwc release` emits a release-profile wasm artifact, defaults to gzip plus Brotli sidecars, writes `wasm-release-manifest.json`, supports optional budget enforcement, and can emit machine-readable JSON summaries. - That release manifest is also the shipped handoff into the `pwa` package through `pwa.ParseWasmReleaseManifestJSON(...)`, `pwa.BuildServiceWorkerAssetPlan(...)`, and `pwa.BuildCacheStoragePlan(...)`.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 393, 936, '- The repo already ships a real Go-native launcher path for wasm build and release work through `gwc build` and `gwc release`. - `gwc release` emits a release-profile wasm artifact, defaults to gzip plus Brotli sidecars, writes `wasm-release-manifest.json`, supports optional budget enforcement, and can emit machine-readable JSON summaries. - That release manifest is also the shipped handoff into the `pwa` package through `pwa.ParseWasmReleaseManifestJSON(...)`, `pwa.BuildServiceWorkerAssetPlan(...)`, and `pwa.BuildCacheStoragePlan(...)`.', '- The repo already ships a real Go-native launcher path for wasm build and release work through `gwc build` and `gwc release`. - `gwc release` emits a release-profile wasm artifact, defaults to gzip plus Brotli sidecars, writes `wasm-release-manifest.json`, supports optional budget enforcement, and can emit machine-readable JSON summaries. - That release manifest is also the shipped handoff into the `pwa` package through `pwa.ParseWasmReleaseManifestJSON(...)`, `pwa.BuildServiceWorkerAssetPlan(...)`, and `pwa.BuildCacheStoragePlan(...)`.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 393, 936, '- The repo already ships a real Go-native launcher path for wasm build and release work through `gwc build` and `gwc release`. - `gwc release` emits a release-profile wasm artifact, defaults to gzip plus Brotli sidecars, writes `wasm-release-manifest.json`, supports optional budget enforcement, and can emit machine-readable JSON summaries. - That release manifest is also the shipped handoff into the `pwa` package through `pwa.ParseWasmReleaseManifestJSON(...)`, `pwa.BuildServiceWorkerAssetPlan(...)`, and `pwa.BuildCacheStoragePlan(...)`.', '- The repo already ships a real Go-native launcher path for wasm build and release work through `gwc build` and `gwc release`. - `gwc release` emits a release-profile wasm artifact, defaults to gzip plus Brotli sidecars, writes `wasm-release-manifest.json`, supports optional budget enforcement, and can emit machine-readable JSON summaries. - That release manifest is also the shipped handoff into the `pwa` package through `pwa.ParseWasmReleaseManifestJSON(...)`, `pwa.BuildServiceWorkerAssetPlan(...)`, and `pwa.BuildCacheStoragePlan(...)`.', 0, 0, 'manual-wasm_releases-20260330T214856763Z', '30a6ed13f257b5ab85935440633a8b22d001d8d414ba3e8b0e9e866267982c22', '06f59066aa9463e43902d917f49aee58bec99c6d19a88c44e1f0ada255482d19', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('da9a482ebdafb706ce9d0c95d47d09dac50f6727', 'docs\WASM_RELEASES.md', 'Wasm Build Profiles and Release Engineering', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'The intended wasm build profiles are explicit, not one generic `go build` command reused for every job.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 957, 1060, 'The intended wasm build profiles are explicit, not one generic `go build` command reused for every job.', 'The intended wasm build profiles are explicit, not one generic `go build` command reused for every job.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 957, 1060, 'The intended wasm build profiles are explicit, not one generic `go build` command reused for every job.', 'The intended wasm build profiles are explicit, not one generic `go build` command reused for every job.', 0, 0, 'manual-wasm_releases-20260330T214856763Z', '30a6ed13f257b5ab85935440633a8b22d001d8d414ba3e8b0e9e866267982c22', '2621a41f6b4b657741641d348414666c7f16100616a63aec3756284f97483a98', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
