when the custom side channel is no longer needed - `pool.Drain(ctx)` waits for already accepted work to finish before terminating the worker set, while `pool.Close()` terminates the pool immediately and causes queued or active requests to fail promptly', 0, 0, 'manual-workers-20260330T214856777Z', 'c77f5e6ffe161b45a8366232b7b379ed9ecb7fc989fb6fabd00ad2142c1c1f0a', 'd7f87e1519739b36aab90c906bdffc06bc28a5b2724fbedf0b698dbbc8724d0f', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('32d83809d619bbcb8826b61ae5a9e0fcadf3dcfb', 'docs\WORKERS.md', 'Worker Guidance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'For UI ownership, keep the worker handle scoped to the route, component, or service that owns the background job. Cleanup should terminate the worker or at least cancel any in-flight request contexts when the owner unmounts.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10066, 10290, 'For UI ownership, keep the worker handle scoped to the route, component, or service that owns the background job. Cleanup should terminate the worker or at least cancel any in-flight request contexts when the owner unmounts.', 'For UI ownership, keep the worker handle scoped to the route, component, or service that owns the background job. Cleanup should terminate the worker or at least cancel any in-flight request contexts when the owner unmounts.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 10066, 10290, 'For UI ownership, keep the worker handle scoped to the route, component, or service that owns the background job. Cleanup should terminate the worker or at least cancel any in-flight request contexts when the owner unmounts.', 'For UI ownership, keep the worker handle scoped to the route, component, or service that owns the background job. Cleanup should terminate the worker or at least cancel any in-flight request contexts when the owner unmounts.', 0, 0, 'manual-workers-20260330T214856777Z', 'c77f5e6ffe161b45a8366232b7b379ed9ecb7fc989fb6fabd00ad2142c1c1f0a', '26fe0895d83b39115f19ded7affc2ee0b575c66a9f473511456b265fb5ebc576', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('05f9eadf577c4f423d36b62ce9b334e27bcb3f67', 'docs\WORKERS.md', 'Worker Guidance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '`worker.Request(...)` is context-driven.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10337, 10377, '`worker.Request(...)` is context-driven.', '`worker.Request(...)` is context-driven.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 10337, 10377, '`worker.Request(...)` is context-driven.', '`worker.Request(...)` is context-driven.', 0, 0, 'manual-workers-20260330T214856777Z', 'c77f5e6ffe161b45a8366232b7b379ed9ecb7fc989fb6fabd00ad2142c1c1f0a', 'c133bee78b5910faf654b4776356c2953521c8b70f1a350e06296ac2c55794f7', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('d982bff7d1b5b9a3e61d9bca23e977dba8417e5d', 'docs\WORKERS.md', 'Worker Guidance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- `context.WithCancel(...)` cancels the wait path and returns `interop` error code `cancelled` - `context.WithTimeout(...)` or deadlines return code `timeout` - late worker responses are ignored because the request listeners are removed once the request completes, times out, or is cancelled', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10379, 10670, '- `context.WithCancel(...)` cancels the wait path and returns `interop` error code `cancelled` - `context.WithTimeout(...)` or deadlines return code `timeout` - late worker responses are ignored because the request listeners are removed once the request completes, times out, or is cancelled', '- `context.WithCancel(...)` cancels the wait path and returns `interop` error code `cancelled` - `context.WithTimeout(...)` or deadlines return code `timeout` - late worker responses are ignored because the request listeners are removed once the request completes, times out, or is cancelled', 0.9, 'pass', '', 10379, 10670, '- `context.WithCancel(...)` cancels the wait path and returns `interop` error code `cancelled` - `context.WithTimeout(...)` or deadlines return code `timeout` - late worker responses are ignored because the request listeners are removed once the request completes, times out, or is cancelled', '- `context.WithCancel(...)` cancels the wait path and returns `interop` error code `cancelled` - `context.WithTimeout(...)` or deadlines return code `timeout` - late worker responses are ignored because the request listeners are removed once the request completes, times out, or is cancelled', 0, 0, 'manual-workers-20260330T214856777Z', 'c77f5e6ffe161b45a8366232b7b379ed9ecb7fc989fb6fabd00ad2142c1c1f0a', '48c8ef2e1df92bfb4ea78848d43c6e504b3a84fa90530c293b9e800ebbfd1762', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('35b2a1893dc9aad3914f573d9d3e9a848c79b7fd', 'docs\WORKERS.md', 'Worker Guidance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Backpressure is now available through explicit pool sizing and queue limits:', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10672, 10748, 'Backpressure is now available through explicit pool sizing and queue limits:', 'Backpressure is now available through explicit pool sizing and queue limits:', 0.9, 'pass', '', 10672, 10748, 'Backpressure is now available through explicit pool sizing and queue limits:', 'Backpressure is now available through explicit pool sizing and queue limits:', 0, 0, 'manual-workers-20260330T214856777Z', 'c77f5e6ffe161b45a8366232b7b379ed9ecb7fc989fb6fabd00ad2142c1c1f0a', 'c1fa3011cfe91bca76aefbe171d141a7040a0be15d1349f986da919be1e6ca75', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('3bb113fa73fff0cd423bb870ede97f1245379881', 'docs\WORKERS.md', 'Worker Guidance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- each direct `worker.Request(...)` call is still independent - `OpenWorkerPool(...)` provides fixed-size scheduling and bounded queueing for request-style worker jobs - once the pool is full, later requests wait for admission until capacity frees or their request context is cancelled or times out - apps should still debounce noisy UI input and choose pool sizes or queue limits that match the worker protocol and hardware budget - if a worker protocol only supports one active job at a time, open a pool with `Size: 1` and a deliberate `QueueLimit` instead of hand-rolling the scheduler', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 10750, 11339, '- each direct `worker.Request(...)` call is still independent - `OpenWorkerPool(...)` provides fixed-size scheduling and bounded queueing for request-style worker jobs - once the pool is full, later requests wait for admission until capacity frees or their request context is cancelled or times out - apps should still debounce noisy UI input and choose pool sizes or queue limits that match the worker protocol and hardware budget - if a worker protocol only supports one active job at a time, open a pool with `Size: 1` and a deliberate `QueueLimit` instead of hand-rolling the scheduler', '- each direct `worker.Request(...)` call is still independent - `OpenWorkerPool(...)` provides fixed-size scheduling and bounded queueing for request-style worker jobs - once the pool is full, later requests wait for admission until capacity frees or their request context is cancelled or times out - apps should still debounce noisy UI input and choose pool sizes or queue limits that match the worker protocol and hardware budget - if a worker protocol only supports one active job at a time, open a pool with `Size: 1` and a deliberate `QueueLimit` instead of hand-rolling the scheduler', 0.9, 'pass', '', 10750, 11339, '- each direct `worker.Request(...)` call is still independent - `OpenWorkerPool(...)` provides fixed-size scheduling and bounded queueing for request-style worker jobs - once the pool is full, later requests wait for admission until capacity frees or their request context is cancelled or times out - apps should still debounce noisy UI input and choose pool sizes or queue limits that match the worker protocol and hardware budget - if a worker protocol only supports one active job at a time, open a pool with `Size: 1` and a deliberate `QueueLimit` instead of hand-rolling the scheduler', '- each direct `worker.Request(...)` call is still independent - `OpenWorkerPool(...)` provides fixed-size scheduling and bounded queueing for request-style worker jobs - once the pool is full, later requests wait for admission until capacity frees or their request context is cancelled or times out - apps should still debounce noisy UI input and choose pool sizes or queue limits that match the worker protocol and hardware budget - if a worker protocol only supports one active job at a time, open a pool with `Size: 1` and a deliberate `QueueLimit` instead of hand-rolling the scheduler', 0, 0, 'manual-workers-20260330T214856777Z', 'c77f5e6ffe161b45a8366232b7b379ed9ecb7fc989fb6fabd00ad2142c1c1f0a', 'f6cd334a4c3c6f4ae39952f42ca7cd03bd564fcf58d61be8891b4ea83ca144ce', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('9d833298efc898f95ac5138065bcc310bcd789f2', 'docs\WORKERS.md', 'Worker Guidance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', 'Worker payloads should stay structured-clone friendly and, for typed decoding, JSON-shaped.', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 11370, 11461, 'Worker payloads should stay structured-clone friendly and, for typed decoding, JSON-shaped.', 'Worker payloads should stay structured-clone friendly and, for typed decoding, JSON-shaped.', 0.9, 'pass', '', 11370, 11461, 'Worker payloads should stay structured-clone friendly and, for typed decoding, JSON-shaped.', 'Worker payloads should stay structured-clone friendly and, for typed decoding, JSON-shaped.', 0, 0, 'manual-workers-20260330T214856777Z', 'c77f5e6ffe161b45a8366232b7b379ed9ecb7fc989fb6fabd00ad2142c1c1f0a', '796e8c9eb2d6cb61a084fe69a2b4b221b13711d84c7d6cd757812bfeb9becd3a', 1, 'manual-v1', 'none', datetime('now')),
('d0f0198bbe7dd8bcc2cf38259498202a2b8e318b', 'docs\WORKERS.md', 'Worker Guidance', NULL, 'paragraph', 'Paragraph', '- preferred: strings, booleans, numbers, arrays, slices, maps, and structs - acceptable with care: byte slices or large arrays, as long as the worker script expects cloneable data - first-class today: `MessagePort` ownership transfer through `worker.PostPorts(...)`, `scope.PostPorts(...)`, and `port.PostPorts(...)`, plus `SharedBuffer` and `[]byte` values posted directly, used as `WorkerMessage.Payload`, or nested inside documented string-keyed map, slice, array, and exported struct payload graphs - current limit: nested `SharedBuffer` or `[]byte` transport is documented for acyclic JSON-shaped payload graphs only; non-string-keyed maps, cyclic graphs, and opaque host objects remain outside the structured-conversion contract - not yet first-class in the public Go API: `ArrayBuffer` transfer helpers, `ReadableStream`, or other browser-native ownership-transfer types - unsupported for typed helpers: functions, DOM nodes, cyclic objects, and opaque host objects', '{"type":"paragraph"}', 11463, 12435, '- preferred: strings, booleans, numbers, arrays, slices, maps, and structs - acceptable with care: byte slices or large arrays, as long as the worker script expects cloneable data - first-class today: `MessagePort` ownership transfer through `worker.PostPorts(...)`, `scope.PostPorts(...)`, and `port.PostPorts(...)`, plus `SharedBuffer` and `[]byte` values posted directly, used as `WorkerMessage.Payload`, or nested inside documented string-keyed map, slice, array, and exported struct payload graphs - current limit: nested `SharedBuffer` or `[]byte` transport is documented for acyclic JSON-shaped payload graphs only; non-string-keyed maps, cyclic graphs, and opaque host objects remain outside the structured-conversion contract - not yet first-class in the public Go API: `ArrayBuffer` transfer helpers, `ReadableStream`, or other browser-native ownership-transfe